hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3001","7 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated to us: my father narrated to us. 8 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me that Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith al-Ansari narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to him that he and Umar ibn al-Khattab discussed charity one day. Umar said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mention misappropriation of charity: whoever misappropriates a camel or a sheep from it will come carrying it on the Day of Resurrection? Abd Allah ibn Unays said: Yes. Ibn Majah narrated it from Amr ibn Sawwad, from Ibn Wahb. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi concerning the Prophet's, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, employment of Ibn al-Lutbiyyah."
"3002","Another. 9 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us: Abu al-Hasan narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was praying. I stood at his left, and the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took me and placed me at his right. Upon me was a torn garment that did not cover me; whenever I prostrated I held it with my hand, fearing my nakedness would be exposed, with women behind me. When the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished, he called for a garment for me and clothed me with it, and said: Keep this worn garment of yours. Al-Tabarani said: This Abu al-Hasan from whom Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated is Muhajir Abu al-Hasan from whom Shu'bah narrated, a Kufan. Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman is Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, the brother of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla. Sulayman ibn Kathir is the brother of Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi; Yahya ibn Ma'in said: weak. Al-Bukhari and Muslim have narrated from him."
"3003","Musnad of Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari. Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari, Abu Isa, may Allah be pleased with him — other than al-Huna'i; Ali ibn al-Madini and Shabab, Khalifah ibn Khayyat, distinguished between them. 10 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib narrated to me that Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated to him, he said: A hadith reached me from a man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which he heard from the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that I had not heard from him. He said: So I bought a camel, fastened my saddle upon it, and traveled to him for a month until I came to Syria, when he was Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari. I sent to him that Jabir was at the door. He said: The messenger returned to me and said: Jabir ibn Abd Allah? I said: Yes. He said: The messenger returned, then came back to me; he embraced me and I embraced him. He said: So I said: A hadith reached me that you heard from the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning wrongs, which I have not heard; I feared I would die or you would die before I heard it. Did you hear the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah will gather the servants — or he said: Allah will gather the people — he said: gesturing with his hand toward Syria — naked, uncircumcised, buhman? I said: What is buhman? He said: With nothing with them. He said: Then He will call them with a voice heard by the distant as the near hears it: I am the King, I am the Reckoner. It is not fitting for any of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise while any of the people of Hell seeks him for a wrong, nor for any of the people of Hell to enter Hell while any of the people of Paradise seeks him for a wrong — even a slap. He said: We said: How is that, when we come to Allah naked, uncircumcised, buhman? He said: With good deeds and evil deeds. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun, from Hammam ibn Yahya, with his chain in full. Al-Bukhari narrated its beginning, citing it as evidence without a chain, suspended."
"3004","Another. 11 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, he said: Abd Allah ibn Unays said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who will deal with Khalid ibn Nubayh for me — a man of Hudhayl, then at Arafah? Abd Allah said: So I said: I will, O Messenger of Allah; describe him to me. He said: If you saw him you would fear him. I said: By the One Who honored you, I have never feared anything. So I went out until I met him at the mountains of Arafah before the sun set. I met him and was struck with awe of him; I recognized, when I was struck with awe of him, what the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had said. He said: Who is the man? I said: One seeking a need; is there lodging? He said: Yes, join me. He said: So I went out after him, prayed Asr two light rak'ahs, then went out fearing he would see me, then caught up with him and struck him with the sword. I hid until, when the people left, I came out until I arrived at the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Madinah and told him the news. Muhammad ibn Ka'b said: The Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave him a short staff and said: Keep this with you until you meet me with it on the Day of Resurrection; the fewest people that day will be those who carry short staffs. Muhammad ibn Ka'b said: When Abd Allah ibn Unays died, he ordered it placed upon his belly, shrouded over it, and buried with him."
"3005","12 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me. 13 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, they said: Ya'qub narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from the son of Abd Allah ibn Unays, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me and said: It has reached me that Khalid ibn Sufyan ibn Nubayh al-Hudhali is gathering people against me to raid me, while he is at Uranah; so go to him and kill him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, describe him to me so I may know him. He said: When you see him you will find a shudder. He said: So I went out girded with my sword until I stood over him while he was at Uranah with women in howdahs, seeking a dwelling for them; it was the time of Asr. When I saw him I found what the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had described to me of the shudder. I advanced toward him, fearing a struggle between me and him would distract me from the prayer, so I prayed while walking toward him, gesturing the bowing and prostration with my head. When I reached him he said: Who is the man? I said: A man of the Arabs who heard of you and your gathering against this man, coming to you for that. He said: Yes, I am engaged in that. He said: So I walked with him a while until, when I was able, I struck him with the sword until I killed him, then left with his women in howdahs bending over him. When I came to the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he saw me, he said: The face has prospered. He said: I said: I killed him, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You have spoken truly. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and took me into his house, giving me a staff. He said: Keep this with you, O Abd Allah ibn Unays. He said: So I went out with it among the people, and they said: What is this staff? He said: I said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave it to me, commanding me to keep it. They said: Will you not return to the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ask him about that? He said: So I returned to the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you give me this staff? He said: A sign between me and you on the Day of Resurrection; the fewest people that day will be those who carry staffs. He said: Abd Allah joined it to his sword; it remained with him until, when he died, he ordered it joined with him in his shroud, then both were buried together. The wording of the hadith of Imam Ahmad, and the narration of Abu Khaythamah is similar. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yahya ibn Adam, from Ibn Idris, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, from one of the children of Abd Allah ibn Unays — or he said: from Abd Allah ibn Unays — mentioning similar. We only brought out this narration as a witness for the narration of Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi from Abd Allah ibn Unays, for in the narration of Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr the son of Abd Allah ibn Unays is not named."
"3006","Another. 14 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, at Isfahan, that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us. 15 - Another: Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, they said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to us: my uncle al-Hasan ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, that the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him on a detachment alone. Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abd al-Warith, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq in full. And from Ahmad ibn al-Azhar, from Ya'qub, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq; in both narrations from the son of Abd Allah ibn Unays. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili."
"3007","Musnad of Abd Allah ibn Badr al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Badr al-Juhani Abu Badr, may Allah be pleased with him. 16 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us. 17 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bishr al-Hariri narrated to us, they said: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ba'jah ibn Abd Allah: that his father informed him that the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them one day: This is the day of Ashura, so fast it. A man of Banu Amr ibn Awf stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I left my people, some fasting and some breaking fast. The Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Go to them; whoever was fasting, let him complete the rest of his day. Al-Daraqutni mentioned Abd Allah ibn Badr al-Juhani; his son Ba'jah narrated from him, as Yahya ibn Abi Kathir said from him; al-Bukhari or Muslim is obliged to bring out his hadith."
"3008","Musnad of another Abd Allah ibn Badr, may Allah be pleased with him. Another Abd Allah ibn Badr, may Allah be pleased with him. 18 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Juwayriyah, from Abd Allah ibn Badr: that the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no vow in disobedience. Abu al-Juwayriyah — his name is Hittan ibn Khufaf al-Jarmi; he has a narration in Sahih al-Bukhari from Ibn Abbas."
"3009","19 - With the same chain, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from Shu'bah: Abu al-Juwayriyah narrated to me, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Badr mention from the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There is no vow in disobedience."
"3010","Musnad of Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini. Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini, his kunya Abu Safwan — and it is said Abu Busr — lived in Hims, may Allah be pleased with him. Arta'ah ibn al-Mundhir from Abd Allah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with him. 20 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: al-Hakim Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Marwan ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, at Damascus: Hisham ibn Khalid — meaning al-Azraq — narrated to us: Mubashshir ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Arta'ah — meaning Ibn al-Mundhir — narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr: that two men came to the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. One of them said: O Messenger of Allah, which men are best? He said: One whose life is long and whose deed is good. The other said: The laws of Islam have become many for us, so command us with a comprehensive matter. He said: Let your tongue remain moist with the remembrance of Allah. Umar ibn Qays al-Kindi narrated it from Abd Allah."
"3011","Azhar ibn Abd Allah al-Harazi from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 21 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Amr, he said: Azhar ibn Abd Allah al-Harazi informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: My mother said: If only we made food for the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and invited him? So we made tharid with ghee for him. Then the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and entered the house; my mother placed for him a velvet cloth of ours, folding it for him to make it softer for him. The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sat upon it. We placed water for him, and he said: Take, in the name of Allah — pointing to its top with his three fingers. When he finished I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for us. He said: O Allah, have mercy upon them, forgive them, and bless them in their provision. We have mentioned what Muslim brought out in the biography of Sulaym ibn Amir; and in this is what Muslim did not mention."
"3012","Azhar ibn Sa'id from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 22 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratis i narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Azhar ibn Sa'id, from Abd Allah ibn Busr: that a man entered while the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was delivering the sermon on Friday, stepping over people's necks. The Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Sit, for you have harmed and come late."
"3013","Hudayr ibn Kurayb, Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 23 - Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Su'ud al-Busiri informed us, in Egypt, that Murshid ibn Yahya ibn al-Qasim al-Madini informed them, recited to him: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya al-Naysaburi informed us: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i narrated to us: Wahb ibn Bayan narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: I was sitting beside him on Friday. He said: A man came stepping over people's necks on Friday while the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was addressing the people. The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Sit, for you have harmed."
"3014","24 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah — meaning Ibn Salih — from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, he said: I was sitting with Abd Allah ibn Busr on Friday, when a man came stepping over people's necks. He said to me: A man came stepping over people's necks while the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was delivering the sermon, and he said: Sit, for you have harmed and come late."
"3015","25 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us, at Herat, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather informed us: Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, he said: I was sitting with Abd Allah ibn Busr on Friday, and it continued until the imam came out. A man came stepping over people's necks while the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was delivering the sermon, and he said to him: Sit, for you have harmed and come late."
"3016","26 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them — by ijazah if not by hearing: Mansur ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah narrate from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: I was sitting beside him on Friday, and he said: A man came stepping over people's necks, and the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Sit, for you have harmed and come late. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Zayd ibn al-Hubab. Abu Dawud narrated it from Harun ibn Ma'ruf, from Bishr ibn al-Sari, both from Mu'awiyah. Al-Nasa'i narrated it as we brought it out. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih as above. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Harmalah ibn Yahya."
"3017","Hariz ibn Uthman al-Rahabi from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 27 - Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Qurashi al-Khushu'i informed us, at Damascus, that Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khadir informed them: Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kinani informed us: Tammam ibn Muhammad al-Razi informed us: Abu Zur'ah Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Ahmad al-Qurashi — known as Ibn al-Tammar — informed us: Ali ibn Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: I heard the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever seeks a matter through disobedience, that will sooner cause what he hopes to miss him, and sooner bring what he fears."
"3018","Another. 28 - With the same chain, Abu Zur'ah Muhammad ibn Sa'id informed us: Ali ibn Amr narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Hariz narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek needs with dignity of soul, for matters proceed by decrees."
"3019","Another. 29 - With the same chain, Tammam ibn Muhammad informed us: Abu Ya'qub Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Adhru'i informed us: Abu al-Asbagh Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurqusani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Mansur ibn Isma'il al-Harrani narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Maryam, Safwan ibn Amr, Hariz ibn Amr, and Hariz ibn Uthman, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: I saw the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, trimming his mustache, cutting it."
"3020","30 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: my father narrated to us. 31 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Hammal narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us: Mansur ibn Isma'il ibn Ma'bad ibn Yazid al-Harrani, the freedman of Umm al-Banin bint Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan, narrated to me: Safwan ibn Amr, Hariz ibn Uthman, and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, trimming his mustache, cutting it. Junadah ibn Marwan narrated from Hariz ibn Uthman, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: The mustache of the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was level with his lip. Ya'qub ibn Muhammad — we brought it out as a witness."
"3021","Al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 32 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to me, he said: My sister would sometimes send me with something to the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as a treat for him, and he would accept it from me."
"3022","33 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: My sister used to treat the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with something, sending it with me, and he would accept it."
"3023","34 - With the same chain, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us: my father Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: My sister used to send a gift to the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would accept it. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Ahmad, from al-Hasan ibn Ayyub."
"3024","Another. 35 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Hisham ibn Sa'id narrated to me: al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated to me: Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to accept the gift and not accept charity."
"3025","36 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Fil al-Antaki narrated to us: Abu Tawbah narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr: that the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to accept the gift and not accept charity."
"3026","Another. 37 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr: that he had a mole on his head, and the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: This will surely live to see a generation."
"3027","38 - With the same chain, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Busr showed me a mole on his forelock and said: The Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed his hand upon it and said: It will surely live to see a generation. Abd Allah used to comb his head."
"3028","39 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us: Abu Abd Allah al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Busr showed me a mole on his forelock, so I placed my finger upon it. He said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed his finger upon it, then said: It will surely reach a generation. Abu Abd Allah said: And he had thick hair."
"3029","Hassan ibn Nuh from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 40 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us: Mubashshir ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Nuh, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini say: Do you see this hand of mine? With it I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I heard him say: Do not fast Saturday except in what has been obligated upon you; even if one of you finds only tree bark, let him break fast upon it."
"3030","41 - With the same chain, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Abd Allah — that is Ahmad ibn Ibrahim — narrated to us: Mubashshir narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Nuh, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr, the Companion of the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Do you see this hand of mine? I placed it upon the hands of the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I heard him say: Do not fast Saturday except as an obligation; even if one of you finds only tree bark, let him break fast upon it."
"3031","42 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us: Hassan ibn Nuh narrated to us, he said: I saw Abd Allah ibn Busr and heard him say: Do you see this palm of mine? I bear witness that I placed it upon the palm of Muhammad, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he forbade us from fasting Saturday except as an obligation, saying: If one of you finds only tree bark, let him break fast upon it. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ali ibn Ayyash, with: let him break fast upon it. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Husayn ibn Mansur, from Mubashshir. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, from al-Hakam ibn Musa."
"3032","Another. 43 - Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Abd Allah Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Mubashshir narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Nuh, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr, the Companion of the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Two Bedouins came to the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. One of them said: Who are the best of men, O Muhammad? He said: One whose life is long and whose deed is good. The other said: The laws of Islam have become many for us; direct us to a comprehensive matter we may confine ourselves to. He said: Let your tongue remain moist with the remembrance of Allah. Ali ibn Ayyash narrated it from Hassan ibn Nuh, from Amr ibn Qays, from Abd Allah ibn Busr; perhaps he heard it from Abd Allah and heard it from Amr from him, narrating it with both narrations, for in Mubashshir's narration from him: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr, and Allah knows best."
"3033","Hafs ibn Rawahah from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 44 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Abu Sa'd ibn Hafs ibn Rawahah narrated to us, from his father: Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to us, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to a house, he came to it from its side, not from its door. And I heard the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Measure your food; it will be blessed for you. It has a witness in Sahih al-Bukhari concerning measuring food from the hadith of al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib."
"3034","Al-Hakam ibn al-Walid from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 45 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us. 46 - And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, they said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Uthman ibn Khalid ibn Amr al-Sulafi al-Himsi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Khabayiri narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr say: My mother sent me to the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a cluster of grapes, and I ate it. My mother said to the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Did Abd Allah bring you a cluster? He said: No. So whenever the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw me, he would say: Treacherous, treacherous."
"3035","Khalid ibn Ma'dan from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 47 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abu Bakr — that is Ibn Abi Shaybah — narrated to us. 48 - And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not fast Saturday except in what has been obligated upon you; even if one of you finds only a grapevine stick or tree bark, let him break fast upon it. Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim said: Or tree bark, let him suck it. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ali ibn Khashram, from Isa ibn Yunus; and from Amr ibn Uthman, from Baqiyyah, from al-Zubaydi, from Luqman ibn Amir, from Amir ibn Jashib, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan; and from Imran ibn Bakkar, from Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih, from Baqiyyah, from al-Zubaydi, from Amir ibn Jashib, from Khalid. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah in agreement."
"3036","Salim ibn Amir from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 49 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed him: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Abu Mushir narrated to us. 50 - Sulayman said: And Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, they said: Sadaqah narrated to us, from Ibn Jabir, from Salim ibn Amir, from Ibn Busr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon us; we placed for him a velvet cloth of ours, shaking it out, and he sat. Revelation descended upon him in our house. We offered him butter or dates — and he loved butter. On the head of one of them was a forelock of hair gathered like a horn. He said: Do I not see in my ummah a horn? We said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for us. He said: O Allah, have mercy upon them until You forgive them and provide for them."
"3037","51 - Muhammad also informed us that Mahmud al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Sadaqah narrated to us, from Ibn Jabir, from Salim ibn Amir, from the two sons of Busr, they said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon us; we offered him dates and butter — and he loved butter. Abu Dawud narrated this last one: we offered him butter and dates — and he loved butter and dates — from Muhammad ibn Wazir, from al-Walid ibn Yazid, from Ibn Jabir, from Salim. Ibn Majah narrated it similarly from Hisham ibn Ammar in agreement. Muhammad ibn Awf — asked about Ibn Busr — said: Abd Allah and Atiyyah. Muslim brought out: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, alighted upon my father; we brought him food and moist dates, and he ate from them. Then dates were brought, and he would eat them, placing the pits between his fingers, joining the index and middle fingers. Then drink was brought; he drank, then passed it to the one on his right. He said: My father said — holding the bridle of his mount: Supplicate to Allah for us. He said: O Allah, bless them in what You have provided them, forgive them, and have mercy upon them. I say: In what we have mentioned is what Muslim did not mention."
"3038","Safwan ibn Amr from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 52 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini narrated to me, he said: My father sent me to the Prophet to invite him to food; he came with me. When I drew near the house I hastened and informed my parents. They came out, met the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, welcomed him, and placed for him a Zubayri velvet cloth of ours; he sat upon it. Then my father said to my mother: Bring your food. She brought a bowl containing flour kneaded with water and salt, placed before the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Take, in the name of Allah, from around it, leaving its top, for the blessing is in it. The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate, and we ate with him; some remained. Then the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, forgive them, have mercy upon them, bless them, and expand their provisions."
"3039","Abd Allah ibn Abi Bilal from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 53 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us: Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ibn Abi Bilal, from Abd Allah ibn Busr."
"3040","54 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad, the grandson of Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Mandah, informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us. 55 - Another: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, they said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ibn Abi Bilal, from Abd Allah ibn Busr: that the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Between the great battle and the conquest of the city are six years, and the false messiah, the Dajjal, will emerge in the seventh. Al-Tabarani's narration does not contain the word masih."
"3041","56 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Khawwas narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ibn Abi Bilal, from Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The great battle and the emergence of the Dajjal are within six years, and the conquest of Constantinople in the seventh. Abu Dawud brought it out from Haywah ibn Shurayh. Ibn Majah narrated it from Suwayd ibn Sa'id, from Baqiyyah, from Bahir, from Khalid ibn Abi Bilal, from Abd Allah ibn Busr — a mistake; rather it is Khalid from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bilal, as Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned in his book."
"3042","Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Bakri from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 57 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Bakri, he said: I entered upon the two sons of Busr al-Maziniyyayn and said: Did you see the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? They said: Yes; he visited us in our dwellings, we brought him food, he ate from our food, he saw on the forelock of one of us matted hair, placed his hand upon it, and said: Praise be to Allah Who has placed in my ummah the like of this."
"3043","Abd al-Rahman al-Jundi from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 58 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Adhani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us: Sawadah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abd al-Rahman al-Jundi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I heard that there will be in this ummah a people, while they are drinking wine and striking instruments, until Allah overturns it upon them, and they become apes and pigs. The Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is not mentioned in it."
"3044","Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah ibn Busr from his father Abd Allah ibn Busr. 59 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-A'raj narrated to us: al-Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri, of the descendants of Abd Allah ibn Busr, narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awza'i narrated to me, he said: I passed by your grandfather Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah ibn Busr while I was on campaign, when he was governor over Hims. He said to me: O Abu Amr, shall I not narrate to you a hadith that will please you? By Allah, I have often concealed it from rulers. I said: Yes. He said: My father Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to me, he said: While we were sitting in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah, he came out to us bright-faced, beaming. We stood to face him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what we see of the radiance of your face and its cheerfulness pleases us. The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me just now and gave me glad tidings that Allah has granted me intercession. We said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for Banu Hashim specifically? He said: No. We said: For Quraysh generally? He said: No. We said: For your ummah? He said: It is for my ummah, for the sinful burdened ones."
"3045","60 - Abu Ja'far also informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Fadl ibn Sahl al-A'raj Abu al-Abbas narrated to us: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri — of the descendants of Abd Allah ibn Busr — narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman al-Awza'i narrated to me, he said: I passed by Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah ibn Busr while I was on campaign, when he was governor over Hims. He said to me: O Abu Amr, shall I not narrate to you a hadith that will please you? By Allah, I have often concealed it from rulers. He said: I said: Yes. He said: My father Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to me, he said: While we were in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he came out to us bright-faced, beaming. He said: So we stood to face him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the radiance of your face and its beaming pleases us. The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril came to me tonight and gave me glad tidings that Allah has granted me intercession. We said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for Banu Hashim specifically? He said: No. We said: For Quraysh generally? He said: No. We said: For your ummah? He said: He clenched with his hand and said: It is for my ummah, for the sinful burdened ones. Abu al-Abbas said: The letter of 'There is no blame upon the doers of good' dropped from my book."
"3046","61 - Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Khushui informed us, recitation in his presence, that Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khadir al-Sulami informed them; Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kattani informed us; Tamam ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Razi informed us; Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Sinan informed us; Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated to me. 62 - Tamam said: And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Qutays and Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Khalid narrated to us, both saying: Abu Yahya Junayd ibn Khalaf ibn Hajib ibn al-Walid ibn Junayd al-Samarqandi narrated to us; Abu al-Abbas al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us; al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us; Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri, of the descendants of Abd Allah ibn Busr, informed us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awzai narrated to me, saying: I passed by your grandfather Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah ibn Busr while I was on a military expedition, and he was governor over Hims, and he said: O Abu Amr, shall I not narrate to you a hadith that will please you? By Allah, I would sometimes conceal it from the rulers. He said: I said: Yes. He said: My father Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to me, saying: We were one day sitting in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came out to us radiant, glowing, and so we stood up before him and said: O Messenger of Allah, may Allah gladden you; what we see of the radiance of your face and its cheerfulness indeed gladdens us... and he mentioned the rest of it similarly. Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri: Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He is not used as proof. And al-Bukhari narrated for him a hadith from Wathila ibn al-Asqa."
"3047","Amr ibn Bilal al-Qurashi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 63 - Al-Asad ibn Baldark al-Jibrili informed us in his book, and my cousin the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Maqdisi informed us from him, may Allah have mercy on them, that Abu al-Khattab Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Harun informed them; Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas ibn Khuzaymah informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn al-Dahhak al-Zubaydi narrated to us; Umar ibn Bilal Abu Hafs narrated to us, saying: I saw Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini, a short man, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: How will you be when the rulers act unjustly over you."
"3048","64 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us; my grandfather Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us; Umar ibn Bilal al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: I saw Abd Allah ibn Busr, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was sitting in the mosque, and he was a very old, aged sheikh, when his servant boy came to him and said: My master, these camels of yours have been seized for forced labor at al-Ziblah - meaning the house of al-Abbas ibn al-Walid which is at the gate of the mosque in Hims - and there were two men with him, and they took hold of his upper arms until he stood up. Umar said: So I walked with him until he came to al-Ziblah, and there were his camels made to kneel, and they were loading soil into sacks, so he took the sack and began opening it for them, and some Christians said: This is the companion of your Prophet, and you treat him like this? If we saw a man from the companions of Isa we would carry him upon our heads. So the people moved to seize hold, and he said: Leave me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: How will you be when the rulers act unjustly over you."
"3049","Umar ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Ahmusi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 65 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad in Isfahan informed us that Umm Ibrahim al-Juzdani informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us; al-Jarrah ibn Yahya the muezzin narrated to us; Umar ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Ahmusi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever opens the beginning of his day with good and seals it with good, Allah Almighty says to His angels: Do not record against him the sins between that."
"3050","Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 66 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them, recitation in his presence; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Amr ibn Qays, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr say: Two bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of them said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best? He said: He whose life is long and whose deeds are good. And the other said: O Messenger of Allah, the laws of Islam have become many upon me, so command me with a matter I may cling to. So he said: Let your tongue remain moist with the remembrance of Allah."
"3051","67 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us; Hassan ibn Nuh narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: Two bedouins came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of them said: Who are the best of men, O Muhammad? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He whose life is long and whose deeds are good. And the other said: The laws of Islam have become many upon us, so to which of them do we hold fast? So he said: Let your tongue remain moist with the remembrance of Allah."
"3052","68 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim and Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Mihrabazd both said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us; Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Muawiyah informed us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: Two bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, and one of them said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best? He said: He whose life is long and whose deeds are good. He said: And the other said: O Messenger of Allah, the laws of Islam have become many, so inform me of a matter from them that I may cling to. He said: Let your tongue remain moist with the remembrance of Allah Almighty."
"3053","69 - Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Said ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad the muezzin al-Sabbagh informed us that Fatimah bint Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Baghdadi informed them, recitation in her presence - it was said to her: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed you; Jafar ibn Abd Allah ibn Yaqub informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani narrated to us; Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Hamdani narrated to us; Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Amr ibn Qays, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, that a bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the best of people? He said: He whose life is long and whose deeds are good. The Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ali ibn Ayyash. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it in full from Abu Kurayb, from Zayd ibn Hubab, from Muawiyah, and said: A hasan gharib hadith from this angle. And Ibn Majah narrated its end, from Abu Bakr, from Zayd ibn Hubab. And Abu Hatim al-Busti brought out his saying: Let your tongue remain moist with the remembrance of Allah, from Ibn Qutaybah, from Yazid ibn Mawhab, from Ibn Wahb."
"3054","Al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 70 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us; Abu Salih al-Farra - he is Mahbub ibn Musa - narrated to us; Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Sad ibn Ubadah and said: Whom do you count as the martyrs from my nation? He said that three times. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Sad ibn Ubadah said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wishes, he may permit me and I will inform him who the martyrs from his nation are. He said: Then inform me who the martyrs from my nation are. He said: Prop me up, so he was propped up, then he said: Whoever believes in Allah and strives in the path of Allah and fights until he is killed, then he is a martyr. He said: Then the martyrs of my nation are few; the one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, and the one who dies of a belly disease is a martyr, and the one who dies of plague is a martyr, and the one who drowns is a martyr, and the woman who dies in childbirth is a martyr. It has a supporting witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The martyrs are five: the one who dies of plague, and the one who dies of a belly disease, and the drowned, and the one crushed under a collapsed building, and the martyr in the path of Allah."
"3055","Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 71 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, recitation in his presence while he was present; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Abi Asim informed us; Yaqub ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, from Shubah, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings for whoever saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings for them and a good final abode."
"3056","Another. 72 - Abu Jafar also informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us; Abu Haywah Shurayh ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand upon my head and said: This boy will live a century. So he lived a hundred years, and there was a wart on his face, and he said: He will not die until the wart disappears from his face, and he did not die until the wart disappeared from his face."
"3057","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq al-Yahsabi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 73 - Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari, and Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Mallah in Baghdad, and Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi in Cairo informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad al-Shaybani informed them; Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafii informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated to us; Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to us, saying: A sheep was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while food was scarce that day, so he said to his family: Cook this sheep, and look at this flour and bake it, and cook, and make tharid over it. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a bowl called al-Gharra, carried by four men, and when morning came and they glorified Allah in the forenoon, that bowl was brought, and they gathered around it, and when the people became many the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knelt down, and a bedouin said: What is this sitting? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has made me a noble servant, and has not made me an obstinate tyrant. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat from its sides and leave its top, it will be blessed for you in it. Then he said: Take and eat, for by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the lands of Persia and Rome will be opened for you until food becomes abundant and the name of Allah will not be mentioned over it."
"3058","74 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ibrahim ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us; Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr say: A sheep was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while food was scarce that day, so he said to his family: Prepare this sheep, and look at this flour and bake it, and when tomorrow comes then cook it and make tharid over it. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a bowl called al-Ghada - and the correct is al-Gharra - carried by four men, and when the people awoke in the morning and glorified Allah in the forenoon, that bowl was brought and they gathered around it, and when the people became many the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knelt down, and a bedouin said: What is this sitting? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has made me a noble servant, and has not made me an obstinate tyrant. Abu Dawud narrated it from Amr ibn Uthman similarly. And Ibn Majah narrated part of it: Eat from its sides, also from Amr."
"3059","Another. 75 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi narrated to us (h). 76 - And Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Said informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us. Abd Allah said: And I heard it from al-Hakam; Baqiyyah narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi narrated to me, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a door seeking permission, he would not face it directly; he said: Walking along the wall until he seeks permission and is permitted or leaves."
"3060","77 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to the house of a people, would come to them from the direction of their wall, and would not come to them from the direction of their door."
"3061","78 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Abd al-Salam ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Labbab informed them; al-Mutahhar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazani informed us; Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah the Hafiz informed us by dictation; al-Hasan ibn Mansur informed us; Hubaysh ibn Yazid ibn Madi Karib narrated to us; Uthman ibn Said narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to us, saying: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the door of a people, he would not face the door directly, but from its right side or its left side, and would say: Peace be upon you, and that is because there were no curtains upon them. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muammal ibn al-Fadl al-Harrani, from Baqiyyah."
"3062","Another. 79 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us; Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us; Uthman ibn Said ibn Kathir al-Himsi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings for whoever finds much seeking of forgiveness in his record. Ibn Majah brought it out in his Sunan, and al-Nasai, both in the Sunan and in the book of the deeds of day and night, from Amr ibn Uthman, from his father."
"3063","Another. 80 - Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; al-Walid ibn Shuja Abu Hammam narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr (h)."
"3064","81 - And Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Saud al-Busiri informed us in Egypt that Yahya ibn al-Mushrif ibn Ali ibn al-Khadir al-Tammar informed them; Ahmad ibn Said ibn Ahmad ibn Nafis al-Muqri informed us; Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Bundar informed us; Abu Tahir al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Fil informed us; Malik ibn Sulayman al-Himsi narrated to us; Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq al-Yahsabi say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (h)."
"3065","82 - And Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abi Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us; Ismail ibn Ayyash informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Measure your food, it will be blessed for you in it. Ibn Majah narrated it from Hisham ibn Ammar. Ismail ibn Ayyash is another; we brought it out as supporting evidence, and this hadith has already come in the narration of Hafs ibn Rawahah from Abd Allah ibn Busr, and we mentioned its supporting witness in Sahih al-Bukhari from the hadith of al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib."
"3066","Another. 83 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdani informed them; Abu Bakr ibn Ridhah informed us; Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani informed us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us; Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us; my father narrated to us (h). 84 - Al-Tabarani said: And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to me (h)."
"3067","85 - And Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu Abd Allah al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi; Abd Allah ibn Busr, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aim rightly and receive glad tidings, for Allah Almighty is not quick to punish you, and there will come a people who have no proof. Their wording is one."
"3068","Another. 86 - Abu al-Majd al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Dawud - meaning Ibn Rashid - narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings for whoever saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings for whoever believed in me and did not see me; glad tidings for them and a good final abode."
"3069","87 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad informed us that Umm Ibrahim al-Juzdani informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us; Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq al-Yahsabi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings for whoever saw me, and glad tidings for whoever saw one who saw me; glad tidings for them and a good final abode. It has come before in the narration of Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abd Allah ibn Busr."
"3070","Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Himsi Abu al-Qasim, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 88 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Duhaym narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Qasim, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr say: My father came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they entered the house, and my father took a velvet cloth of ours that had once been red and spread it for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he said to my sister Buhaymah: Give us lunch, so she brought a bowl containing hays. I said to Abd Allah ibn Busr: O Abu Safwan, what is hays? He said: Dried yogurt, ghee and dates. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - pointing to the middle of the bowl with three fingers -: Eat in the name of Allah. So we ate until we were full, and I do not think the bowl decreased at all. We have mentioned it in the narration of Sulaym ibn Amir which Muslim brought out with its wording, and in this hadith is what Muslim did not bring out."
"3071","Al-Muthanna ibn Wail, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 89 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Musaffa and Amr ibn Uthman both said: Isam ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: I heard my father al-Muthanna ibn Wail say: I came to Abd Allah ibn Busr and he wiped my head, and I placed my hand upon his forearm."
"3072","90 - And Abu Ghalib ibn Hamzah ibn al-Husayn al-Asadi informed us in Damascus that his grandfather al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan informed them; Ali ibn Abi al-Ala and al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi al-Hadid both said: Ali ibn Musa ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Simsar al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Tanukhi al-Fadl narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Fil narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us; Isam ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: I heard my father al-Muthanna ibn Wail say: I came to Abd Allah ibn Busr and he wiped my head, and I placed my hand upon his forearm, when a man asked him about the wage of the teacher, and he said: A man carrying a bow over his shoulder came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it pleased the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: How excellent your bow is! Did you buy it? He said: No, but a man gifted it to me whose son I taught the Quran. He said: Then would you love that Allah place upon you a bow of fire? He said: No. He said: Then return it. The wording of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Awf. And in the narration of Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Fil, about the wage of the teacher or instructor, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a bow, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was amazed by it. And with him: Did you buy it? He said: No, O Messenger of Allah. And with him, he said: Would you love to be made to wear a bow of fire."
"3073","Yahya ibn Hassan, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 91 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talqani narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Hassan, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini say: Do you see this hand of mine? For I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah with it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast on Saturday except what has been made obligatory upon you."
"3074","92 - And Muhammad informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us; Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not fast on Saturday except what has been made obligatory upon you."
"3075","Yazid ibn Khumayr al-Rahabi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 93 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Umm Ibrahim al-Juzdani informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman narrated to us (h). 94 - And Abu Jafar also informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recitation in his presence while he was present; Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab - he is Ibn Najdah al-Hawti - narrated to us; Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us; Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us; Yazid ibn Khumayr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no one from my nation but that I will recognize him on the Day of Resurrection (h)."
"3076","95 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us; Safwan narrated to us; Yazid ibn Khumayr narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no one from my nation but that I will recognize him on the Day of Resurrection (h)."
"3077","96 - And Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us that the Hafiz Abu al-Barakat Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Mubarak al-Anmati and Abu Ghalib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Asad al-Ukbari al-Khurqi both said: Abu al-Husayn Asim ibn al-Hasan ibn Asim al-Asimi informed us; Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Misri narrated to us, recitation in his presence; Ibrahim ibn Abi Dawud al-Burullusi narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman narrated to us; Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr al-Rahabi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no one from my nation but that I will recognize him on the Day of Resurrection. They said: And how will you recognize them, O Messenger of Allah, among the multitude of creatures? He said: What do you think, if you entered an enclosure containing black horses, all dark, and among them a horse with a white blaze on its forehead and white marks on its legs, would you not recognize it among them? He said: Yes. He said: My nation on that day will be radiant with white blazes and marks from ablution. The wording of Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah, and the wording of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah from al-Tabarani is similar. And the wording of the Imam Ahmad: Would you not recognize among them; he said: Yes. He said: Then my nation on that day will be radiant from prostration, with white marks from ablution. And in the narration of al-Burullusi: If you were admitted into an enclosure containing black horses, all dark, among them a horse with a white blaze and white leg marks, would you not recognize it among them? They said: Yes. He said: Then he said: My nation on that day will be radiant from the trace of prostration, with white marks from ablution. Al-Tirmidhi brought out its end from Abu al-Walid Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, and said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith from this angle. I say: And this hadith meets the condition of Muslim, and Allah knows best. And it has a supporting witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Nuaym al-Mujmir, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation will be called on the Day of Resurrection radiant with white marks from the traces of ablution."
"3078","And from the kunyas: Abu Ubaydah al-Himsi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 97 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us; Abu Ubaydah al-Himsi narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Busr narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali to Khaybar and turbaned him with a black turban, then let it hang behind him - or he said: upon his left shoulder - then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out following the army while leaning upon a bow, when a man carrying a Persian bow passed by him, and he said: Throw it away, for it is cursed, cursed is whoever carries it; upon you are spears and Arab bows, for by them Allah will honor your religion and open lands for you. Yahya said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that only then, in that time in the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); as for today, it has become equipment and strength for Islam."
"3079","98 - And Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Dharr informed them while I was present; Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Hayyan informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us; Yaqub ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us; Abu Ubaydah al-Himsi narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, to Khaybar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out following the army while leaning upon his bow, when a man carrying a Persian bow passed by him, and he said: Throw it away, for it is cursed, and whoever carries it; upon you are spears and Arab bows, for by them Allah will honor your religion and open for you. Yahya ibn Hamzah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this only then; as for today, it has become equipment and strength for Islam."
"3080","Abu al-Wazi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr. 99 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us; Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Abu al-Wazi, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Dajjal will surely be met by whoever saw me, and he will be near his death."
"3081","100 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us; Man ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us (h). 101 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Yahya al-Maafiri narrated to us, both saying: We heard Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Abu al-Wazi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Dajjal will surely be met by whoever saw me, or he will be near my death."
"3082","102 - And Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad ibn Yusuf informed us in his book. And my maternal uncle the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi informed us from him, may Allah have mercy on them, that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Khushaysh informed them; al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us; Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Daqqaq narrated to us; Hanbal ibn Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us; Duhaym ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Yahya al-Maafiri narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, saying: Abu al-Wazi narrated to me that he heard Abd Allah ibn Busr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Dajjal will surely be met by whoever saw me, or he will be near my death. This Abu al-Wazi was mentioned by Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz in al-Kuna and he did not name him."
"3083","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Thalabah al-Udhri. Abd Allah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr, also said Ibn Abi Suayr al-Udhri Abu Muhammad, may Allah be pleased with him. 103 - Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Thalabah ibn Abi Suayr - and Mamar confirmed it to me - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over the slain of Uhud and said: I have borne witness over these; wrap them with their wounds and their blood."
"3084","104 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us therein that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Thalabah al-Udhri - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wiped his face - that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the slain of Uhud: Wrap them with their wounds, for there is no wound inflicted for Allah Almighty but that it will come on the Day of Resurrection bleeding; its color the color of blood, and its scent the scent of musk."
"3085","105 - And with it, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us; Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wiped his face and supplicated for him for blessing - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over the slain of Uhud and said: I am a witness over these; wrap them in their garments and their blood. The Imam Ahmad also brought it out, from Yazid ibn Harun and Hushaym together, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Thalabah. And al-Nasai brought it out from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri similarly. Abd al-Razzaq narrated it from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Abi Suayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah. And Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim al-Dimashqi narrated it, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Zahrah, from Abd Allah ibn Thalabah. In the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abu Zurah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is no wound inflicted in the path of Allah but that it will come on the Day of Resurrection as it was when inflicted; its color blood and its scent the scent of musk. And in al-Bukhari from the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Kab ibn Malik, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bury them in their blood - meaning on the day of Uhud - and he did not wash them."
"3086","Another. 106 - The Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn al-Saffar informed us in Nishapur that Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them; Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us; Abu Said Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Hamdun the merchant informed us; Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi informed us; Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Faris al-Dhuhli narrated to us; Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Abd Allah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr informed me, saying: The one who sought the opening was Abu Jahl, and he said when the two parties met: O Allah, whichever of us was more severing of kinship and brought what is unknown, then grant the opening in the morning. He said: So that was his seeking of opening, and Allah Almighty sent down regarding that: If you seek the opening, then the opening has come to you... up to His saying: And that Allah is with the believers."
"3087","107 - And Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yazid narrated to us; Muhammad - meaning Ibn Ishaq - informed us; al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr, that Abu Jahl said when the two parties met: O Allah, the more severing of us of kinship and the bringer of what is unknown, then destroy him in the morning. So he was the one seeking the opening. Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated it from al-Zuhri. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ubayd Allah ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim, from his uncle Yaqub ibn Ibrahim."
"3088","Another. 108 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdani informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Thalabah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people a day or two before al-Fitr and said: Give a sa of dates, or a sa of wheat between two, or a sa of dates, or a sa of barley, on behalf of each one, young and old. The Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq. And he narrated it from Affan, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Thalabah, from his father. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi, from Musa ibn Ismail, from Hammam, from Bakr ibn Wail, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Thalabah, from his father, making it from the Musnad of Thalabah, and in it there is disagreement. Muhammad ibn Yahya said: No one said this hadith, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Thalabah, except Hammam, from Bakr ibn Wail."
"3089","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Jabir al-Abdi, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Jabir al-Abdi, may Allah be pleased with him. 109 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to me (h). 110 - Al-Tabarani said: And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us (h). 111 - He said: And Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Isbahani narrated to us; Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Muqri narrated to us, both saying: Al-Harith ibn Murrah al-Hanafi narrated to us; a sheikh from the people of Basra called Nafis narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Jabir al-Abdi, who said: I was among the delegation who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Abd al-Qays, but I was not with them; I only came with my father, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them from drinking in the vessels you have heard of: al-dubba, al-hantam, al-naqir and al-muzaffat. It has a supporting witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abu Jamrah Nasr ibn Imran, from Ibn Abbas. And in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Abu Nadrah al-Mundhir, from Abu Said al-Khudri. I did not see this hadith in the Musnad of the Imam Ahmad, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3090","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Jabir al-Ansari al-Bayadi, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Jabir al-Ansari al-Bayadi, may Allah be pleased with him. 112 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us; Hashim - meaning Ibn al-Bariyyah - narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Ibn Jabir, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had poured out water, and I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, but he did not return it to me. So I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, but he did not return it to me. So I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, but he did not return it to me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked on with me behind him, until he entered his dwelling, and I entered the mosque and sat grieved and sorrowful. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to me after purifying himself and said: Upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah, upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah, upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah. Then he said: Shall I not inform you, O Abd Allah ibn Jabir, of the best surah in the Quran? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Recite: All praise is for Allah, Lord of the worlds, until you complete it. There is a mawquf in Muslim from the hadith of Abd Allah ibn Umar, who said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was urinating, and greeted him, but he did not return it to him."
"3091","Another. 113 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us (h). 114 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Madini narrated to us, both saying: Abd Allah ibn Sufyan ibn Uqbah narrated to us, saying: I heard my grandfather Uqbah ibn Abi Aishah say: I saw Abd Allah ibn Jabir al-Bayadi, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), placing one of his hands upon his forearms in prayer."
"3092","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Jubayr al-Khuzai, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Jubayr al-Khuzai, may Allah be pleased with him. 115 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us; Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Jubayr al-Khuzai, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pricked a man in his belly either with a stick or with a siwak. He said: You have hurt me, so let me retaliate. So he gave him the stick that was with him and said: Take retaliation. So he kissed his belly, then said: Rather I pardon you, perhaps you will intercede for me with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"3093","Another. 116 - And with it Amr ibn Hammad narrated to us; Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Jubayr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Ansar: Are you not pleased that I make the people the outer garment and you the inner garment? Are you not pleased that if the people took a valley and you took another, I would follow your valley and leave the people? And were it not that Allah Almighty named me among the Muhajirun, I would have loved to be among the Ansar. They said: Yes, we are pleased. Asbat ibn Nasr: some of them criticized him... and Yahya ibn Main declared him trustworthy, and Muslim narrated for him."
"3094","Another. 117 - And with it, from Abd Allah ibn Jubayr al-Khuzai, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was walking among some of his Companions when he was shaded with a garment, and when he saw its shadow he raised his head, and there he was shaded with a covering, so he said to him: Stop, and he took the garment and put it down, and said: I am only a human like you."
"3095","118 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Waki narrated to us (h). 119 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Jubayr al-Khuzai, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was walking with his Companions, a man from his Companions took a garment and shaded him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered it and said: I am only a human like you. Abu Hatim al-Razi mentioned that Abd Allah ibn Jubayr al-Khuzai, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), is mursal. And al-Bukhari said: Abd Allah ibn Jubayr al-Khuzai, from Abi al-Fil, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned; Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah said it, from al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr, from Simak, and it is not known except by this, and no companionship is known for Abi al-Fil."
"3096","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Jada, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Jada, may Allah be pleased with him. 120 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, who said: I sat with a group, I being their fourth, in Iliya, and one of them said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will enter Paradise through the intercession of a man from my nation more than Banu Tamim. We said: Other than you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Other than me. I said: Did you hear it? He said: Yes. And when he stood up I said: Who is this? They said: Ibn Abi al-Jada."
"3097","121 - And with it my father narrated to me; Affan narrated to us; Wuhayb narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Jada, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will enter Paradise through the intercession of a man from my nation more than Banu Tamim. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, other than you? He said: Other than me, other than me. So I said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard it."
"3098","122 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us; Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, saying: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli, who said: I sat with a group, I being their fourth, and a man was narrating, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will enter Paradise through the intercession of a man from my nation more than Banu Tamim. We said: Other than you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Other than me. He said: So I asked about him after he stood up, and they said to me: This is Ibn Abi al-Jada. Sufyan al-Thawri, Shubah, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal and Ali ibn Asim narrated it from Khalid al-Hadhdha. The Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Shubah, from Khalid similarly. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Kurayb, from Ismail ibn Ulayyah, and said: A hasan sahih hadith, and only this one hadith is known for him. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Affan ibn Muslim. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Yusuf, from Nasr ibn Ali, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, from Khalid al-Hadhdha."
"3099","Another. 123 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us; Amr ibn Awn narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Abi al-Jada, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a prophet? He said: While Adam was between the soul and the body."
"3100","124 - And Abu Muhammad Abd al-Razzaq ibn Nasr ibn al-Muslim ibn Nasr al-Najjar informed us in Damascus that Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Khadir ibn Sulayman ibn Said al-Sulami informed them; my father informed us; Abu al-Qasim al-Shaybani informed us; Abu al-Maymun Abd al-Rahman ibn Rashid narrated to us; Bakkar ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abi al-Jada, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a prophet? He said: When Adam was between the soul and the body. Thus is our hearing: from Abi al-Jada, but it is Ibn Abi al-Jada. Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq narrated it from Maysarah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. Al-Daraqutni mentioned a group of Companions whose hadiths were narrated through sound chains, with no aspersion on their transmitters, yet the two Shaykhs did not bring out their hadiths, so bringing them out is required by their method, and he mentioned among them Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Jada, whose hadith Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq from him."
"3101","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. Ismail ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father. 125 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed them, recitation in his presence; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Musab ibn Abd Allah ibn Musab ibn Abd Allah ibn Musab ibn Thabit ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam narrated to us in the city of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); my grandfather Musab ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Ismail ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father, who said: I saw upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two yellow garments."
"3102","126 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Musab ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Ismail ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two garments dyed with saffron, a cloak and a turban."
"3103","127 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Isbahani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdani informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us; Musab ibn Abd Allah ibn Musab al-Zubayri narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Ismail ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father, who said: I saw upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two garments dyed with saffron, a cloak and a turban."
"3104","Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father. 128 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father, regarding these words: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Mighty; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Teach them to your dying. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how are they for the living? He said: Better and better. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abu Amir al-Aqadi. Much has been said about Kathir before, and I did not see this hadith in the Musnad of the Imam Ahmad, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3105","Budayh, freedman of Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his master. 129 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us, from Juwayriyah ibn Asma (h). 130 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Isbahani narrated to us; Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated to us; Umar ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Riyahi narrated to us; Juwayriyah ibn Asma narrated to us, from Isa ibn Umar, from Budayh, who said: Abd Allah ibn Jafar came as a delegate to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, and entered upon him while Yahya ibn al-Hakam was with him, and he asked him, saying: How did you leave Khabitha - meaning Medina - so Abd Allah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named it Taybah and you call it Khabitha. It has a supporting witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Fatimah bint Qays, the hadith of al-Jassasah."
"3106","Al-Hasan ibn Sad ibn Mabad al-Kufi, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar. 131 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma, nephew of Juwayriyah, narrated to us (h). 132 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdani informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us (h). 133 - Sulayman said: And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, all saying: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Yaqub narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sad - Abu Yala al-Mawsili added: freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali - from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted me behind him one day, and confided to me a hadith I do not narrate to anyone, and the most beloved cover for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his need was a raised target or a dense date-palm grove, so he entered a garden of a man from the Ansar, and there was a camel in it, and when it saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it yearned and its eyes shed tears. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and wiped from its withers to its hump and its temples, and it calmed down, and said: Who is the owner of this camel? To whom does this camel belong? So a youth from the Ansar came and said: It is mine, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you not fear Allah regarding this beast which Allah has given you possession of? For it complained to me that you starve it and overwork it."
"3107","134 - And with it, Abu Yala informed us; Shayban narrated to us; Mahdi narrated to us with its chain, and mentioned similar to the hadith of Abd Allah. The wording of Abu Yala al-Mawsili. And in the narration of al-Tabarani: one day he confided to me, he did not say: behind him, and with him: he entered the garden of a man from the Ansar and there was a camel, and with him: its withers and its two temples and it calmed, then said: To whom does this camel belong? And with him: For it complained of you to me that you starve it and overwork it."
"3108","135 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us; my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub narrate from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode his mule and mounted me behind him, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieved himself, the most beloved place to relieve himself in was a concealing target or a dense date-palm grove, so he entered a garden of a man from the Ansar, and there was his water-carrying camel in it, and when it saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it yearned and its eyes shed tears, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted and wiped its temples and its withers and it calmed down, and said: Who is the owner of this camel? So a youth from the Ansar came and said: I am. So he said: Do you not fear Allah regarding this beast which Allah has given you possession of, for it complained of you to me and claimed that you starve it and overwork it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went in the garden and relieved himself, then performed ablution, then came with water dripping from his beard upon his chest, and confided to me something I do not narrate to anyone, so we urged him to narrate to us, and he said: I will not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until I meet Allah."
"3109","136 - And the Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered one day a garden from the gardens of the Ansar, and a camel came to him and its eyes shed tears, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped its withers and its temples and it calmed down, and said: Who is the owner of the camel? So a youth from the Ansar came and said: It is mine, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: Do you not fear Allah regarding this beast which Allah has given you possession of; it complained to me that you starve it and overwork it. Muslim brought out its beginning: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted me, up to his saying: a dense date-palm grove, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma and Shayban ibn Farrukh, both from Mahdi. And the Imam Ahmad also narrated it in full from Yazid ibn Harun, from Mahdi ibn Maymun similarly. And Abu Dawud brought it out in full from Musa ibn Ismail, from Mahdi ibn Maymun similarly. And Ibn Majah narrated part of it, its beginning, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Abi al-Numan, from Mahdi."
"3110","Another. 137 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us; my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub narrate from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army and put Zayd ibn Harithah in command over them: if Zayd is killed or martyred then your commander is Jafar, and if he is killed or martyred then your commander is Abd Allah ibn Rawahah. So they met the enemy and Zayd took the banner and fought until he was killed, then Jafar took the banner and fought until he was killed, then Abd Allah ibn Rawahah took it and fought until he was killed, then Khalid ibn al-Walid took the banner and Allah gave victory through him, and their news reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he went out to the people and praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: Your brothers met the enemy, and Zayd took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred, then after him Jafar ibn Abi Talib took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred, then Abd Allah ibn Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred, then a sword from the swords of Allah, Khalid ibn al-Walid, took the banner and Allah gave victory through him. Then he gave the family of Jafar three days respite before coming to them, then he came to them and said: Do not weep for my brother after today. Call to me the two sons of my brother. He said: So we were brought as if we were chicks, and he said: Call for me the barber, so the barber was brought and shaved our heads. He said: As for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib, and as for Abd Allah, he resembles my appearance and character. Then he took my hand and raised it and said: O Allah, take care of Jafar in his family, and bless Abd Allah in his dealings. He said it three times. He said: So our mother came and mentioned to him our orphanhood, and kept lamenting to him, so he said: Do you fear poverty for them while I am their guardian in this world and the Hereafter? His saying: lamenting to him, it is said: distressed him and removed grief from him, and it is narrated with jim. Ibn al-Arabi said: The comfortless is one who has no clan."
"3111","138 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdani informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us; Musa ibn Ismail al-Minqari narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us. 139 - Al-Tabarani said: And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Yaqub, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army and put Zayd ibn Harithah in command over them, saying: If he is killed or martyred then your commander is Jafar ibn Abi Talib, and if he is killed or martyred then your commander is Abd Allah ibn Rawahah. So they went and met the enemy, and Zayd ibn Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed, then Jafar took the banner and fought until he was killed, then Abd Allah ibn Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred, then a sword from the swords of Allah, Khalid ibn al-Walid, took the banner and Allah gave victory through him, and their news reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he went out and ascended the pulpit, and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, your brothers met the enemy, and Zayd ibn Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred, then Jafar took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred, then Abd Allah ibn Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred, then a sword from the swords of Allah, Khalid ibn al-Walid, took the banner and Allah gave victory through him. Then he gave the family of Jafar three days respite before coming to them, then he came to them and said: Do not weep for him after today. Then he said: Call to me the sons of my brother, so we were brought as if we were chicks. Then he said: Call for me the barber, so he commanded him and he shaved our heads. Then he said: As for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib, and as for Awn, he resembles my appearance and character. Then he took my hand and raised it, and said: O Allah, take care of Jafar in his family and bless Abd Allah in his dealings. He said it three times. He said: So our mother came and mentioned our orphanhood, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you fear poverty for them while I am their guardian in this world and the Hereafter?"
"3112","140 - And Abu Jafar also informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recitation in his presence while he was present; Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Ahmad ibn Bundar al-Shaar narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us; Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us; my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub narrate from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: O Allah, bless Abd Allah ibn Jafar in his dealings. Abu Dawud narrated from it that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the family of Jafar three days respite before coming to them, then he came to them and said: Do not weep for my brother after today. Then he said: Call to me the sons of my brother, so we were brought as if we were chicks, and he said: Call for me the barber, so he commanded him and he shaved our heads. From Uqbah ibn Mukram and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Wahb ibn Jarir. And al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Mansur and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, both from Wahb ibn Jarir with its chain, similar to what Abu Dawud narrated. And he narrated it in full from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Wahb, with its meaning. I say: In the first narration: Abd Allah, and in the second: Awn, and Allah knows best what is correct. It is mentioned in al-Bukhari from the narration of Abd Allah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded in the expedition of Mutah Zayd ibn Harithah, saying: If Zayd is killed then Jafar, and if Jafar is killed then Abd Allah ibn Rawahah. Abd Allah said: So I was with them in that expedition."
"3113","Khalid ibn Sarah, also said Ibn Ubayd ibn Sarah, al-Makhzumi al-Makki, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar. 141 - The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Jamil informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Khalid, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: When the news of Jafar came the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prepare food for the family of Jafar, for there has come to them what occupies them."
"3114","142 - And Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Sufyan narrated to us; Jafar ibn Khalid narrated to us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: When the news of Jafar came, when he was killed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prepare food for the family of Jafar, for there has come to them a matter that occupies them, or: there has come to them what occupies them."
"3115","143 - And Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh al-Isbahani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us; al-Humaydi narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Khalid, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: When the news of Jafar came the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make food for the family of Jafar, for there has come to them what occupies them. Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari and Abd al-Razzaq narrated it from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Sufyan. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani and Ali ibn Hujr, from Sufyan, and said: A hasan hadith. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Hisham ibn Ammar and Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from Sufyan similarly."
"3116","Another. 144 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Sayrafi informed them; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Muallim informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Jamil informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us; Rawh narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, saying: Jafar ibn Khalid informed me that his father informed him, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his hand over my head three times. He said: When he wiped he said: O Allah, take care of Jafar in his offspring."
"3117","145 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us; Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Jafar ibn Khalid, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his head three times and said: O Allah, take care of Jafar in his family."
"3118","Another. 146 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Rawh narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; Jafar ibn Khalid ibn Sarah informed me that his father informed him that Abd Allah ibn Jafar said: If you had seen me and Qutham and Ubayd Allah ibn Abbas while we were boys playing, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by upon a mount and said: Lift this one to me, so he carried me in front of him, and said to Qutham: Lift this one to me, so he placed him behind him. And Ubayd Allah was more beloved to Abbas than Qutham, yet he was not shy before his uncle to carry Qutham and leave him. He said: Then he wiped over his head three times and said each time he wiped: O Allah, take care of Jafar in his offspring. He said: I said to Abd Allah: What happened to Qutham? He said: He was martyred. He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best what is good. He said: Yes."
"3119","147 - And the Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Qurashi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Ishaq informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us; Rawh narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, saying: Jafar ibn Khalid informed me that his father informed him that Abd Allah ibn Jafar said: If you had seen me and Qutham and Ubayd Allah, the two sons of al-Abbas, while we were boys playing, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by upon a mount and said: Lift this one to me, so he placed me in front of him, and said to Qutham: Lift this one to me. He said: So he placed him behind him. I say: And this hadith is other than the one Muslim narrated from the narration of Mawraq al-Ijli, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar; for that was when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came from a journey, would be met by the children of his household, so I was met with one of the two sons of Fatimah, either Hasan or Husayn, and he carried one of us in front of him and the other behind him."
"3120","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar. 148 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja informed them; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Muallim informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us (h). 149 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yazid - he is Ibn Harun - narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, saying: I saw Ibn Abi Rafi wearing a ring on his right, so I asked him about that and he mentioned that he saw Abd Allah ibn Jafar wearing a ring on his right. Abd Allah ibn Jafar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a ring on his right. Their wording is one."
"3121","150 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us; Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a ring on his right."
"3122","151 - And Abu Jafar also informed us - as I recall - that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, recitation in his presence while he was present; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Abi Asim informed us; Hudbah narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, raised, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a ring on his right."
"3123","152 - And with it, Ahmad ibn Abi Asim informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: I saw the ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his right."
"3124","153 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Husayn informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a ring on his right."
"3125","154 - And with it, Abu Yala informed us; Ibn Numayr narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a ring on his right. The Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani and said: Muhammad - meaning al-Bukhari - said: And this is the soundest thing narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this chapter. And he narrated it in al-Shamail from Yahya ibn Musa, from Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Mamar, from Hibban, from Hammad ibn Salamah with its chain: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a ring on his right. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah."
"3126","Another. 155 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us, from Ahmad; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Samad narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Rafi, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: that he married his daughter to al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, and said to her: When he comes to you then say: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And he claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a matter distressed him, would say this. Hammad said: So I thought he said: And he did not reach her."
"3127","156 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi, that Abd Allah ibn Jafar said to his daughter when al-Hajjaj consummated with her: When he comes to you then say: There is no god but Allah, the High, the Mighty; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And he claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say it when hardship befell him, so she said it and he did not reach her. Al-Nasai narrated it in the book of the deeds of day and night, from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith, from Hammad. He also narrated it from Qutaybah, from Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And from Ubayd Allah ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim, from his uncle Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Aban ibn Salih, from Muhammad ibn Kab, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from Ali, peace be upon him, and it has paths in his book to Ali, peace be upon him. And the well-known is that it is from the narration of Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his uncle Ali ibn Abi Talib, peace be upon him."
"3128","Ubayd ibn Abi Kilab, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar. 157 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim and Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Mihrabazd both said: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani informed us; Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ayyub and Ibn Lahiah informed me, from Abi al-Aswad, that he heard Ubayd ibn Abi Kilab while informing Urwah ibn al-Zubayr that he heard Abd Allah ibn Jafar say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sneezed he praised Allah, so it would be said to him: May Allah have mercy on you, and he would say: May Allah guide you and set right your state. Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated it from Ibn Lahiah. And the Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ishaq ibn Isa and Yahya ibn Ishaq together, from Ibn Lahiah. We only brought it out for the narration of Yahya ibn Ayyub of it, for he is from the men of Muslim."
"3129","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar. 158 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr, grandson of Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Mandah, informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, author of al-Maghazi, narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded (h)."
"3130","159 - And al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yaqub narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, saying: Hisham ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father Urwah, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded (h)."
"3131","160 - And Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Asadi informed us in Damascus that his grandfather Abu al-Qasim al-Husayn informed them; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Massisi informed us, recitation in his presence, saying: I read upon Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ukbari therein and he acknowledged it; my father narrated to us; Abu Khalifah narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us; Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq; Hisham ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to give Khadijah glad tidings of a house of hollowed pearl in which there is no noise nor toil. In the narration of Ahmad, author of al-Maghazi: to give Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollowed pearl in which there is no noise nor toil. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Qahtabah, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim, from Wahb ibn Jarir, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq. It has a supporting witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3132","Another. 161 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, recitation in his presence while he was present; Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us (h). 162 - And Abu Jafar also informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, both saying: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Salih al-Qasim ibn al-Layth al-Rasibi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar Dhi al-Janahayn, who said: When Abu Talib died the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Taif walking on his feet, and he called them to Allah but they did not answer him, so he came to the shade of a tree and prayed two rakahs beneath it, then said: O Allah, to You I complain of my weakness and my lowliness before people, Most Merciful of the merciful, to whom do You entrust me, to a distant one who frowns upon me or to a near one to whom You have given my affair; if You are not angry with me then I do not care, to You is pleasing until You are pleased, and there is no might nor power except by You. I seek refuge in the light of Your Noble Face by which the heavens were lit and the darknesses shone and by which the affair of this world and the Hereafter was set right, from Your anger descending upon me or Your wrath alighting upon me. The wording of the narration of Ibn Fadhshah from al-Tabarani, and he did not say in the narration of Ibn Ridhah his saying: Dhi al-Janahayn. And with him: When Abu Talib passed away, and with him: he called them to Islam but they did not answer him, so he turned away and came to the shade of a tree and prayed two rakahs, then said: O Allah, to You I complain of the weakness of my strength, the paucity of my means and my lowliness before people, Most Merciful of the merciful, You are the Most Merciful of the merciful, to whom do You entrust me, to an enemy who frowns upon me or to a near one to whom You have given my affair; if You are not angry with me then I do not care, except that Your well-being is more spacious for me. I seek refuge in the light of Your Face by which the darknesses shone and by which the affair of this world and the Hereafter was set right, from Your anger descending upon me or Your wrath alighting upon me. To You is pleasing until You are pleased, and there is no might nor power except by You."
"3133","Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, also said Utbah ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar. 163 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us therein that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them; Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us; Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; the Imam my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us; Abu Musa narrated to us; Rawh narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Musafi informed me that Musab ibn Shaybah informed him, from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever forgets something in his prayer should prostrate two prostrations while sitting. Thus Abu Musa said to us, from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, and the companions of Ibn Jurayj differ over the name of this sheikh. Hajjaj ibn Muhammad and Abd al-Razzaq said: from Utbah ibn Muhammad, and this is the correct in my knowledge."
"3134","164 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us; Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us (h). 165 - Al-Tabarani said: And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Yahya ibn Main narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, both from Ibn Jurayj; Abd Allah ibn Musafi informed me, from Musab ibn Shaybah, from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever doubts about something in his prayer should prostrate two prostrations after he gives salam."
"3135","166 - And Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Said informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Hajjaj narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj said: Abd Allah ibn Musafi informed me that Musab ibn Shaybah informed him, from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever doubts in his prayer should prostrate two prostrations after he gives salam. The Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Rawh ibn Ubadah. And from Ali ibn Ishaq, from Ibn al-Mubarak, and he did not mention Musab ibn Shaybah in this narration. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Ibrahim, from Hajjaj ibn Muhammad with its chain, except that with him is Utbah ibn Muhammad. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim, from Hajjaj. And from Harun ibn Abd Allah, from Hajjaj and Rawh. And from Suwayd ibn Nasr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak. And from Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Balabakki, from al-Walid, all from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd Allah ibn Musafi, from Utbah ibn Muhammad, and he did not mention Musab. And Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih as we brought it out. And Musab ibn Shaybah: it is narrated from Ahmad ibn Hanbal that he said: He has rejected hadiths. And al-Daraqutni said: He is not strong."
"3136","Al-Qasim ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar. 167 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them while he was present; Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us; Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us; Said ibn al-Saib al-Taifi narrated to me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Thaqafi, that Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Asma informed him that al-Qasim ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed him that Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first of my nation for whom I intercede are the people of Medina, the people of Mecca and the people of Taif. Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned Said ibn al-Saib al-Taifi, narrating from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Zuhayr. And he mentioned Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Tayma al-Thaqafi, from whom Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Zuhayr narrated."
"3137","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar. 168 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them; Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated to us; Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"3138","169 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us that Hibat Allah informed him; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us (h). 170 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a prophet to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta. The wording of the Imam Ahmad. And in the narration of al-Azdi: It is not fitting for a prophet to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Salamah similarly. It has a supporting witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah: It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta, peace be upon him, and in them from the hadith of Rufay, from Ibn Abbas."
"3139","Another. 171 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us; Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us; Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: He forbade killing them. Meaning the snakes that are in houses. It has a supporting witness in the two Sahihs, the hadith of Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir al-Ansari."
"3140","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar. 172 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recitation in his presence while he was present -; Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Faris informed us; Ismail ibn Abd Allah Sammuyah informed us; Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Said ibn Sufyan, from Jafar, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is with the debtor until he repays his debt, so long as his debt is not what Allah Almighty dislikes."
"3141","173 - And Abu Jafar also informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present -; Abu Nuaym informed us (h). 174 - And Abu Jafar also informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, both saying: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us; al-Humaydi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us; Said ibn Sufyan al-Aslami narrated to me, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Almighty, is with the indebted until he repays his debt, so long as his debt is not in what Allah dislikes. The wording of Abu Nuaym from al-Tabarani. And in the narration of Ibn Ridhah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah Almighty is with the debtor. And the rest is similar. And in the narration of Abu Nuaym, al-Tabarani said: This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Jafar except with this chain; Ibn Abi Fudayk is alone in it."
"3142","175 - And Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Sulami al-Dimashqi informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them by ijazah, and it was said to our sheikh: Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Ghazzal informed you, recitation in his presence; Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us, both saying: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us; al-Humaydi narrated to us (h). 176 - Abu Nuaym said: And Abu Ahmad ibn al-Sindi narrated to us; Musa ibn Harun the Hafiz narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us; Said ibn Sufyan, freedman of the Aslamis, narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is with the debtor until he repays his debt, so long as it is not in what Allah dislikes. He said: So Abd Allah ibn Jafar used to say to his treasurer: Go and take a debt for me, for I dislike to spend a night except with Allah with me, after what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Abd Allah Ibn Majah brought it out from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami with the words of Abd Allah ibn Jafar."
"3143","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Fahmi, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar. 177 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yahya narrated to us; Misar narrated to us; a sheikh from Fahm narrated to me - and I think he is called Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman - he said: and I think he is Hijazi, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrate to Ibn al-Zubayr, when a slaughter-camel or camel had been slaughtered for the people, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the people were offering meat to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The best meat is the meat of the back."
"3144","178 - And Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present -; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Misar, from a sheikh from Fahm, who heard Abd Allah ibn Jafar say: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when food was mentioned, and I heard him say: The best meat is the meat of the back."
"3145","179 - And with it Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, saying: Musaddad informed us; Yahya ibn Said narrated to us; Misar narrated to us, from a man from Fahm called Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"3146","180 - And Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us. 181 - And Abu Jafar also informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present -; Abu Nuaym informed us, both saying: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhui and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, both saying: Musaddad narrated to us; Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Misar, from a man from Fahm called Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best meat is the meat of the back."
"3147","182 - And Abu Jafar informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Abu Nuaym narrated to us; Misar narrated to us, from a sheikh from Fahm, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best meat is the meat of the back."
"3148","183 - And Abu Jafar informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them, while he was present; Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Khallad narrated to us; al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah narrated to us; Abu Nuaym narrated to us; Misar narrated to us, from a man from Fahm: I heard Abd Allah ibn Jafar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best - or: best - meat is the meat of the back. The Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Waki, from Misar. And from Hashim ibn al-Qasim, from al-Masudi: a sheikh who came to us from Hijaz narrated to us, saying: I witnessed Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr and Abd Allah ibn Jafar at Muzdalifah, and Ibn al-Zubayr would cut meat for Abd Allah ibn Jafar, so Abd Allah ibn Jafar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best meat is the meat of the back. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it in al-Shamail from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, from Misar. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Yahya, from Misar, from a man from Fahm. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Bakr ibn Khalaf, from Yahya ibn Said, from Misar, saying: A sheikh from Fahm narrated to me, I think he is called Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, similarly."
"3149","Muawiyah ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father. 184 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us therein that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad al-Darimi and his grandfather Abu Nasr Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Asim al-Sufi both informed them, recitation upon them, both saying: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Farisi informed us, saying: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Qarrab informed us; Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Hamid ibn Mamar ibn Imran ibn Hassan ibn Sulayman ibn Qays ibn Ziyad ibn Amr ibn al-Mundhir al-Shami narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Yazid, from Muawiyah ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people shooting at a ram, and said: Do not mutilate animals."
"3150","185 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Musab - he is Ibn Abd Allah - narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to me, from Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Muawiyah ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people shooting a ram with arrows and disliked that, and said: Do not mutilate animals. Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated it from Yazid ibn Abd Allah. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Zunbur."
"3151","Another. 186 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari and Abu Hamid al-Isbahani both said: Abu Zurah Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Jafar ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; my uncle Musa ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muawiyah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ali is my root and Jafar is my branch. Or: Jafar is my root and Ali is my branch."
"3152","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz ibn Madi Karib ibn Amr ibn Usm ibn Uwayj ibn Amr ibn Zubayd al-Zubaydi, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz ibn Madi Karib ibn Amr ibn Usm ibn Uwayj ibn Amr ibn Zubayd al-Zubaydi - he settled in Egypt and went blind before his death - Yahya ibn Bukayr said: he died in the year eighty-six. 187 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us therein that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Abu Yazid Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Karimah al-Muqri narrated to us; Utbah ibn Thumamah al-Muradi narrated to me, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz came to us in Egypt and I heard him narrate in the mosque of Egypt, and he was asked about what fire touched, and he said: I saw myself as one of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of a man, when Bilal passed and called for prayer, so we went out and passed by a man with his pot upon the fire, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Has your pot cooked well? He said: Yes, by my father and mother. So he took a piece from it and kept chewing it until he entered prayer while I was looking at him."
"3153","188 - And Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Saud al-Busiri informed us in Egypt that Abu Sadiq Murshid ibn Yahya ibn al-Qasim al-Madini informed them, recitation in his presence; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad al-Khallal informed us in his book; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Qammah informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Qudayd al-Azdi informed us; Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Sarh narrated to us; Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Karimah al-Maafiri narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Thumamah al-Muradi, who said: Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi - from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - came to us in Egypt, and I heard him narrate in the mosque of Egypt, so it was said to him: What brought you to Egypt when you have no sword-stroke, spear-thrust nor arrow-shot in you? He said: I came to be in the ranks of the Muslims, perhaps a stray arrow will come to me and kill me. It was said to him: What do you say about what fire touched? He said: And what has fire touched? It was said to him: Cooked or ripened meat. He said: I saw myself as one of seven - or: one of six - with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of a man, when Bilal passed and called him to prayer, so he went out and passed by a man with his pot upon the fire, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Has your pot cooked? He said: Yes, by my father and you my mother. So he took a piece from it and kept chewing it until he entered prayer while I was looking at him. Ibn Qudayd said: Abu al-Tahir Ahmad ibn Amr narrated it to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Karimah similarly. Abu Dawud narrated it similarly from Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh."
"3154","Another. 189 - The Imam Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja ibn Ghanaim the preacher informed us between Cairo and Egypt that Abu Sabir Abd al-Sabur ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi informed them; Abu Amir Mahmud ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad informed us; Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Marwazi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub informed us; Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sawrah al-Tirmidhi informed us; Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Khallal narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ishaq, he is al-Silayhini, narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz, who said: The laughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was only smiling. Thus al-Tirmidhi narrated it and said: A sahih gharib hadith, we know it from the hadith of Layth ibn Sad only from this angle. And the Imam Ahmad narrated from Musa ibn Dawud, from Ibn Lahiah, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, who said: I never saw anyone smile more than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And from Hajjaj, from Ibn Lahiah, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Harith say: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except smiling."
"3155","Another. 190 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us; Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Amr ibn al-Harith informed me. He said: And Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami narrated to me that he heard Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Zubaydi say: We used to eat in the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque bread and meat, then pray without performing ablution."
"3156","191 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Amr ibn al-Harith informed us; Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami narrated to me that he heard Abd Allah ibn al-Harith say: We used to eat in the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque bread and meat, then pray without performing ablution."
"3157","192 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Haywah ibn Shurayh informed me, from Uqbah ibn Muslim, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, who said: Food was placed in the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in al-Suffah, so we ate, then prayer was established and we prayed without performing ablution."
"3158","193 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Harun, he is Ibn Maruf, narrated to us; Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard from Harun; Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us; Haywah ibn Shurayh informed me; Uqbah ibn Muslim informed me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, who said: We were one day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in al-Suffah when food was placed for us and we ate, then prayer was established and we prayed without performing ablution. Ibn Majah narrated it from Harmalah ibn Yahya. And Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah."
"3159","Another. 194 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that Zahir al-Shahhami informed them; Muhammad al-Kanjrudhi informed us; al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Tamimi narrated to us by dictation; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Duwayri narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib (h). 195 - And Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid al-Isbahani informed us that his grandfather Ghanim ibn Khalid informed them; Abu al-Tayyib Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Zabban ibn Habib ibn Zabban narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, saying: al-Layth informed us, from Yazid - he is Ibn Abi Habib - that he heard Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi say: I am the first who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Let none of you urinate facing the qiblah, and I am the first who narrated that to people. The wording of Ibn Rumh. And in the narration of Qutaybah: I am the first who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Let none of you urinate... and the rest is similar. Amr ibn al-Harith and Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated it from Yazid."
"3160","196 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, who said: I am the first who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid urinating facing the qiblah."
"3161","197 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us; Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Ghawth ibn Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami narrated to us; my father Sulayman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, saying: We entered upon Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz on Friday and he called for a basin and said to the servant girl: Screen me, so she screened him and he urinated in it, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid that one of you urinate facing the qiblah."
"3162","198 - And with it al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Muhammad al-Ansanawi narrated to us; Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, who said: I am the first who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Let none of you urinate facing the qiblah. The Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Asim. And from Yunus ibn Muhammad, Hajjaj and Musa ibn Dawud, from Layth. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rumh. And Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab. It has a supporting witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3163","Another. 199 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to him that he heard Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: In Hell there are snakes like the necks of Bactrian camels; they sting one of you the sting and he feels its heat for forty autumns."
"3164","200 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us; Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Amr informed me: that Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to him that he heard Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: In Hell there are snakes like the necks of Bactrian camels; they sting one of them the sting and he feels its heat for forty autumns, and in it there are scorpions like bridled mules; one of them stings and he feels its heat for forty autumns. The Imam Ahmad narrated it from Musa ibn Dawud and Hasan ibn Musa, from Ibn Lahiah, from Darraj like the narration of Harmalah. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Salim, from Harmalah. Ahmad ibn Rashdin: we brought him out for consideration."
"3165","Another. 201 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us therein that Abu al-Qasim Tamim ibn Abi Said al-Jurjani informed them; Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn Masrur the ascetic informed us, recitation in his presence; Abu Amr Ismail ibn Nujayd al-Sulami narrated to us; Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Said al-Bushanji narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Bukayr narrated to us (h). 202 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Harmalah narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to me (h). 203 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us; Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; Nafi ibn Yazid and al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, both saying: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us. And in the narration of Ibn Bukayr, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Uqbah ibn Muslim, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels and the soles of the feet from Hell. The wording of Ibn Bukayr. And in the narration of Said ibn Abi Maryam there is not: and the soles of the feet. The Imam Ahmad narrated it from Harun ibn Maruf, from Ibn Wahb, from Haywah with its chain, and he did not raise it. Abd Allah said: And I heard it from Harun. And from Hasan ibn Musa, from Ibn Lahiah, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, raised."
"3166","Another. 204 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Said informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Harun narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us; Amr narrated to us that Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi narrated to him (h)."
"3167","205 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them; Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us; Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Amr informed me that Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi narrated to him that he and a companion of his passed by Ayman and youths from Quraysh who had loosened their waist-wrappers and made them into whips with which they struck one another while naked. Abd Allah said: When we passed by them they said: These are priests, so leave them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them, and when they saw him they scattered, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned angry until he entered, and I was behind the chamber hearing him say: Glory be to Allah, they were neither shy before Allah nor concealed themselves from His Messenger, while Umm Ayman was saying: Seek forgiveness for him, O Messenger of Allah. Abd Allah said: By my father, he did not seek forgiveness for him. The wording of Harmalah. And in the narration of Harun: that he and a companion of his passed by, and with him that these are priests, and with him: so I heard him say: Glory be to Allah, they were neither shy before Allah nor concealed themselves from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umm Ayman with him saying: Seek forgiveness for them, O Messenger of Allah. Abd Allah said: By my father, he did not seek forgiveness for them."
"3168","206 - And Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Kanjani informed us in Isfahan that Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Tayyan informed us; Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshayd informed us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi informed us; Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi narrated to him that he passed by Ayman... and mentioned similarly."
"3169","Another. 207 - Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Ulabi ibn Saud al-Ansari informed us in Egypt that Murshid ibn Yahya ibn al-Qasim al-Madini informed them, recitation in his presence; Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad al-Khallal informed us in his book; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Qammah informed us; Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Khalaf ibn Qudayd al-Azdi informed us; Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, saying: The hadith of al-Layth ibn Sad, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, who said: A man from those who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a stranger died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while at the grave: What is your name? So I said: al-Asi. And he said to Ibn Amr: And what is your name? So he said: al-Asi. And he said to al-Asi ibn al-Asi: What is your name? He said: al-Asi. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Asi, you are Abd Allah, dismount. He said: So we buried our companion, then we came out of the grave with our names changed. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam said: Shuayb ibn al-Layth, Abd Allah ibn Salih and Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Bukayr narrated it to us."
"3170","208 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by ijazah if not by hearing; Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Sad informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz, who said: A companion of ours who was a stranger died in Medina, and we were at his grave, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is your name? So I said: al-Asi. And he said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: What is your name? So he said: al-Asi. And he said to Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As: What is your name? So he said: al-Asi. So he said: Dismount and bury him, for you are Abd Allah. He said: So we buried our brother, and came out with our names changed. Thus in the narration of Ibn Wahb... Abd Allah ibn Umar, and it is a mistake, and Allah knows best. And al-Tabarani narrated it from Muttalib ibn Shuayb, from Abd Allah ibn Salih, from al-Layth with its chain. And in it: And he said to al-Asi ibn al-Asi, instead of Abd Allah ibn Umar, and with him: You are Ubayd Allah. Al-Daraqutni mentioned a group of Companions that al-Bukhari or Muslim must bring out their hadith, and mentioned Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, the narration of Yazid ibn Abi Habib from him."
"3171","Musnad Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim, may Allah be pleased with him. 209 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Halabi narrated to us; Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us; al-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who said: Abd Allah ibn al-Harith used to pass by us saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed food and spread peace, you will inherit gardens."
"3172","Another. 210 - And with it, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Abi Salman, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray with Umamah bint Abi al-As upon his shoulder; when he bowed he put her down, and when he stood he carried her. Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib: I saw no mention of him in the Tarikh of al-Bukhari, nor did Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim mention him in his book. And Abu Salman: Abu Ahmad did not mention him in the book of al-Kuna, except that his hadith has a supporting witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abu Qatadah al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3173","Musnad Abd Allah al-Bahili Abi Mujibah, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Bahili Abu Mujibah, may Allah be pleased with him. 211 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, recitation in his presence while he was present; Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Jurayri, from Abi al-Salil, from Abi Mujibah, from his father or his uncle, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am the man who came to you last year. He said: Why do I see your body emaciated? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not eaten food in the daytime since I pledged to you. So he said: Who commanded you to torment yourself? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am strong. He said: Fast the month of patience and two days after it. I said: I am strong. He said: Fast the month of patience and three days after it, and fast the sacred months."
"3174","212 - And Abu Hamid Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit al-Baghdadi informed us therein that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzaz informed them; Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Kaysan the grammarian informed us; Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ismail ibn Hammad ibn Zayd the judge informed us; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abi al-Salil, from Mujibah al-Bahiliyyah, from her father or her uncle: that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then left, and returned to him after a year with his state and appearance changed, and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you not recognize me? He said: And who are you? He said: I am the Bahili who came to you last year. He said: What changed you when you were of good appearance? He said: I have not eaten food since I left you except at night. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And why did you torment yourself? Fast the month of patience, and one day from each month. He said: Increase for me, for I have strength. He said: Fast two days from each month. He said: Increase for me, for I have strength. He said: Fast three days from each month. He said: Increase for me, for I have strength. He said: Fast from the sacred months and leave. Saying it three times. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musa ibn Ismail, from Hammad ibn Salamah similarly. And al-Nasai narrated it from Abdah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Dawud al-Hafari, from Sufyan, from al-Jurayri, from Abi al-Salil, from Mujibah al-Bahili, from his uncle similarly, thus he mentioned it. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah with its chain from Abi Mujibah, from his father or his uncle."
"3175","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Hubshi al-Khathami, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Hubshi al-Khathami, may Allah be pleased with him. 213 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali the preacher informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said: Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to me, from Ali al-Azdi, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Abd Allah ibn Hubshi al-Khathami: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: Faith in which there is no doubt, striving in which there is no misappropriation, and an accepted pilgrimage. It was said: Then which prayer is best? He said: Length of standing. It was said: Then which charity is best? He said: The effort of one of little means. It was said: Then which emigration is best? He said: Whoever abandons what Allah has forbidden to him. It was said: Then which striving is best? He said: Whoever strives against the polytheists with his wealth and himself. It was said: Then which killing is noblest? He said: Whose blood is shed and whose horse is hamstrung."
"3176","214 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya ibn Main narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ali al-Azdi, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Abd Allah ibn Hubshi al-Khathami: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: Faith in which there is no doubt, striving in which there is no misappropriation, and an accepted pilgrimage. It was said: Then which prayer is best? He said: Length of standing. It was said: Then which charity is best? He said: The effort of one of little means. It was said: Then which emigration is best? He said: Whoever abandons what Allah has forbidden. It was said: Then which striving is best? He said: Whoever strives against the polytheists with his wealth and himself. It was said: Then which killing is noblest? He said: Whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed. Abu Dawud narrated it from the Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal. And al-Nasai narrated it from Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Hakam al-Warraq, from Hajjaj. And he narrated part of it from Harun ibn Abd Allah, from Hajjaj."
"3177","Another. 215 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah al-Juzdani informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Said ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Abd Allah ibn Hubshi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts a lote-tree, Allah will plunge his head into Hell. Abu Dawud narrated it from Nasr ibn Ali, from Abu Usamah, from Ibn Jurayj. And from Makhlad ibn Khalid and Salamah ibn Shabib, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from a man from Thaqif, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And al-Nasai narrated it from Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mustam, from Makhlad ibn Yazid, from Ibn Jurayj, saying: Abd Allah al-Khathami. Al-Daraqutni mentioned a group of Companions whose bringing out is required of al-Bukhari and Muslim or one of them, and mentioned Abd Allah ibn Hubshi al-Khathami, whose hadith Ibn Jurayj narrated from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ali al-Azdi, from Ubayd ibn Umayr from him, all of them from their category."
"3178","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Abi Habibah al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Abi Habibah al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. 216 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us; Mujammi ibn Yaqub - from the people of Quba - narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to me that some of his family said to his grandfather from his mother side, he being Abd Allah ibn Abi Habibah: What did you attain from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He came to us in this mosque of ours, so I came and sat beside him, and drink was brought then handed to me while I was on his right. He said: And I saw him that day pray in his sandals while I was then a boy."
"3179","217 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdani informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us (h). 218 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; al-Qanabi narrated to us, both saying: Mujammi ibn Yaqub al-Ansari narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ismail, who said: It was said to Abd Allah ibn Abi Habibah: What did you attain from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us in our mosque in Quba, so I came while a young boy until I sat on his right, and Abu Bakr sat on his left. He said: Then he called for drink and drank and handed to me on his right."
"3180","And with it he said: It was said to Abd Allah ibn Abi Habibah: What did you attain from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He stood praying and I saw him pray in his sandals. The Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Said. Abd Allah said: And Qutaybah wrote it to me from Mujammi ibn Yaqub. And from Yunus ibn Muhammad, from al-Attaf, from Mujammi, from a boy from the boys of the people of Quba, that he reached him as an old man, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us in Quba and sat in the courtyard of the stone houses and people gathered to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for drink, and mentioned it. It has a supporting witness in the mention of drink in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Sahl ibn Sad: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought drink and drank, with a boy on his right and elders on his left, so he said to the boy: Do you permit me to give these? So he said: By Allah, I would not prefer anyone with my share from you. So he placed it in his hand. And prayer in sandals: in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abi Maslamah Said ibn Yazid, from Anas ibn Malik."
"3181","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him. 219 - Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yaqub narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq; Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt narrated to me, from al-Qaqa ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Hadrad, from his father Abd Allah ibn Abi Hadrad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us to Idam, so I went out among a group of Muslims including Abu Qatadah al-Harith and Muhallam ibn Jathamah ibn Qays, and we went out until we were in the valley of Idam when Amir al-Ashjai passed by us upon a young camel of his with a follower of his and a skin of milk, and when he passed by us he greeted us and we held back from him, and Muhallam ibn Jathamah attacked him and killed him over something between him and him, and took his camel and his follower. And when we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him the news, the Quran came down regarding us: O you who believe, when you go out in the path of Allah then verify and do not say to whoever greets you: You are not a believer, seeking the goods of worldly life, for with Allah are many spoils; thus you were before and Allah favored you, so verify; Allah is Aware of what you do."
"3182","220 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us; Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt narrated to me, from Ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Hadrad, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us to Idam, so I went out among a group of Muslims including Abu Qatadah al-Harith ibn Ribi and Muhallam ibn Jathamah ibn Qays, and we went out until when we were in the valley of Idam, Amir ibn al-Adbat al-Ashjai passed by us upon a young camel with a follower of his and a skin of milk, and when he passed by us he greeted us with the greeting of Islam, so we held back from him, and Muhallam ibn Jathamah attacked him and killed him over an evil between him and him, and took his camel and his follower. And when we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him the news, the Quran came down regarding us: O you who believe, when you go out in the path of Allah then verify... the verse. Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, from his father. Neither Muhammad ibn Salamah nor Hammad ibn Salamah named Ibn Abi Hadrad in their narrations. And Yaqub named him, from his father, in the narration of the Imam Ahmad from Yaqub. This hadith has a supporting witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas similarly."
"3183","Another. 221 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi and Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid informed us that Ghanim ibn Khalid informed them; Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us; Isa ibn Hammad narrated to us, saying: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Ismail ibn al-Qaqa ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Hadrad, that he said: My grandfather Abd Allah ibn Abi Hadrad married a woman for four uqiyahs, and informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of that, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you were carving from Quba - or he said: from Uhud - you would not add; that with us is half her dowry. Abd Allah said: So I went and gathered it and paid it to my wife, then I informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of that, so he said: Did I not say to you with us is half the dowry, so perhaps you did that because of my saying. So I said: No, O Messenger of Allah, and I had only that. Ibn Abi Hatim did not mention Ismail ibn al-Qaqa, nor do I verify his hearing from his grandfather, except that he said Abd Allah: So I went and gathered it and paid it to my wife."
"3184","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah ibn Qays ibn Adi al-Sahmi Abu Hudhafah, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah ibn Qays ibn Adi al-Sahmi Abu Hudhafah, may Allah be pleased with him. 222 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali the preacher al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd Allah - meaning Ibn Abi Bakr - and Salim Abi al-Nadr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to announce in the days of Tashriq that they are days of eating and drinking."
"3185","223 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking."
"3186","224 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Masud ibn al-Hakam al-Ansari, from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah al-Sahmi to ride his mount on the days of Mina and shout among the people: Let no one fast, for they are days of eating and drinking. He said: I saw him upon his mount announcing that. Al-Nasai narrated it from Abbas al-Anbari, from Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Salim and Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr. And from Muhammad ibn Rafi, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar with its chain. I say: And this narration is not from the narration of Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah, and the hadith of Sulayman ibn Yasar from Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah: Yahya ibn Main said: Sulayman ibn Yasar did not hear from Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah. And Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He did not reach him. Except that it has a supporting witness in the Sahih of Muslim from the hadith of Nubayshah al-Hudhali: The days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking, and he mentioned part of it."
"3187","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hamsa, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hamsa, may Allah be pleased with him. 225 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them; Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us; Muadh ibn Hani narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us; Budayl ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hamsa, who said: I traded with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before he was sent, and something remained owed to him from me, so I promised him to come to him at his place, but I forgot to come to him that day and the next, so I came to him on the third day and found him in that same place, and he said to me: You have burdened me; I am here for three days."
"3188","226 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Awfi narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abd al-Karim, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hamsa, who said: I traded with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before he was sent, and a remainder remained for him, so I promised him to bring it to him at that same place, but I forgot my day and the next, so I came to him on the third day and found him in his place, and he said: O youth, you have burdened me; I am here for three days waiting for you. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi, from Muhammad ibn Sinan. Muhammad ibn Yahya said: This with us is: Abd al-Karim ibn Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq. Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated it from Ibrahim, from Budayl, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hamsa, from his father. And Abu Awn al-Ziyadi narrated it from Ibrahim, from Budayl, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hamsa, and perhaps what is correct is what Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Awfi said. And Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi: we brought him out for consideration."
"3189","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Hanzalah, washed by the angels, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd Allah ibn Hanzalah, washed by the angels, may Allah be pleased with him. 227 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti both said: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, who said: I said to Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar: Did Ibn Umar perform ablution for every prayer? So he said: Asma bint Zayd ibn al-Khattab narrated to me that Abd Allah ibn Hanzalah narrated to her: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded with ablution for every prayer, whether pure or not pure, and when it became hard upon them he was commanded with the siwak for every prayer, and Ibn Umar saw that he had strength for that, and would perform ablution for every prayer, whether pure or not pure."
"3190","228 - And Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yaqub narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban al-Ansari then al-Mazini, Mazin of Banu al-Najjar, narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, who said: I said to him: What about the ablution of Abd Allah ibn Umar for every prayer, whether pure or not pure, what is it? So he said: Asma bint Zayd ibn al-Khattab narrated to me: that Abd Allah ibn Hanzalah ibn Abi Amir ibn al-Ghasil narrated to her: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded with ablution for every prayer, whether pure or not pure, and when that became hard upon the Messenger of Allah he commanded the siwak at every prayer and ablution was lifted from him except from ritual impurity. He said: So Abd Allah saw that he had strength for that and would do it until he died. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Awf al-Tai, from Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi. Abu Dawud said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated it from Ibn Ishaq, saying Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah: and this is the narration which the Imam Ahmad narrated from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, from his father. Abu al-Qasim al-Dimashqi said: Ali ibn Mujahid and Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated it from Ibn Ishaq, inserting between him and Muhammad: Muhammad ibn Talhah. I say, and with Allah is success: as for his narrating from Abd Allah and from his brother Ubayd Allah, it is possible he narrated it from both. And as for the narration of Ali ibn Mujahid and Salamah ibn al-Fadl and their addition of Muhammad ibn Talhah, it does not affect, for in the narration of the Imam Ahmad from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban narrated to me. And Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakkai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban narrated to me."
"3191","229 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated: Jarir - meaning Ibn Hazim - narrated: from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn Hanzalah (Ghasil al-Malaikah) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dirham of riba that a man consumes while he knows is worse than thirty-six acts of adultery."
"3192","230 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ubayd ibn Ghannam al-Kufi narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated: from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dirham of riba that a man consumes while he knows is worse before Allah than thirty-six acts of adultery. Abu al-Qasim Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated this hadith from Hashim ibn al-Harith al-Marwazi, from Ubaydullah ibn Amr, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn Hanzalah, and he said: Jarir ibn Hazim and Ubaydullah ibn Amr both narrated this hadith from Layth, together from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn Hanzalah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and both in my view are mistaken."
"3193","Musnad of Abdullah ibn Hawalah al-Azdi, Abu Hawalah, may Allah be pleased with him. 231 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated. 232 - al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi narrated to us: Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to me: from Bujayr ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abu Qutaylah, from Ibn Hawalah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Matters will come to you being organized troops: a troop in al-Sham, a troop in Yemen, and a troop in Iraq. Ibn Hawalah said: Choose for me, O Messenger of Allah, if I live to see that. He said: Upon you is al-Sham, for it is Allah's best choice from His land; He gathers to it His best chosen servants. If you refuse, then upon you is your Yemen, and drink from your ponds, for Allah Almighty has guaranteed al-Sham and its people for me. Abu Qutaylah's name is Marthad ibn Wadaah al-Jufi al-Himsi. Abu Idris al-Khawlani narrated it from Abdullah."
"3194","233 - Abu al-Majd al-Fadl ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim ibn Sulayman ibn al-Baniyasi al-Muaddal informed us - in Damascus - that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad and Abu al-Hasan Ali, the two sons of al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Mawazini, informed them. 234 - And Abu Talib al-Khadir ibn Hibatullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Tawus informed us - in Damascus, read to him in Damascus - it was said to him: al-Sharif al-Nasib Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ibrahim, that is Ibn al-Abbas al-Husayni, and Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai, and Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Tahir ibn Jafar al-Sulami informed you - read to them - they said: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yahya ibn Salwan al-Mazini informed us, he said: Abu al-Qasim al-Fadl ibn Jafar al-Tamimi al-Muadhhin informed us: Abu Bakr Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Faraj ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Hashimi informed us: Abu Mushir Abd al-Ala ibn Mushir al-Ghassani narrated: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abdullah ibn Hawalah al-Azdi, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You will be organized as troops: a troop in al-Sham, a troop in Iraq, and a troop in Yemen. Al-Hawali said: Choose for me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Upon you is al-Sham; whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from his ponds, for Allah has guaranteed al-Sham and its people for me. Whenever Abu Idris al-Khawlani narrated this hadith, he would turn to Ibn Amir and say: Whoever Allah guarantees, there is no loss upon him. Salman ibn Sumayr narrated it from Ibn Hawalah."
"3195","235 - Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated to me: Issam ibn Khalid and Ali ibn Ayyash narrated: Hariz narrated: from Sulayman ibn Sumayr, from Ibn Hawalah - and he was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There will be organized troops: Sham, Yemen, and Iraq, and Allah knows best with which he began; and upon you is al-Sham, verily upon you is al-Sham, verily upon you is al-Sham; whoever dislikes it, then upon him is his Yemen, and let him drink from his ponds, for Allah Almighty has entrusted al-Sham and its people to me."
"3196","236 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us: Fatimah informed them: Ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated: Salman ibn Sumayr narrated: from Abdullah ibn Hawalah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There will be troops: a troop in al-Sham, a troop in Yemen, and a troop in Iraq, and Allah knows best with which he began; so upon you is al-Sham - three times - whoever dislikes it, then upon him is his Yemen, let him drink from his ponds, for Allah has guaranteed al-Sham and its people for me. And Busr ibn Ubaydullah narrated it from Ibn Hawalah."
"3197","237 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us: Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated: Zayd ibn Waqid narrated: from Busr ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibn Hawalah al-Azdi: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be organized troops: a troop in Yemen, Sham, and Iraq. I said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. He said: Upon you is al-Sham; whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from the ponds of Yemen, for Allah has guaranteed al-Sham and its people for me. Imam Ahmad and Abu Dawud narrated it from Haywah ibn Shurayh. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Makhul - in Beirut - from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazyad, from his father, from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Makhul, from Abu Idris."
"3198","Another: 238 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim and Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Mihrabazd informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated: Ibn Wahb narrated: Muawiyah narrated to me: from Damrah ibn Habib, from Ibn Zughb al-Iyadi who said: Ibn Hawalah al-Azdi (a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) stayed with me, and I heard him narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: We were sent around Madinah to take spoils, and we returned having taken nothing. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the hardship that had befallen us, he said: O Allah, do not entrust them to me lest I be too weak for them, nor entrust them to people lest they be deemed insignificant by them, nor entrust them to themselves lest they be incapable of it, but rather take charge of their provision Yourself. Then he said: Al-Sham will surely be opened for you, and the treasures of Persia and Rome will surely be divided, and one of you will come to have so much and so much wealth, until one of you will be given a hundred dinars and be displeased with it. He said: Then he placed his hand on my head and said: O Ibn Hawalah, when you see the caliphate descend upon the Holy Land, then earthquakes and killing have drawn near, and the Hour is closer to people than this hand of mine is to your head."
"3199","239 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush al-Harimi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated: Muawiyah narrated: from Damrah ibn Habib, that Ibn Zughb al-Iyadi narrated to him, he said: Abdullah ibn Hawalah al-Azdi stayed with me and said to me - while he was staying with me in my house: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on foot around Madinah to take spoils, and we returned having taken nothing, and he recognized hardship on our faces, so he stood among us and said: O Allah, do not entrust them to me lest I be weak, nor entrust them to themselves lest they be incapable of it, nor entrust them to people lest they prefer themselves over them. Then he said: Al-Sham, Rome, and Persia - or Rome and Persia - will surely be opened for you, until one of you will have so many camels, so many cattle, and so many sheep, until one of them will be given a hundred dinars and be displeased with it. Then he placed his hand on my head - or on my crown - and said: O Ibn Hawalah, when you see the caliphate descend upon the Holy Land, then earthquakes, calamities, and grave matters have drawn near, and the Hour on that day is closer to people than this hand of mine is to your head. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Salih, from Asad ibn Musa, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, similarly."
"3200","Another, containing part of the two previous hadiths. 240 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated. al-Tabarani said: And Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from his father: Nasr ibn Alqamah narrated to me, tracing the hadith back to Jubayr ibn Nufayr, he said: Ibn Hawalah said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we complained to him of poverty, nakedness, and lack of means, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rejoice, for by Allah, I fear abundance of means for you more than I fear its scarcity for you. By Allah, this matter will remain among you until He opens for you a troop in al-Sham, a troop in Iraq, and a troop in Yemen, and until a man will be given a hundred and be displeased with it. Abdullah ibn Hawalah said: And when will Sham be able to stand against Rome with horns? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will surely open it for you and make you successors in it, until a group among them - white their shirts, shaven their napes - will stand over the little black man among you; whatever they command them, they do it. And today there are men among them in whose eyes you are more contemptible than ticks on camels' behinds. Abdullah ibn Hawalah said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me if I live to see that. He said: I choose al-Sham for you, for it is Allah's choicest part of His lands, and to it He gathers His choicest servants. O people of Yemen, upon you is al-Sham, for Allah's choicest part of the earth is al-Sham; whoever refuses, let him drink from the ponds of Yemen, for Allah Almighty has guaranteed al-Sham for me."
"3201","Another: 241 - Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Khalid ibn Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Khalid informed them: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated: Isa ibn Hammad narrated: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated: from Yazid, that is Ibn Abi Habib, from Rabiah ibn Laqit al-Tujibi, from Ibn Hawalah al-Asadi, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever is saved from three has been saved, whoever is saved from three has been saved. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what? He said: My death, and from the killing of a caliph who perseveres upon the truth, giving it its due, and the Dajjal."
"3202","242 - Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr al-Harimi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Hajjaj narrated: Layth narrated: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me: from Rabiah ibn Laqit al-Tujibi, from Abdullah ibn Hawalah al-Azdi, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever is saved from three has been saved. They said: What, O Messenger of Allah? He said: My death, and from the killing of a caliph who perseveres upon the truth, giving it its due, and the Dajjal."
"3203","243 - And with it my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me: from Rabiah ibn Laqit, from Abdullah ibn Hawalah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is saved from three has been saved - three times - my death, the Dajjal, and the killing of a caliph who perseveres upon the truth, giving it its due."
"3204","Another: 244 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isfahani informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Said al-Jurayri, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abdullah ibn Hawalah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was under a lote tree enrolling people. He raised his head to me and said: O Abdullah ibn Hawalah, shall I enroll you? I said: Whatever Allah and His Messenger choose for me. He kept dictating and raising his head to me, saying: O Abdullah ibn Hawalah, shall I enroll you? I said: Whatever Allah and His Messenger choose for me. Then I saw in the register Abu Bakr and Umar, so I knew they would only be enrolled in something good, so I said: Yes, so he enrolled me. Then he said: O Abdullah ibn Hawalah, what will you do during a tribulation that will be in the regions of the earth as if it were the horns of cows, and the one after it in which there is like the leap of a rabbit? I said: Whatever Allah and His Messenger choose for me. He said: Follow this one, for he and whoever follows him are upon the truth. So I caught up with the man, took him by his shoulders and turned him around, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, this one? He said: Yes, and behold it was Uthman ibn Affan."
"3205","245 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated: Yazid ibn Harun narrated: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated: from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Hawalah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he said: O Ibn Hawalah, how will you be when you witness a tribulation raging in the regions of the earth as if it were the horns of cows? I said: What do you command me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon you is al-Sham."
"3206","246 - And from Ibn Hawalah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we stopped at a resting place in the shade of a lote tree. I went out for a need of mine, then I came back while there was a scribe with him writing. When he saw me he said: Shall I enroll you, O Ibn Hawalah? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he turned to the scribe, and I drew near until I stood over them, and I looked and behold in the register were Abu Bakr and Umar, so I thought they would only be enrolled in something good. He said: Shall we enroll you, O Ibn Hawalah? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah."
"3207","247 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated: al-Jurayri narrated: from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Hawalah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting in the shade of a lote tree, with a scribe dictating to him. He said: Shall I not enroll you, O Ibn Hawalah? I said: I do not know; whatever Allah and His Messenger choose. So he turned away from me. And Ismail once said in the first: Shall we enroll you, O Ibn Hawalah? I said: For what, O Messenger of Allah? So he turned away from me and bent over his scribe dictating to him. Then he said: Shall we enroll you, O Ibn Hawalah? I said: I do not know; whatever Allah and His Messenger choose for me. So he turned away from me and bent over his scribe dictating to him. He said: So I looked and behold in the register was Umar, so I knew Umar would only be enrolled in something good. Then he said: Shall we enroll you, O Ibn Hawalah? I said: Yes. Then he said: O Ibn Hawalah, what will you do during a tribulation emerging in the outskirts of the earth as if it were the horns of cows? I said: I do not know; whatever Allah and His Messenger choose for me. He said: Then what will you do during another emerging after it, as if the first compared to it were the swelling of a rabbit? I said: I do not know; whatever Allah and His Messenger choose for me. He said: Follow this one. He said: And a man with his back turned at that moment. He said: So I went and hastened and took him by his shoulders, and I brought his face toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This one? He said: Yes, and behold it was Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun, from Kahmas, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq: A man from Anazah called Zaidah or Mazyadah ibn Hawalah narrated to me, and he mentioned something like the hadith of Yazid ibn Harun from Kahmas. And Idris ibn Jafar: we included him for corroboration. So it is possible - and Allah knows best - that Abdullah ibn Hawalah's name was Zaidah or Mazyadah, then changed to Abdullah."
"3208","Musnad of Abdullah ibn Khubayb al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him. 248 - Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me: al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated: from Asid ibn Abi Asid, from Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, from his father who said: We were struck by drizzle and darkness, so we waited for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pray for us. He came out, took my hand, and said: Say. I fell silent. He said: Say. I said: What shall I say? He said: Say He is Allah, the One, and the two Muawwidhatayn, when you enter evening and when you enter morning, three times; they will suffice you every day, twice."
"3209","249 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Abu al-Mahasin Asad ibn Ziyad informed them: Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us: Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah al-Sarakhsi informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Khuraym al-Shashi informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd ibn Humayd ibn Nasr narrated: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated: from Abu Said al-Barrad, from Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, from his father who said: We went out on a rainy, dark, intensely severe night, and I sought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pray for us. He said: So I found him, and he said: Say. I said nothing. Then he said: Say. I said nothing. He said: Say. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall I say? He said: Say He is Allah, the One, and the two Muawwidhatayn, when you enter evening and morning, three times; they will suffice you against everything."
"3210","250 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated: from Abu Asid, from Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Hubayb, from his father who said: We went out on a night of rain and intense darkness seeking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pray for us. He said: So I found him, and he said: Say. I said nothing. Then he said: Say. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall I say? He said: Say He is Allah, the One, and the two Muawwidhatayn, when you enter evening and when you enter morning, three times; they will suffice you. Abu Dawud included it from Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa, from Ibn Abi Fudayk, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Abu Asid al-Barrad. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd ibn Humayd and said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith from this route. And Abu Said al-Barrad is Asid ibn Abi Asid. And al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Ali, from Abu Asim, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Asid ibn Abi Asid, from Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, from his father. And from Yunus, from Ibn Wahb, from Hafs ibn Maysarah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, from his father, similarly."
"3211","Abdullah ibn Rabiah al-Sulami, may Allah be pleased with him. 251 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us - at al-Harbiyyah - that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Waki narrated: Shubah narrated: from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abdullah ibn Rabiah al-Sulami who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and heard a muadhdhin saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will find him a shepherd or one away from his family. When he descended into the valley he said: He passed by a discarded kid, and said: Do you see this as insignificant to its owners? The world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to its owners."
"3212","252 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - in Isfahan - that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated: Shubah narrated: from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abdullah ibn Rabiah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and heard the voice of a man calling the adhan, so he began answering him with the like of his adhan until he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is surely a shepherd or one away from his family. He said: So we descended into the valley, and behold it was a dead sheep. He said: Do you see this as insignificant to its owners? They said: Yes. He said: The world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to its owners. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Shubah. And he narrated it in the book of the deeds of day and night from Ismail ibn Masud, from Yazid ibn Zuray, from Shubah similarly. The mention of the kid has a corroboration in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, similarly."
"3213","Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah, whose name is Amr ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Makhzum al-Qurashi, may Allah be pleased with him. 253 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isfahani informed us - there - that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated: my father narrated to me. 254 - al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated: they both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed thirty thousand from us. Then wealth came to him, so he gave me and said: May Allah bless you in your family and wealth; the reward of a loan is only praise and repayment."
"3214","255 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari and Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Makhzumi narrated: from his father, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a dozen or so thousand from him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned on the day of Hunayn and wealth came to him, he called for Ibn Abi Rabiah and said: Take what you lent; may Allah bless you in your wealth and children; the reward of a loan is only repayment and praise."
"3215","256 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Waki narrated: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah al-Makhzumi narrated: from his father, from his grandfather: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed thirty or forty thousand from him when he raided Hunayn. When he returned he repaid him, then said: May Allah bless you in your family and wealth; the reward of a loan is only repayment and praise. Al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Waki, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdullah. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim mentioned Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah al-Makhzumi, who narrated from his father; al-Thawri and Hatim ibn Ismail narrated from him. I heard my father and Abu Zurah saying that. And he said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah al-Makhzumi narrated from his father from his grandfather: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed thirty or forty thousand from him when he raided Hunayn; Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated from him."
"3216","Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam al-Asadi, Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. Zuraah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 257 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Isfahani informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated: al-Ala ibn Salih narrated: Zuraah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr saying: Aligning the feet and placing the hand upon the hand in prayer is from the Sunnah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Nasr ibn Ali, from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri."
"3217","Sulayman ibn Atiq from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 258 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr ibn Muhammad - in Cairo - informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated: Sahl ibn Ubayd al-Tustari narrated: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated: from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Sulayman ibn Atiq: he heard Ibn al-Zubayr saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques."
"3218","Tawus ibn Kaysan from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 259 - Abu Jafar and Fatimah informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Musa ibn Harun narrated: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated. 260 - al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Harawi narrated: al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated: from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever draws his sword then lays it down, his blood is wasted - meaning by laying it down: striking with it."
"3219","261 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us - more than once - that Hibatullah ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Tabari informed them: Ibrahim ibn Umar al-Barmaki informed us: Abu Umar Muhammad ibn al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Dawud narrated: Muhammad ibn Adam al-Marwazi narrated: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated: Mamar informed us: from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever draws his sword then lays it down, his blood is wasted. Abu Bakr said: This is a practice unique to the people of Yemen. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh."
"3220","Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr from his father. 262 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Harun ibn Maruf narrated. Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Harun: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Abdullah ibn al-Aswad al-Qurashi narrated to me: from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Proclaim marriage."
"3221","263 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated: my father narrated to me: Ibn Wahb narrated: Abdullah ibn al-Aswad narrated: from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Proclaim marriage."
"3222","Another: 264 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Isfahani informed us - there - that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated: Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated: from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father who said: Abu Bakr's name was Abdullah ibn Uthman, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Atiq, freed from the Fire."
"3223","265 - My maternal uncle, Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on them - informed us that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad - known as Ibn al-Batti - informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Qasim ibn Bishr al-Narsi informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafii informed us: Junayd ibn Hakim narrated: Hamid ibn Yahya narrated: from Sufyan, from Ibn Ajlan and Ziyad ibn Sad - or one of them - from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father who said: Abu Bakr's name was Abdullah ibn Uthman, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You are Allah's freed one from the Fire, so he was named Atiq. Junayd ibn Hakim: al-Daraqutni said: He is not strong; so he is a corroboration for others."
"3224","Another: 266 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Musa ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated: Musa ibn Ismail narrated: Hunayd ibn al-Qasim narrated. 267 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Durran ibn Sufyan al-Qattan al-Basri narrated: Musa ibn Ismail narrated: al-Hunayd ibn al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Maiz narrated, he said: I heard Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrating that his father narrated to him that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was being cupped. When he finished he said: O Abdullah, take this blood and spill it where no one sees you. When I went out from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I deliberately took the blood and drank it. When I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: What did you do, O Abdullah? He said: I placed it in a spot I thought hidden from people. He said: Perhaps you drank it? I said: Yes. He said: And who commanded you to drink blood? Woe to you from people, and woe to people from you. The wording of Durran. And in the narration of Musa: When he went out from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he deliberately took the blood and drank it. When he returned he said: O Abdullah, what did you do? He said: I placed it in the most hidden place I knew, hidden from people. He said: Perhaps you drank it? He said: Yes. And he said: Why did you drink blood? Woe to people from you and woe to you from people. And he added: Abu Salamah said: So I narrated it to Abu Asim, and he said: They used to view that the strength in him was from that blood."
"3225","Amir ibn Sharahil al-Shabi from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 268 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isfahani informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated: Muhammad ibn Fudayl and Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated: from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Amir al-Shabi who said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr while circumambulating the Kaaba saying: By the Lord of this edifice, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) surely cursed al-Hakam and his offspring."
"3226","269 - And with it, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated: Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated: from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr that he said while on the pulpit: By the Lord of this Sacred House and the Sacred Land, al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As and his children are cursed upon the tongue of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3227","270 - Abu Ali Umar al-Waiz informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Razzaq narrated: Ibn Uyaynah informed us: from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi who said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr while leaning against the Kaaba saying: By the Lord of this Kaaba, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) surely cursed so-and-so and his offspring from his loins."
"3228","Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr from his father. 271 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid al-Basri narrated: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated: my father narrated. 272 - al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Zuhayr Abu Yala al-Ubulli narrated to us: Abdah ibn Abdullah al-Saffar narrated: Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated: Ibn Ishaq narrated: Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to me: from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: Quraysh had mourned their slain, then regretted and said: Do not wail over them lest that reach Muhammad and his Companions and they rejoice at your calamity. Among the captives was Abu Wadaah ibn Subayrah al-Sahmi. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has in Makkah a merchant son, clever, wealthy; as if you see him coming to you for his father's ransom. When Quraysh spoke about ransom as they spoke, al-Muttalib said: You have spoken truthfully; by Allah, if you do, he will press you hard. Then he slipped away by night, came to Madinah, and ransomed his father for four thousand dirhams. Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakkai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father, mursal, without mentioning Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr."
"3229","Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Mulaykah from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 273 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani narrated: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated: from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr: that Ali mentioned the daughter of Abu Jahl, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3230","274 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated: Ahmad ibn Mani narrated: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated: from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that Ali mentioned the daughter of Abu Jahl, and that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Fatimah is only a part of me; what harms her harms me, and what wearies her wearies me."
"3231","275 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated: Ayyub informed us: from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr: that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, mentioned the daughter of Abu Jahl, and it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Fatimah is only a part of me; what harms her harms me, and what wearies her wearies me. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani and said: A hasan sahih hadith. Thus Ayyub said, while more than one said: from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah; and it is possible Ibn Mulaykah narrated it from both together. I say: al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah."
"3232","Abd al-Aziz ibn Asid al-Tahi from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 276 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr and Ahmad al-Dawraqi narrated: they both said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated: Said ibn Yazid informed us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Asid narrated, he said: I heard a man saying to Ibn al-Zubayr: Give us a fatwa about jar nabidh. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade jar nabidh."
"3233","277 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isfahani informed us: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - read to him while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah Sammuyah informed us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated: Ghassan ibn Mudar al-Azdi narrated: Abu Maslamah Said ibn Yazid narrated: from Abd al-Aziz ibn Asid al-Tahi, who said: I witnessed a man stand to Ibn al-Zubayr while he was preaching and say: O Commander of the Faithful, give us a fatwa about jar nabidh. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding it."
"3234","278 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated: Shubah narrated: from Abu Maslamah, that he heard Abd al-Aziz ibn Asid saying: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr, when a man asked him about jar nabidh, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade jar nabidh. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Ismail ibn Ibrahim. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Shubah. It has a corroboration in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Said ibn Jubayr, from Abdullah ibn Umar and Abdullah ibn Abbas, and from the narration of Tawus and Uqbah ibn Hurayth, from Ibn Umar."
"3235","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 279 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Saiqah narrated: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated: Abu Awanah narrated: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one consulted is trusted. And I think Abd al-Malik did not hear it from Ibn al-Zubayr, by evidence of what."
"3236","280 - Fatimah bint Abi al-Fayiz ibn Muhammad ibn al-Tuwayr informed us - in Baghdad - that Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us - by ijazah: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Lulu al-Warraq informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad - that is al-Utaridi - narrated: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated: Abu Awanah narrated: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one consulted is trusted."
"3237","Ubaydah ibn Amr al-Salmani from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 281 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz informed us - at al-Harbiyyah - that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated: Shubah narrated: from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that a man swore by Allah besides whom there is no god, falsely, and he was forgiven. Shubah said: Because of tawhid."
"3238","282 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated: Shubah narrated: from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ubaydah, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that a man swore by Allah besides whom there is no god, falsely, and he was forgiven."
"3239","283 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: Imam Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sad al-Baghdadi informed them: Asim ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi al-Farisi informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Makhlad ibn Hafs al-Duri al-Attar informed us: Abbas ibn Yazid narrated: Khalid ibn al-Harith and Ghundar narrated: they both said: Shubah narrated: from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ubaydah, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man swore by Allah besides whom there is no god, falsely, and he was forgiven. Shubah said: Because of tawhid. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hakam, from Muhammad ibn Jafar Ghundar, similarly. Abu al-Bakhtari's name is Said ibn Fayruz."
"3240","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from his brother Abdullah. 284 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated: Umar ibn Ali narrated: from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: This verse was revealed concerning the Negus: And when they hear what was revealed to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears."
"3241","285 - Shaykh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated: Ismail ibn Ishaq narrated: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated. 286 - Ibn Mardawayh said: And Yaqub ibn Shadhah narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated: they both said: Umar ibn Ali ibn Muqaddam narrated, he said: I heard Hisham ibn Urwah narrating from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: This verse was revealed concerning the Negus and his companions: And when they hear what was revealed to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears. Al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Ali, from Umar ibn Ali ibn Muqaddam."
"3242","Another: 287 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Said narrated: from Hisham: my father informed me: from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling and two sucklings do not prohibit through breastfeeding."
"3243","288 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Ibrahim al-Sami narrated: Wuhayb narrated: from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling and not two sucklings prohibit through breastfeeding."
"3244","289 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me: from Urwah, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, that he narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: One suckling through breastfeeding does not prohibit, nor two sucklings."
"3245","290 - And with it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated: from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling does not prohibit, nor two sucklings. Al-Nasai narrated it from Shuayb ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Said. And from Ziyad ibn Ayyub, from Ibn Ulayyah, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah similarly. Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3246","Another: 291 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us - by ijazah if not by hearing - that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Said narrated: from Hisham who said: My father informed me: from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha, he would bow four rakahs and pray witr with one prostration, then sleep until he prayed his night prayer."
"3247","Another: 292 - Imam Abu Yala Hamzah and Muhammad, the two sons of Ali ibn Hamzah al-Harraniyan, informed us - in Baghdad - that Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Sallal informed them: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah informed us: Umar ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Shii narrated: Humayd - meaning Ibn Masadah - narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated: from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has a disciple, and al-Zubayr is my disciple and my maternal aunt's son."
"3248","293 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isfahani informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Qada al-Jawhari narrated: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has a disciple, and al-Zubayr is my disciple from my ummah."
"3249","294 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, while present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj and Ibn Hisab narrated: they both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr, my maternal aunt's son. It has a corroboration in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"3250","Another: 295 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - in Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them - while present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Khallad ibn Aslam narrated: Hanifah ibn Marzuq narrated: Sharik narrated: from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr who said: And who would eat the crow when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named it a little vicious creature? By Allah, it is not wholesome."
"3251","296 - Abu Jafar also informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated: Khallad ibn Aslam narrated: Hanifah ibn Marzuq narrated: Sharik narrated: from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: Who would eat the crow when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named it vicious."
"3252","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 297 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yunus narrated: Hammad - meaning Ibn Zayd - narrated: Habib al-Muallim narrated: from Ata, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques except the Sacred Mosque, and a prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a hundred prayers in this one. Thus in the narration of Yunus: better than a hundred prayers."
"3253","298 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Arim narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: from Habib al-Muallim, from Ata who said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in others except the Sacred Mosque, and a prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a prayer in my mosque by a thousand prayers. It has a corroboration in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A prayer in the Prophet's mosque (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is better than a thousand prayers in others except the Sacred Mosque. And in Muslim also from the hadith of Nafi, from Ibn Umar. And in the hadith of Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayrah, they both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better - and in the narration of Ibn Umar: superior - to a thousand prayers in others except the Sacred Mosque. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab, from Hammad ibn Zayd."
"3254","Another: 299 - Abu Jafar informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah - in Cairo - that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated: Jafar ibn Mihran al-Sabbak narrated: Abd al-Warith narrated: from Habib al-Muallim, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas and Ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An umrah in Ramadan equals a hajj. Muslim narrated it from Ahmad ibn Abdah, from Yazid ibn Zuray, from Habib al-Muallim, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas alone, without mentioning Ibn al-Zubayr."
"3255","Imran al-Sulami Abu al-Hakam from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 300 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated: Shubah narrated: from Salamah ibn Kuhayl who said: I heard Abu al-Hakam saying: I asked Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade earthen jars and gourds."
"3256","301 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Abu Hudhayfah narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Imran al-Sulami who said: I came to Ibn al-Zubayr and asked him about nabidh. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade jar nabidh and gourds."
"3257","302 - And with it, al-Tabarani informed us: Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi narrated: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated: Shubah narrated: from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Hakam al-Sulami who said: I asked Ibn al-Zubayr, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade jars and gourds."
"3258","Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 303 - And with it, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar narrated: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated: al-Fadl ibn Sulayman narrated: Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya narrated, he said: I saw Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, and he saw a man raising his hands before finishing his prayer. When he finished it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands until he finished his prayer."
"3259","Muslim ibn Jundub al-Hudhali al-Qass from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 304 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrami narrated: Abu Qatan narrated: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated: from Muslim ibn Jundub, from Ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Jumuah with us, and we would race for the shade. In the two Sahihs from the hadith of Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa, from his father who said: We used to pray Jumuah with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then depart while the walls had no shade to shade ourselves with."
"3260","Nafi ibn Thabit ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam al-Asadi Abu Abdullah from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 305 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harimi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated: Nafi ibn Thabit informed me: from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha, he would bow four rakahs and pray witr with one prostration, then sleep until he prayed afterwards his night prayer."
"3261","306 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Isfahani narrated: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Saiqah narrated: Mansur ibn Salamah al-Khuzai narrated: Ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated: Nafi ibn Thabit informed me: from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha, he would bow four rakahs and pray witr with one prostration, then sleep until he prayed afterwards his night prayer."
"3262","Another: 307 - Abu Jafar - in Isfahan - and Fatimah - in Cairo - informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Ibrahim ibn Saduq Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated: Abdullah ibn Nafi ibn Thabit narrated: from his brother, from his father Nafi ibn Thabit ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two or three times. Its chain is hasan, except that Abdullah ibn Nafi did not name his brother. And Ali ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari narrated it without mentioning from his brother."
"3263","308 - al-Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Silafi informed us - by ijazah - that Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Hind al-Kindi - at the Salamās frontier - informed them: my grandfather, Qadi Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Hariz ibn Salamasi, informed us: my father Hariz ibn Ahmad narrated to me: Abu Said Imran ibn Musa - that is Ibn Hilal - narrated: Ali - that is Ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari - narrated: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated: Abdullah ibn Nafi ibn Thabit ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam narrated: from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: I pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twice in one day. In this narration the narrator from Ibn al-Zubayr is Thabit his son, not Nafi; and Allah knows best what is correct."
"3264","Nusayr ibn Dhuluq Abu Tumah from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 309 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated: from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Nusayr ibn Dhuluq: that Ibn al-Zubayr saw people wiping the Maqam and forbade them, saying: You were not commanded to wipe; you were only commanded to pray."
"3265","310 - And with it, al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated: from Sharik, from Nusayr ibn Duluq who said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr circumambulating the House wearing a burtulah. We intended thereby his seeing Ibn al-Zubayr."
"3266","Wahb ibn Kaysan, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 311 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz informed us - at al-Harbiyyah - that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Ibn Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated: my father narrated: from Ibn Ishaq who said: Wahb ibn Kaysan - freedman of the family of al-Zubayr - narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr on the day of Eid saying, when he prayed before the sermon then stood addressing people: O people, thus is Allah's practice and the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3267","312 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated: Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami narrated: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated: from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, who said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr led us in prayer on a day of Eid, then preached after the prayer, then said: Every practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so-and-so changed, even the prayer."
"3268","Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr from his grandfather. 313 - Abu al-Fath Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi and Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Yanal al-Sufi informed us - in writing - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar al-Dinawari informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sunni informed us: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai narrated: al-Harith ibn Miskin said: read to him while I listened: from Ibn Wahb: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me: from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his grandfather that he used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned to al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam in the year of Khaybar four shares: a share for al-Zubayr, a share for the near kin for Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib, mother of al-Zubayr, and two shares for the horse."
"3269","314 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, she said: Ibn Ridhah informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Qadi Waki narrated: Abdullah ibn Shayb al-Madani narrated: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated: Ibn Wahb narrated: from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Junahi, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned to al-Zubayr in the year of Khaybar four shares: a share for al-Zubayr, a share for the near kin, a share for his mother, and a share for his horse. In this hadith there is a discrepancy with what al-Nasai narrated, and as if what he narrated is more deserving; and Allah knows best. Abdullah ibn Shayb - I think the discrepancy is from him, and I view him as the one spoken about; and Allah knows best."
"3270","Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 315 - Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us - in Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Yazid narrated: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us: from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: When: Indeed you will die and indeed they will die, then indeed you on the Day of Resurrection before your Lord will dispute, was revealed, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, will what was between us in the world be repeated upon us along with particular sins? He said: Yes, it will surely be repeated upon you until every rightful one is given his right. Al-Zubayr said: By Allah, the matter is surely grave."
"3271","316 - And with it, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated: from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"3272","317 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated: Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Hatib narrated: from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: When: Indeed you will die and indeed they will die, then indeed you on the Day of Resurrection before your Lord will dispute, was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-Zubayr said: Will what was between us in the world be repeated upon us? He said: Yes, that will surely be repeated upon you until every rightful one is given his right. Al-Zubayr said: By Allah, the matter is surely grave. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abdullah ibn Numayr and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Muhammad ibn Umar, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr. And al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned a group who narrated it from the musnad of al-Zubayr, saying: Abdah ibn Sulayman and Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya, from Ibn al-Zubayr. He said: And the word is the word of whoever traced it from Ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr; and Allah knows best. And it already preceded in the musnad of al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3273","Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. 318 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said and Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Harbiyan informed us - at al-Harbiyyah - that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Jarir narrated: from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: A man from Khatham came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father embraced Islam while an old man unable to mount the camel, while hajj is prescribed upon him; shall I perform hajj on his behalf? He said: Are you his eldest child? He said: Yes. He said: Tell me, if your father had a debt and you settled it on his behalf, would that suffice for him? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform hajj on his behalf."
"3274","319 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: al-Qawariri narrated: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated: from Mansur, from Yusuf, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father is an old man whom Islam reached while unable to stay on the camel. He said: Are you his eldest child? He said: Yes. Tell me, if your father had a debt and you settled it, would it suffice him? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform hajj on behalf of your father. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Mansur with its chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: You are your father's eldest child, so perform hajj on his behalf. And Ahmad ibn Mani narrated it from... And al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Jarir - that is Yaqub ibn Ibrahim - from Abdullah, from Sufyan, from Mansur, like the narration of Imam Ahmad from Abd al-Rahman, abridged. It has a corroboration in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas: concerning the woman who asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a fatwa, and he commanded her to perform hajj on behalf of her father."
"3275","Another: 320 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated: Jarir narrated: from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr who said: Zamah had a slave girl he used to have intercourse with, and she was suspected of another man having relations with her. Zamah died while she was pregnant, and she gave birth to a boy resembling the man she was suspected with. Sawdah mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: As for inheritance, it is his; but as for you, veil yourself from him, for he is not your brother."
"3276","321 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki narrated: my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Adam narrated: Qays and Mufaddal ibn Muhalhal narrated: from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Yusuf who said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he assigned him the inheritance because he was born on Zamah's bed, and said to Sawdah: As for you, veil yourself from him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn al-Zubayr, without mentioning Yusuf. And likewise al-Tabarani narrated it from al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq. And al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Jarir with its chain as Zuhayr narrated it. It has a corroboration in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Urwah, from Aishah: Sad ibn Abi Waqqas and Abd ibn Zamah disputed concerning the son of Zamah's slave girl. He said: This is my brother's son; he entrusted him to me... the hadith."
"3277","Abdullah ibn Zamah ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy al-Asadi, may Allah be pleased with him. 322 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz informed us - at al-Harbiyyah - that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yaqub narrated: my father narrated: from Ibn Ishaq who said: And Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me: from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zamah ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad."
"3278","323 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: al-Zuhri narrated to me: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me: from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zamah ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad."
"3279","324 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Ahmad, known as Ibn al-Saffar, informed us (in Nishapur) that Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, he said: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Hamdun al-Tajir informed us: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi narrated: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Faris al-Dhuhli narrated: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufayli narrated: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri who said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me: from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zamah ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, while I was with him among a group of Muslims, Bilal called him to prayer. He said: Command Abu Bakr to lead people in prayer. He said: So I went out and found Umar among the people, while Abu Bakr was absent. I said: Stand, O Umar, and lead people in prayer. So he stood, and when Umar said the takbir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard his voice - and Umar was a loud-voiced man - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then where is Abu Bakr? Allah and the Muslims refuse that; Allah and the Muslims refuse that. So he sent for Abu Bakr, and he came after Umar had prayed that prayer, and he led people in prayer. Abdullah ibn Zamah said: Umar said to me: Woe to you, what did you do, O Ibn Zamah? By Allah, I only thought when you commanded me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had commanded you with that; had it not been for that I would not have led people in prayer. He said: I said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not command me with that, but when I did not see Abu Bakr, I saw you as the most deserving of those present among people to lead the prayer. The wording of Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli. And in the narration of Abu Shuayb al-Harrani: Bilal called to prayer, and he said: Command whoever will lead people in prayer, so I went out. And with him: And Umar was a loud-voiced man. And with him: Allah and the Muslims refuse that, without repetition. And with him: What did you do to me, O Ibn Zamah. And with him: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not command me; but when I did not see Abu Bakr, I saw you as the most deserving of those present to lead people in prayer. And in the narration of Imam Ahmad from Yaqub, he said: Bilal called for prayer, and he said: Command whoever will lead people in prayer, while Abu Bakr was absent; so he said: Stand, O Umar, and lead people in prayer. He said: So he stood. And with him: What did you do to me, O Ibn Zamah. And with him: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not command me, but when I did not see Abu Bakr, I saw you as the most deserving of those present to lead the prayer. The rest is the same. And with him: Allah and the Muslims refuse that; Allah and the Muslims refuse that. Abu Dawud narrated it in al-Sunnah from Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufayli similarly. And from Ahmad ibn Salih, from Ibn Abi Fudayk, from Musa ibn Yaqub al-Zamai, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, that Abdullah ibn Zamah informed him."
"3280","Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim ibn Amr ibn Awf ibn Mabdhul ibn Amr ibn Ghanm ibn Mazin ibn al-Najjar al-Ansari al-Mazini Abu Muhammad, may Allah be pleased with him. 325 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated: Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi narrated: from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for rain while wearing a black khamisah of his. He wanted to take its lower part and make it its upper, but it was heavy upon him, so he turned it over upon him: the right upon the left and the left upon the right."
"3281","326 - And with it my father narrated to me: Ali ibn Bahr narrated: al-Darawardi narrated: from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the prayer ground seeking rain while wearing a black khamisah. He took its lower part to make it its upper, but it was heavy upon him, so he turned it over."
"3282","327 - And with it my father narrated to me: Yaqub narrated: my father narrated: from Ibn Ishaq: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me: from Abbad ibn Tamim al-Ansari then al-Mazini, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim - and he was one of his tribe - and Abdullah ibn Zayd was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had witnessed Uhud with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he sought rain for us; he prolonged supplication and increased asking. He said: Then he turned toward the qiblah and turned his cloak, flipping it back to front, and people turned with him."
"3283","328 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated: Abu al-Walid narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated: from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought rain while wearing a black khamisah. He wanted to take it by its lower part and make it its upper, but it was heavy upon him, so he turned it over upon his shoulders."
"3284","329 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn al-Fudayl al-Fudayli informed them: Abu Mudar Muhallim ibn Ismail al-Dabbi informed us: Qadi Abu Said al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi narrated: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi informed us: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated: Abd al-Aziz narrated: from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought rain while wearing a black khamisah of his. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to take its lower part and make it its upper; when it was heavy upon him, he turned it over upon his shoulders. Abu Dawud and al-Nasai both narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Said. And Abu Dawud and Abu Awanah Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated from Muhammad ibn Awf who said: I read in the book of Amr ibn al-Harith - meaning al-Himsi - from Abdullah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, and he mentioned: And he turned his cloak, placing its right side upon his left shoulder and its left side upon his right shoulder, then supplicated Allah Almighty. And Abu Awanah al-Isfarayini narrated it in his Sahih from Ismail al-Qadi, from Ibrahim ibn Hamzah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad concerning the black khamisah, and in it: And he turned his cloak; and in one narration: And he flipped his cloak. The two Sahihs mentioned seeking rain, but in what we mentioned is what they did not mention: there is no black khamisah nor the manner of turning; and Allah knows best."
"3285","Another: 330 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated: al-Mualla narrated: Abu Uways narrated, he said: from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle - and he had witnessed Badr - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave girl commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, sell her even for a rope; and al-dafir is a rope."
"3286","331 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Mualla ibn Mansur narrated: Abu Uways narrated: from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And he had mentioned the hadith before this: flog her - three times - then sell her even for a rope. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ahmad ibn al-Azhar, from al-Mualla ibn Mansur, saying: Abu Uways is not strong. I say: Abu Uways's name is Abdullah ibn Uways ibn Abi Amir al-Asbahi; Muslim narrated from him in his Sahih. And it has a corroboration from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani."
"3287","Another: 332 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated: Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated: from Shubah, from Habib ibn Zayd, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped his ears."
"3288","333 - Abu al-Majd al-Thaqafi also informed us: Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Kanjarudhi informed us: Abu Said Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi al-Basri informed us: Abu Labid Muhammad ibn Idris al-Sami al-Sarakhsi informed us: Suwayd - that is Ibn Said - narrated: Yahya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated: from Shubah, from Habib ibn Zayd, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped his ears. Ibn Majah narrated it from Suwayd ibn Said, with the wording: The ears are part of the head."
"3289","Another: 334 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isfahani informed us - there - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Umm Ibrahim Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated. 335 - al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Dirar ibn Surad Abu Nuaym al-Tahhan narrated: they both said: Man ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated: from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of these two trees should not approach our mosque."
"3290","336 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Saffar informed us - in Nishapur - that Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Hamdun al-Tajir informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi narrated: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Faris al-Dhuhli narrated: Ali ibn Abdullah narrated: Man ibn Isa narrated, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad informed me: from Ibn Shihab, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this garlic tree should not harm us in this mosque of ours. Dirar ibn Surad has been spoken about; he is a corroboration for others. And it has a corroboration in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Nafi, from Ibn Umar, and from the hadith of Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, similarly."
"3291","Another: 337 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Zahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Janzudhi informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Ala ibn Kurayb al-Hamdani narrated: Yahya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated: from Shubah, from Ibn Zayd - that is Habib ibn Zayd - from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought two-thirds of a mudd, performed ablution, and began rubbing his forearms."
"3292","338 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Muadh ibn Muadh narrated: my father narrated: Shubah narrated: from Habib al-Ansari and his grandfather Abdullah ibn Zayd, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd - grandfather of Habib - who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought ablution water of two-thirds of a mudd; I saw him performing ablution, rubbing his forearms with it, and rubbing his ears - meaning when he wiped them."
"3293","339 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad informed them - in Baghdad: Abu al-Fadl Ahmad ibn Khayrun informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Qasim al-Narsi informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafii informed us: Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Matar narrated: Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated: my father narrated: Shubah narrated: from Habib al-Ansari and his grandfather Abdullah ibn Zayd, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, grandfather of Habib, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought ablution water of a third of a mudd; I saw him performing ablution, rubbing his forearms with it, and rubbing his ears when he wiped them. Imam Ahmad narrated part of it from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, from Shubah, from Habib ibn Zayd: he heard Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and kept saying thus, rubbing. And Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih as we included it from his hadith."
"3294","Another: 340 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated: Abu Kurayb narrated. 341 - al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated: Ibn Budayl ibn Warqa narrated to me: al-Zuhri narrated: Abbad ibn Tamim narrated: from his uncle who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying. 342 - al-Tabarani said: Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated: Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated: Abu Asim narrated: Ibrahim ibn Budayl narrated: al-Zuhri narrated: from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O announcers of doom for the Arabs, O announcers of doom for the Arabs, the thing I fear most for you is ostentation and hidden lust."
"3295","343 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ibn Numayr narrated: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to me: Abdullah ibn Budayl ibn Warqa narrated to me, he said: We came to al-Zuhri, and he ordered us driven away; then he sent for us, so we came, and he narrated to us. Al-Zuhri said: Abbad ibn Tamim narrated: from his uncle who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O announcers of doom for the Arabs - three times - the thing I fear most for you is ostentation and hidden lust. Abdullah ibn Adi narrated this hadith from Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili with its chain. And he narrated for Abdullah ibn Budayl other hadiths besides this hadith, saying: Abdullah ibn Budayl has other than what I mentioned that is criticized in him, of addition in text or chain, and I did not see any statement of the early ones about him to mention. And Abu Bakr al-Nisaburi and al-Daraqutni said concerning Abdullah ibn Budayl: He is weak in hadith. I say: Abdullah ibn Budayl was not alone in it, for Ibrahim ibn Budayl narrated it from al-Zuhri."
"3296","Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Ansari Abu Muhammad, who was shown the call to prayer, may Allah be pleased with him. 344 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Amr al-Naqid narrated: Yaqub narrated: my father narrated: from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated: from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbihi: Abdullah ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to me, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a bell to be struck to gather people for prayer - and he disliked it for resembling the Christians - a man wearing two green garments, carrying a bell in his hand, circled me by night while I slept. I said: O servant of Allah, will you sell the bell?"
"3297","345 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz informed us - at al-Harbiyyah - that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yaqub narrated: my father narrated: from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me: from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd Rabbihi: my father Abdullah ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a bell to be struck for people to gather for prayer, a man carrying a bell in his hand circled me while I slept. I said to him: O servant of Allah, will you sell the bell? He said: He said: What will you do with it? He said: I said: We will call to prayer with it. He said: Shall I not guide you to what is better than that? He said: I said to him: Yes. He said: You say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer, come to prayer; come to success, come to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. Then he withdrew a short distance, then said: You say when you stand for prayer: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer; come to success; prayer has commenced, prayer has commenced; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. When morning came I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what I saw. He said: It is surely a true dream, Allah willing. So stand with Bilal and cast upon him what you saw; let him call with it, for he has a more melodious voice than you. He said: So I stood with Bilal, and I kept casting it while he called with it. Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, heard that while in his house, and came out dragging his cloak, saying: By the One who sent you with the truth, I surely saw the like of what he was shown. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To Allah belongs praise. The wording of Imam Ahmad's narration. And in the narration of al-Naqid he said: What will you do with it? I said: I will call to prayer with it. He said: Shall I not guide you to better than that? So he recited the adhan to me. I said: Yes. He said: When you intend to call, you say: Allah is Greatest; and in it: You say when you stand: Allah is Greatest; and in it: When morning came I went early. And with him: So stand and cast what you saw upon Bilal; let him call, for he has a more melodious voice. So I stood with Bilal and kept casting upon him while he called with that. Umar heard his voice while in his house at al-Zawra, and stood dragging his lower garment, saying: By the One who sent you with the truth, I was surely shown the like of what he saw. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To Allah belongs praise; the rest is the same."
"3298","346 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us - in Herat - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Ubayd Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather informed us: Muhammad ibn Isa narrated: Salamah - meaning Ibn al-Fadl - narrated: from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it, people would only gather to him for prayer at the times of its timings without any call. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thought of making a horn like the horn of the Jews with which they call to their prayer, then disliked it. Then he commanded a bell, and it was carved to be struck for Muslims for prayer. While they were upon that, Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbihi - brother of Balharith - was shown the call. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, this night a visitor circled me: a man wearing two green garments carrying a bell in his hand passed by me. I said: O servant of Allah, will you sell this bell? He said: And what will you do with it? I said: We will call to prayer with it. He said: Shall I not guide you to better than that? I said: And what is it? He said: You say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer, come to prayer; come to success, come to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. He said: Then he withdrew not far, then said the like of what he said, saying: And he made it odd except that he said: Prayer has commenced, prayer has commenced; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. When he informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of it, he said: It is surely a true dream, Allah willing. So stand with Bilal and cast it upon him, for he has a more melodious voice than you. He said: When Bilal called with it, Umar ibn al-Khattab heard it while in his house, and went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dragging his cloak, saying: O Prophet of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I surely saw the like of what he saw. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To Allah belongs praise; that is more established. Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated this hadith to me from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbihi with this hadith."
"3299","347 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Fayruz informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Qasim ibn Bishr al-Narsi informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafii informed us: Muhammad ibn Ghalib ibn Harb narrated: Mualla ibn Mansur narrated: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated: from Abu Umays, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd, from his father, from his grandfather: that when he was shown the adhan, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal, so he called, then commanded Abdullah ibn Zayd, so he performed the iqamah. Abu Umays's name is Utbah ibn Abdullah. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yaqub, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: And Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri mentioned, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbihi, and he mentioned it at length. And from Zayd ibn al-Hubab, from Abu Sahl Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, that he was shown the adhan, abridged. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi, from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Said ibn Yahya al-Umawi, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, in part, saying: A hasan sahih hadith. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Maymun al-Madani, from Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Ibn Ishaq with the chain. And Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih as we included it, and from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim similarly. And he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Yahya saying: There is no report among the reports of Abdullah ibn Zayd concerning the adhan story better than this, because Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd heard it from his father, while Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla did not hear from Abdullah ibn Zayd. And he also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq who said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Ubaydullah ibn Shihab al-Zuhri mentioned, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbihi with this report, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is surely a true dream, Allah willing; then he commanded the call, and Bilal, freedman of Abu Bakr, would call with that. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili."
"3300","Another: 348 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated: Abd al-Wahhab narrated: Ubaydullah narrated: from Bashir ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Zayd."
"3301","349 - Farhah bint Firtash ibn Tantash al-Zafariyyah informed us - in Baghdad - that al-Hafiz Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Amal al-Samarqandi informed them: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Mansur al-Zajjaji al-Tabari informed us: Shaykh Abu Ahmad Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Mihran - that is al-Faradi - informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ismail narrated: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas narrated: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated: from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Bashir ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Zayd: that he gave a walled garden of his in charity. His parents came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, it was only the support of our livelihoods, and we have nothing besides it. So he called Abdullah and said: Allah has accepted your charity and returned it to your parents. He said: So we inherited it after that. The wording of Muhammad ibn Amr. And in the narration of Ibn al-Muthanna: It was the support of our livelihoods, and we had nothing besides it."
"3302","350 - And with it, Abu Yala informed us: Abu Musa narrated: Yahya ibn Said narrated: Ubaydullah narrated: Bashir ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to me: that his grandfather Abdullah gave wealth in charity, having no other wealth. His parents came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned similarly."
"3303","351 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated: Muhriz ibn Salamah narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated: from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Bashir ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd who was shown the call, from his father who said: Abdullah ibn Zayd gave wealth in charity, having no other wealth; he and his children lived in it. He handed it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). His father came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah: Abdullah ibn Zayd gave his wealth in charity, while it was that in which he lived. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Abdullah ibn Zayd and said: Allah Almighty has accepted your charity from you and returned it as inheritance to your parents. Bashir said: So we inherited it. In the first narration, the narration of Bashir from his grandfather; in the narration of al-Darawardi, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd was added in it."
"3304","352 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us - in Baghdad - that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them: Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Jabalah al-Tirmidhi narrated: Hajjaj narrated: Hammad narrated: from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm: that Abdullah ibn Zayd had land and made it charity. His parents said: O Messenger of Allah, we had nothing to sustain us besides it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned it to his parents; then he died, and Abdullah inherited it. Al-Nasai narrated it similarly from Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala, from Ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, from Abdullah ibn Zayd."
"3305","Another: 353 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - read to him while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah Sammuyah informed us: Musa ibn Ismail narrated: Aban narrated: Yahya narrated: that Abu Salamah narrated to him: from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd: he narrated to him: that his father witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the slaughter place; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was distributing sacrificial animals, and nothing reached him nor his companion. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved his head into his garment and gave it to him, and trimmed his nails and gave them to his companion. He distributed part of it among men; and it is with us dyed with henna and katam, or katam and henna."
"3306","354 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali and Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbiyan informed us - at al-Harbiyyah - that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated: Aban - meaning al-Attar - narrated: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated: from Abu Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd: that his father narrated to him that he witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the slaughter place, with a man from Quraysh, while he distributed sacrificial animals. Nothing reached him nor his companion. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved his head into his garment and gave it to him, so he distributed part of it among men; and trimmed his nails and gave them to his companion. He said: It is indeed with us dyed with henna and katam - meaning his hair."
"3307","355 - And with it my father narrated to me: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated: Aban al-Attar narrated: from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: that Abu Salamah narrated to him: that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd informed him from his father: that he witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the slaughter place, he and a man from the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sacrificial animals; nothing reached him nor his companion. He shaved his head into his garment and gave it to him - meaning part of it - and distributed part of it among men; and trimmed his nails and gave them to his companion. His hair is indeed with us dyed with henna and katam."
"3308","Abdullah ibn al-Saib ibn Sayfi ibn Aidh ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Makhzum al-Makhzumi, may Allah be pleased with him. 356 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Said narrated: from Ibn Jurayj: Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar narrated to me: from Abdullah ibn Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the day of the Conquest and placed his sandals to his left."
"3309","357 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated: from Ibn Jurayj: Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar narrated: tracing it to Abu Salamah ibn Sufyan and Abdullah ibn Amr al-Qari, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib who said: I attended the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest; he prayed facing the Kaaba, took off his sandals and placed them to his left, then began Surah al-Muminin. When he came to the mention of Jesus or Moses, a cough seized him, so he bowed. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hawdhah ibn Khalifah. And Abu Dawud narrated up to his words: to his left, from Musaddad, from Yahya ibn Said. And al-Nasai narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Said al-Sarakhsi and Shuayb ibn Yusuf, from Yahya. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Yahya. As for the mention of Jesus or Moses, a cough seized him and he bowed: Muslim included it in his Sahih from Harun al-Hammal, from Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, and from Muhammad ibn Rafi, from Abd al-Razzaq - both from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn Abbad, from Abu Salamah ibn Sufyan, Abdullah ibn Amr, and Abdullah ibn al-Musayyib, all from Ibn al-Saib."
"3310","Another: 358 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Harawi narrated. 359 - al-Tabarani said: And Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated. 360 - He said: And Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us: Said ibn Sulayman and Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dawlabi narrated: they said: al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated: from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib that he said: I attended the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Eid, and he said: The prayer has been concluded; whoever wishes to sit for the sermon, let him sit, and whoever wishes to leave, let him leave. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ibrahim al-Marwazi, from al-Fadl ibn Musa, with its chain, similarly, saying: This is a mistake; the correct is mursal. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Hadiyyah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Marwazi and Amr ibn Rafi al-Bajali, from al-Fadl ibn Musa."
"3311","Another: 361 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz and others informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Said narrated: from Ibn Jurayj: Yahya ibn Ubayd informed me: from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying between the Yemeni Corner and the Stone: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. And Abd al-Razzaq, Ibn Bakr, and Rawh said in this hadith: He heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying between the corner of Banu Jumah and the Black Corner: Our Lord, give us."
"3312","362 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Yahya ibn Ubayd, freedman of al-Saib, informed me that he informed him: that Abdullah ibn al-Saib informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying between the corner of Banu Jumah and the Black Corner: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"3313","363 - And with it al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Abu Nuaym narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Ibn Jurayj, from Yahya ibn Ubayd, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq, Rawh, and Ibn Bakr, from Ibn Jurayj, from Yahya ibn Ubayd, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Isa ibn Yunus, from Ibn Jurayj, from Yahya ibn Ubayd, from his father. And al-Nasai narrated it from Yaqub al-Dawraqi, from Yahya ibn Said, like the narration of Imam Ahmad. In both narrations of al-Tabarani there is no from his father, unless Yahya heard it from Abdullah al-Saib; and Allah knows best, otherwise it dropped."
"3314","Another: 364 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Said narrated: from al-Saib ibn Umar: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Saib narrated to me: that Abdullah ibn al-Saib used to lead Ibn Abbas and station him at the third opening from the door side facing the Stone. I said - meaning the speaker is Ibn Abbas - to Abdullah ibn al-Saib: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand here, or pray here. He would say: Yes. So Ibn Abbas would stand and pray."
"3315","365 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated: al-Saib ibn Umar narrated: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me: that Ibn Abbas sent to Abdullah ibn al-Saib: Stand and show me where the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed facing the Kaaba. He said: At the third opening. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Qawariri. And al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Ali, both from Yahya ibn Said, similarly."
"3316","Another: 366 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah narrated: from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray four before Zuhr after the sun declined, saying: The gates of heaven are opened, so I love to send forth a righteous deed in them."
"3317","367 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Amr ibn Awn narrated: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated: from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray four rakahs when the sun declined. He was asked about that and said: This is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, so I love that a righteous deed of mine ascends in it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Abu Dawud. Ibn Abi Layla - I think him Muhammad; we included it as corroboration for others."
"3318","Another: 368 - Abu Jafar Muhammad informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated: they both said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated: from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib who said: I was a partner of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When I came to Madinah he said: Do you know me? I said: You were my partner; what an excellent partner - you would not quarrel nor evade."
"3319","369 - And with it, al-Tabarani informed us: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated: Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated: from his father, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance. I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you know me? He said: Yes; were you not once my partner, and I found you the best partner - you neither evade nor quarrel."
"3320","370 - Abu Hashim ibn Ahmad al-Dawshabi informed us, in writing. 371 - And Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us from him that Abu Abdullah al-Hammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Busri informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed us: Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl informed us: Abd al-Karim - that is Ibn al-Haytham al-Dayr Aquli - narrated: Said ibn Sulayman Sadawayh narrated: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated: from al-Amash, from Mujahid who said: My master Abdullah ibn al-Saib narrated to me, he said: I was a partner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the pre-Islamic era. I came to Madinah and he said: Do you know me? I said: Yes; you were my partner; what an excellent partner - you would not quarrel nor evade. Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated it from Mujahid, from al-Saib ibn Abi al-Saib, that he used to partner the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before Islam in trade. When the day of the Conquest came, he came to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Welcome to my brother and partner; he would neither evade nor quarrel. And Israil narrated it from Ibrahim, from Mujahid, from al-Saib, like this narration. And both narrations contain discrepancy: in the narration of Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym and in the narration of Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah, from his father, from al-Amash, from Mujahid: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the speaker. And in the narration of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir and Mansur ibn al-Aswad, al-Saib and Abdullah his son - each one of them is the speaker to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And it is possible - and Allah knows best - that both used to partner the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) together, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it to both together, or both said it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): in the narration of al-Saib, he came on the day of the Conquest; in this narration of Abdullah: When I came to Madinah. So the story of al-Saib is other than the story of his son; and whoever was a partner of a man, the son's assistance to him in his trade is not denied; and Allah knows best."
"3321","Abdullah ibn Sabrah, may Allah be pleased with him. 372 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated: from Abdullah ibn Nusayb, from Muslim ibn Abdullah ibn Sabrah, from his father: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I forbid you three things: gossip, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth."
"3322","373 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdan ibn Ahmad and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated: they both said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated: from Abdullah ibn Nusayb, from Muslim ibn Abdullah ibn Sabrah, from his father: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah forbids you gossip, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth. It has a corroboration in the two Sahihs from the hadith of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah."
"3323","Abdullah ibn Sarjis al-Muzani, may Allah be pleased with him. 374 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated: my father narrated to me: from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3324","375 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated: my father narrated to me: from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should urinate in a burrow; and when you sleep, extinguish the lamp, for the mouse takes the wick and burns the household; tie the waterskins, cover drinks, and lock doors at night. They said to Qatadah: What is disliked about urinating in a burrow? He said: It is said they are dwellings of the jinn. The wording is one, except that in the narration of al-Qawariri: from the dwellings of the jinn. Abu Dawud narrated from al-Qawariri its beginning: the prohibition of urinating in a burrow. And al-Nasai narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Said al-Sarakhsi, from Muadh, likewise concerning urination. It was reported from Imam Ahmad that he said: I do not know Qatadah narrating from any Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Anas. It was said: Then Ibn Sarjis? As if he did not view it as hearing. It has a corroboration in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, concerning his words: Cover vessels, tie waterskins, and close doors."
"3325","Another: 376 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - read to him while present: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Nasr ibn Ali narrated: Nuh ibn Qays narrated: from Abdullah ibn Imran, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis al-Muzani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3326","377 - Abu Jafar also informed us: Abu Ali informed them - while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated: Nuh ibn Qays narrated: Abdullah ibn Imran narrated: Abdullah ibn Sarjis narrated, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"3327","378 - Abu Jafar also informed us: Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated: Nasr ibn Ali narrated: Nuh ibn Qays al-Huddani narrated: from Abdullah ibn Imran al-Qurashi, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Moderation, deliberation, and good composure are one part of twenty-four parts of prophethood. In the narration of Ibn Abi Asim: Good composure, deliberation, and moderation. And in the narration of Muslim ibn Ibrahim: Deliberation and good composure."
"3328","379 - Imam Abu al-Futuh Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli and Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad Abu Abdullah al-Qadi al-Barakati narrated: Nasr ibn Ali narrated: Nuh ibn Qays narrated: from Abdullah ibn Imran al-Huddani, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Righteous guidance, righteous composure, moderation, and deliberation are one part of twenty-four parts of prophethood. al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Asim except Abdullah ibn Imran; Nuh ibn Qays was alone in it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Nasr ibn Ali like the narration of Ibn Abi Asim, saying: A hasan gharib hadith. And from Qutaybah, from Nuh, from Abdullah ibn Imran, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, similarly, without mentioning Asim al-Ahwal. He said: The correct is the hadith of Nasr."
"3329","Another: 380 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isfahani informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - read to him while present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated: Abu Muawiyah narrated: Asim narrated: from Abdullah ibn Sarjis who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In cupping there is healing."
"3330","381 - Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sad and Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us of it: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - both present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us: Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat al-Razi narrated: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli informed us: Abu Muawiyah narrated: from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In cupping there is healing."
"3331","Another: 382 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr - in Cairo - that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh informed us, he said: I said to Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq: Did Ibn Jurayj mention from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day wearing a namirah, and said to a man among his Companions: Give me your garment and take my namirah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, your namirah is better than my namirah. He said: Yes, but in it is a red thread, and I feared looking at it lest it distract me. So he affirmed it, saying: Yes."
"3332","383 - And with it al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated: Said ibn Salamah narrated: Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me: from Abdullah ibn Sarjis: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day wearing a namirah, and said to a man among his Companions: Give me your namirah and take my namirah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, your namirah is better than my namirah. He said: Yes, but in it is a red line, and I feared looking at it lest it distract me from my prayer. Muhammad ibn Zakariyya is al-Ghallabi; al-Daraqutni spoke about him; we included him for corroboration."
"3333","Another: 384 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated: Abu Awn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Awn narrated: Abu Hurayrah Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Wasiti narrated: Amr ibn Sulayman narrated: from Abdullah ibn Imran - kunyah Abu Abd al-Rahman - from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis who said: I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I love Abu Dharr. He said: Did you inform him of that? I said: No. He said: Then inform him. So I met Abu Dharr and said: I love you for Allah's sake. He said: May the One for whom you loved me love you. So I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Verily that brings reward for whoever mentions it."
"3334","Abdullah ibn Sad al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. 385 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated: Muawiyah - meaning Ibn Salih - narrated: from al-Ala - meaning Ibn al-Harith - from Haram ibn Hakim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Sad: that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about what necessitates ghusl, about fluid after fluid, about praying in my house, about praying in the mosque, and about eating with a menstruating woman. He said: Allah is not shy of the truth. As for me, when I do such and such - and he mentioned ghusl - he said: I perform my ablution for prayer, washing my private part - then he mentioned ghusl - and as for fluid after fluid, that is madhy; every male emits madhy, so I wash my private part from that and perform ablution. As for praying in the mosque and praying in my house: you see how close my house is to the mosque, yet praying in my house is more beloved to me than praying in the mosque, except an obligatory prayer. As for eating with a menstruating woman: eat with her."
"3335","386 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Bundar narrated: Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Mahdi - narrated: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated: al-Ala ibn al-Harith narrated: from Haram, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Sad."
"3336","Ibn Khuzaymah said: Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muawiyah (Ha). He said: And Bahr ibn Nasr al-Khawlani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Haram ibn Hakim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Sad who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about praying in my house and praying in the mosque, and he said: You see how close my house is to the mosque; yet for me to pray in my house is dearer to me than for me to pray in the mosque, except the obligatory prayer. This is the wording of Bundar."
"3337","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi reported to them, recited to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab reported to us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Haram ibn Muawiyah, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Sad who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about eating with a menstruating woman, and he said: I eat with her while she is menstruating. Imam Ahmad also narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Muawiyah, from Haram ibn Muawiyah, from his uncle who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about eating with a menstruating woman, and he said: Eat with her. I say: The well-known name is Haram ibn Hakim, and Allah knows best."
"3338","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Maali ibn Ghanimah ibn al-Hasan informed us at the Basra Gate of Baghdad that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi reported to them: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khatib reported to us, al-Qasim ibn Jafar al-Hashimi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lului reported to us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Marwan, meaning Ibn Muawiyah, narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Ala ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Hizam ibn Hakim, from his uncle that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is lawful for me of my wife while she is menstruating? He said: What is above the waist-wrapper. And he mentioned eating with a menstruating woman as well and related the hadith. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it. Abu Dawud also narrated from Ibrahim ibn Musa, from Abdullah ibn Wahb, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from al-Ala, from Hizam ibn Hakim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Sad al-Ansari: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about what makes ghusl obligatory and about the fluid that comes after fluid, and he said: That is madhy, and every stallion emits madhy, so wash your private part and your testicles from that, and perform wudu as you do for prayer. Al-Tirmidhi narrated the story of eating with a menstruating woman only, from Abbas al-Anbari and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, from Ibn Mahdi. And he narrated in the book of Shama il from Abbas his asking about praying in his house or in the mosque. And Ibn Majah narrated the story of eating with a menstruating woman and the story of prayer in the house or prayer in the mosque, from Bakr ibn Khalaf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi."
"3339","Abdullah ibn Said ibn al-As, may Allah be pleased with him. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani informed us at Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bahr al-Hujaymi narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya ibn Said ibn Umar ibn Said ibn al-As narrated to us, my grandfather Said ibn Umar narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Said ibn al-As that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is your name? He said: al-Hakam. He said: You are Abdullah. He said: I am Abdullah, O Messenger of Allah."
"3340","Abdullah ibn Sufyan al-Azdi, may Allah be pleased with him. Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad reported to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti and Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Habib ibn Ubayd referring it to Abu Bishr, Abu Bishr referring it to Uthamah ibn Qays, Uthamah referring it to Abdullah ibn Sufyan al-Azdi, both of them among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no man who fasts a day in the path of Allah except that Allah distances him from the Fire by a measure of one hundred years. Abdullah ibn Sufyan said: I only narrate to you what I heard, and I do not narrate to you what you desire."
"3341","Abdullah ibn Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him. With the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us: Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my uncle Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abdullah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: A Jew came demanding dates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke harshly to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so his Companions were about to attack him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not sanctified, or he said: Allah does not have mercy upon, a nation who do not take for the weak among them his right without stammering. Then he sent to Khawlah bint Hakim and borrowed dates from her and paid him, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Thus do the faithful servants of Allah act. Indeed there were dates with us, but they were dusty."
"3342","Abdullah ibn Salam Abu Yusuf, may Allah be pleased with him. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ikhwah al-Baghdadi then al-Isbahani informed us at Isfahan that Abu Sahl Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sadawayh reported to them: Abu al-Fadl Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi reported to us, the judge Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Raffa al-Surramara i reported to us (Ha). And Abu al-Hasan al-Muayyad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Tusi informed us, with my recitation to him at Nishapur, I said to him: Abu Muhammad Hibatullah ibn Sahl ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn known as al-Sayyidi reported to you, recited to him while you heard: Abu Uthman Said ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Buhayri reported to us, Abu Ali Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi reported to us, both saying: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Samad al-Hashimi reported to us, Abu Musab Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Zuhri narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah that he said: I went out to al-Tur and met Kab al-Ahbar, and I sat with him and he narrated to me from the Torah and I narrated to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Among what I narrated to him was that I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; on it Adam was created, on it he was sent down, on it he died, on it his repentance was accepted, and on it the Hour will come. And there is no creature except that it listens intently on Friday from morning until sunrise, out of fear of the Hour, except jinn and mankind. And on it there is an hour which no Muslim servant coincides with while praying and asking Allah for something except that He gives it to him. Kab said: That is one day in every year? I said: Rather, in every Friday. He said: So Kab read the Torah and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth. Abu Hurayrah said: Then I met Basrah ibn Abi Basrah al-Ghifari and he said: From where have you come? I said: From al-Tur. He said: Had I met you before you went to it, you would not have gone to it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, or this mosque of mine, or the mosque of Iliya, or Bayt al-Maqdis, doubting which of the two. Abu Hurayrah said: Then I met Abdullah ibn Salam and told him of my sitting with Kab al-Ahbar and what I had narrated to him about Friday, and I said to him: Kab said that is one day in every year. Abdullah ibn Salam said: Kab lied. I said: Then he read the Torah and said: Rather it is in every Friday. Abdullah ibn Salam said: Kab spoke the truth. Then Abdullah ibn Salam said: I know which hour it is. Abu Hurayrah said: I said to him: Tell me of it and do not withhold from me. Abdullah ibn Salam said: It is the last hour of Friday. Abu Hurayrah said: And how can it be the last hour of Friday when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim servant coincides with it while praying, and that is an hour in which prayer is not performed? Abdullah ibn Salam said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not say: Whoever sits in a sitting waiting for prayer is in prayer until he prays? Abu Hurayrah said: Yes. He said: Then that is it. This is the wording of the hadith of Zahir al-Sarakhsi except his saying: before you went to it, for according to him: before you went out, you would not have gone to it. And in the narration of Ali al-Surramara i: on it he was sent down and on it Allah accepted his repentance, and according to him there is no: on it he died, and according to him: the Sacred Mosque and this mosque of mine, and according to him there is no: Abu Hurayrah said: And how can it be the last hour of Friday."
"3343","Abu al-Qasim Hibatullah ibn Ali ibn Saud ibn Thabit al-Ansari al-Busiri informed us in Egypt more than once that Abu Sadiq Murshid ibn Yahya ibn al-Qasim al-Madini reported to them, recited to him: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Naysaburi known as Ibn al-Taffal reported to them, recited to him from the original of his hearing: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh al-Naysaburi reported to them, recited to him: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali al-Nasai narrated to us, in wording recited to us from his book: Qutaybah ibn Said reported to us, Bakr, who is Ibn Mudar, reported to us, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I came to al-Tur and found Kab, and I and he remained a day, I narrating to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he narrating to me from the Torah. I said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; on it Adam was created, on it he was sent down, on it his repentance was accepted, on it he was taken, and on it the Hour will come. There is no creature on the face of the earth except that it wakes on Friday listening intently until sunrise, out of fear of the Hour, except the son of Adam. And on it there is an hour which no believer coincides with while in prayer asking Allah for something except that He gives it to him. Kab said: That is one day in every year. I said: Rather it is in every Friday. Then Kab read and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth; it is in every Friday. Then I went out and met Basrah ibn Abi Basrah al-Ghifari and he said: From where have you come? I said: From al-Tur. He said: Had I met you before you came to it, you would not have come to it. I said to him: Why? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, my mosque, and the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis. Then I met Abdullah ibn Salam and said to him: Had you seen me, I went out to al-Tur and came to Kab, and I and he were a day, I narrating to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he narrating to me from the Torah. I said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; on it Adam was created, on it he was sent down, on it his repentance was accepted, on it he was taken, and on it the Hour will come. There is no creature on earth except that it wakes on Friday listening intently until sunrise out of fear of the Hour except the son of Adam. And on it there is an hour which no believing servant coincides with while in prayer asking Allah Almighty for something except that He gives it to him. Kab said: That is one day in every year. Abdullah ibn Salam said: Kab lied. I said: Then Kab read and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth; it is in every Friday. Abdullah ibn Salam said: Kab spoke the truth. I know that hour. I said: O my brother, tell me of it. He said: It is the last hour of Friday before the sun sets. I said: Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No believer coincides with it while in prayer, and that is not an hour of prayer? He said: Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays and sits waiting for prayer remains in prayer until the next one comes to him? I said: Yes. He said: Then it is so."
"3344","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq reported to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from Abdullah ibn Salam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sits waiting for prayer is in prayer."
"3345","With the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us: Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Awaqi narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Harith, from Abu Salamah who said: Abu Hurayrah used to narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: In Friday there is an hour which no Muslim coincides with while in prayer asking Allah for good except that He gives it to him. Abu Hurayrah would make it seem small with his hand. When Abu Hurayrah died I said: If I went to Abu Said and asked him. So I came to him and asked him, then I went out from him and was directed to Abdullah ibn Salam and asked him. He said: Allah Almighty created Adam on Friday and took him on Friday, and on it the Hour will come, and it is the last hour. I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: in prayer, and it is not an hour of prayer. He said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One waiting for prayer is in prayer? I said: Yes. He said: Then by Allah, it is it. The point of this hadith is the narration of Abdullah ibn Salam. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yunus and Shurayh, from Fulayh; and from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Malik; and from Yazid ibn Harun; and from Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Qays ibn Sad, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim similarly. And Abu Dawud narrated the narration of Abdullah ibn Salam from al-Qanabi, from Malik. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ishaq ibn Musa, from Man, from Malik, and said: A sound hadith. Al-Nasai narrated it as we narrated it from his hadith."
"3346","Another. Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us at al-Harim that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Awf, Zurarah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salam said (Ha). Imam Ahmad said: And Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Zurarah, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived, the people rushed toward him, and I was among those who rushed. When I discerned his face I knew that his face was not the face of a liar. The first thing I heard him say was: Spread peace, feed food, join kinship ties, and pray while people sleep; you will enter Paradise in peace."
"3347","Abu Ali Diya ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Ali known as Ibn al-Khurayf informed us at Baghdad that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Ansari reported to them, saying: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari narrated to us by dictation: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan ibn Malik al-Qatii narrated to us (Ha). And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, both saying: Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muadh ibn Awdhullah al-Qurashi narrated to us, both saying: Awf narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Medina, the people rushed toward him and I was among those who went out. When I saw his face I knew it was not the face of a liar. The first thing I heard him say was: Feed food, spread peace, join kinship ties, and pray while people sleep; you will enter Paradise in peace. The wording is that of al-Tabarani. The narration of al-Qatii says: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, he said: So I came among the people to look. When I discerned his face I knew his face was not the face of a liar. The first thing I heard him utter was that he said: O people, spread peace and feed food. The rest is similar."
"3348","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad reported to them while present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Said ibn al-Hasan al-Askari narrated to us, Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa Abdan narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Awf, from Zurarah, Abdullah ibn Salam narrated to me, saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Medina, the people rushed toward him, and it was said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has arrived. So I came among the people to look at him. When I discerned his face I knew his face was not the face of a liar. The first thing I heard him utter was that he said: O people, spread peace, feed food, join kinship ties, and pray at night while people sleep; you will enter Paradise in peace. In this hadith is clarification of Zurarah hearing from Abdullah ibn Salam. Al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah both narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from al-Thaqafi and Anid and Ibn Abi Adi and Yahya ibn Said, from Awf. Ibn Majah also narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Tirmidhi said: A sound hadith. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: I do not think Zurarah heard from Abdullah ibn Salam."
"3349","Another. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Utbah, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he spoke would raise his head to the sky."
"3350","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ubayd ibn Ghannam ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali and Uqbah ibn Mukram and Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Utbah ibn al-Mughirah ibn al-Akhnas, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father who said: We would be with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he spoke he would raise his head to the sky. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani, from Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq similarly."
"3351","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: I sat among a group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they said: Which of you will go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him which deeds are most beloved to Allah? Then it was revealed: O you who believe, why do you say what you do not do. Abu Salamah said: Abdullah ibn Salam recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Yahya said: Abu Salamah recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Al-Awzai said: Yahya recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Al-Walid said: Al-Awzai recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Duhaym said: Al-Walid recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Ibrahim said: My father recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept. Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani said: Ibrahim recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then he wept."
"3352","Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Samad al-Sulami informed us that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa ibn Shuayb al-Sijzi reported to them: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah al-Sarakhsi reported to us, Isa ibn Umar ibn al-Abbas al-Samarqandi reported to us, Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Bahram al-Darimi al-Samarqandi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: A group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and conversed, and we said: If we knew which deeds are most beloved to Allah we would do them. Then Allah revealed: Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on earth glorifies Allah, and He is the Exalted, the Wise. O you who believe, why do you say what you do not do, until its end. Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it to us until its end. Abu Salamah said: Ibn Salam recited it to us. Yahya said: Abu Salamah recited it to us, and Yahya recited it to us, and al-Awzai recited it to us, and Muhammad recited it to us. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from al-Darimi. And he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated this hadith from al-Awzai, from Yahya, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Salam, or from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Salam. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Asim al-Ansari al-Dimashqi, who was a chief among its chiefs, from Hisham ibn Ammar, from al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"3353","Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan that al-Husayn al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, from al-Awzai, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Hilal narrated to me that Ata ibn Yasar narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Salam narrated to him, or he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: We conversed among ourselves and said: Which of you will go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him which deeds are most beloved to Allah? We feared that any of us would stand, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for us man by man until he gathered us. We came, some of us pointing to others, and he recited to us the surah: Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on earth glorifies Allah, and He is the Exalted, the Wise. O you who believe, why do you say what you do not do. He recited it from its beginning to its end. He said: Abdullah ibn Salam recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Hilal said: Ata recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Yahya said: Hilal recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Al-Awzai said: Yahya recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yamur and Yahya ibn Adam, from Ibn al-Mubarak, and the hadith of Yamur is more complete. In the narration of Yahya ibn Adam from Ibn al-Mubarak from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, or from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Salam, and in it there is no Hilal."
"3354","Another. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi reported to them: Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim and Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani reported to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb reported to us, Amr informed me, from Ibn Abi Hilal, that Yahya ibn Abdullah narrated to him (Ha). And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us (Ha). He said: And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki and Masad ibn Sad al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us (Ha). He said: And Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, all saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, that Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, from Awn ibn Abdullah, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father who said: While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he heard the people saying: Which deeds are best, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith in Allah and His Messenger, jihad in His path, and an accepted pilgrimage. Then he heard a call in the valley saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I bear witness, and I bear witness that no one bears it except that he is cleared of polytheism. The wording is that of the hadith of Ahmad ibn Salih and Harmalah, except that Harmalah in his narration has: and jihad in the path of Allah. Al-Nasai narrated it in the book of deeds of day and night from Amr ibn Mansur, from Asbagh ibn al-Faraj with his chain: While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he heard in the valley a man saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. Ahmad ibn Rishdin, we brought him for consideration. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Ibn Salim, from Harmalah ibn Yahya."
"3355","Another. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, al-Dahhak narrated to me, from Abi al-Nadr, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Salam (Ha)."
"3356","Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, all from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: I said while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting: We find in the Book of Allah concerning Friday an hour which no Muslim servant coincides with while in prayer asking Allah Almighty for something except that He gives him what he asked. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured, saying: Part of an hour. He said: I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth. Abu al-Nadr said: Abu Salamah said: I asked him which hour it is? He said: The last hours of the day. I said: It is not an hour of prayer. He said: Yes, the Muslim servant when he prays then sits in his prayer place, nothing detains him except waiting for prayer. The wording is that of Imam Ahmad. In the narration of Ibn Abi Fudayk: We find. And according to him: A believing servant praying, asking Allah for something except that He fulfills his need for him. Abdullah said: He gestured to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Part of an hour. I said: You spoke the truth, part of an hour. I said: Which hour is it? He said: The last hours of the day. I said: It is not an hour of prayer. He said: Yes, the believing servant when he prays then sits, nothing detains him except prayer, so he is in prayer. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abd al-Rahman known as Duhaym similarly. This resembles the first hadith of Abdullah, except that in it are things not in that one, and some of those who compiled the appendices made it other than that. In this narration: I said: It is not an hour of prayer, is from the saying of Abdullah ibn Salam, and its end is from the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). In the narration of Imam Ahmad it is from the saying of Abu Salamah, and its end is from the saying of Abdullah ibn Salam."
"3357","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us there that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, both saying: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Salam who said: When Allah Almighty willed the guidance of Zayd ibn Sanah, Zayd ibn Sanah said: There is no sign of prophethood except that I recognized it in the face of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I looked at him, except two I had not tested in him: his forbearance precedes his anger, and severity of ignorance against him only increases him in forbearance. I was being subtle with him to mix with him so I would know his forbearance from his anger. Zayd ibn Sanah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day from the apartments, with him Ali ibn Abi Talib, and a man on his mount like a Bedouin came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, Busra near me, a village of so-and-so, have embraced Islam and entered Islam, and I had told them if they embraced Islam provision would come to them abundantly. A year of drought and hardship and lack of rain has afflicted them, and I fear, O Messenger of Allah, that they will leave Islam out of greed just as they entered it out of greed. If you think fit to send them something to help them, do so. He looked at a man beside him, I think it was Ali, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing of it remains. Zayd ibn Sanah said: So I drew near to him and said: O Muhammad, will you sell me known dates from the orchard of so-and-so until such-and-such term? He said: No, O Jew, but I will sell you known dates until such-and-such term, without naming the orchard of so-and-so. I said: Yes. So he dealt with me, and I released my purse and gave him eighty mithqals of gold for known dates until such-and-such term, and he gave it to the man and said: Hasten, deal justly with them and help them with it. Zayd ibn Sanah said: Two or three days before the term, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out with Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman among a group of his Companions. When he prayed over a funeral and drew near a wall to sit, I came to him and seized the collars of his shirt and cloak, and looked at him with a harsh face, and said to him: Will you not pay me, O Muhammad, my due? By Allah, I have only known you, O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, as delayers, and I had knowledge from mixing with you. I looked at Umar and his eyes were turning in his face like a revolving wheel. Then he cast his sight at me and said: O enemy of Allah, do you say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I hear, and do to him what I see? By Him who sent him with the truth, were it not that I fear missing him, I would strike your head with my sword. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was looking at Umar in calmness, composure and smiling, then he said: O Umar, he and I needed other than this: that you command me to pay well and command him to demand well. Go with him, O Umar, and give him his due, and add to him twenty sas of dates in place of your frightening him. Zayd said: Umar took me and gave me my due and added twenty sas of dates. I said: What is this addition, O Umar? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to add to you in place of my frightening you. He said: Do you know me, O Umar? He said: No. What made you do to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what you did and say to him what you said? I said: O Umar, there was no sign of prophethood except that I recognized it in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I looked at him, except two I had not tested in him: his forbearance precedes his anger, and severity of ignorance against him only increases him in forbearance. They have now been tested. I call you to witness, O Umar, that I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet. And I call you to witness that half my wealth, for I am among the wealthiest of them, is charity upon the nation of Muhammad. Umar said: Or upon some of them, for you cannot encompass them. I said: Or upon some of them. Umar and Zayd returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Zayd said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He believed in him, affirmed him, pledged to him, and witnessed many battles with him, then he died in the expedition of Tabuk, advancing, not retreating. May Allah have mercy on Zayd. Ibn Majah narrated part of it from Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib, from al-Walid ibn Muslim with his chain, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: So-and-so have embraced Islam, for a people of the Jews, and they are hungry, and I fear they will apostatize. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who has anything? A Jewish man said: I have such-and-such, for something he named, I think he said: three hundred dinars at such-and-such price from the orchard of so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: At such-and-such price until such-and-such term, and not from the orchard of so-and-so. This is the portion Ibn Majah narrated. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it in full from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan and Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah, from Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil, who is Ibn Abi al-Sari, similarly, and in it: O Messenger of Allah, the village of so-and-so have embraced Islam. The hadith we narrated in the musnad of Zayd ibn Sanah is more fitting, and Allah knows best. It is possible that Abdullah ibn Salam witnessed that, for what Ibn Majah narrated has no mention of Zayd ibn Sanah, and he made the story from the saying of Abdullah."
"3358","Another. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi reported to them: Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim and Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani reported to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb reported to us, Amr reported to us that Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari narrated to him that Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban narrated to him: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is no burden upon one of you, if he finds means, or: It is no burden upon you, if you find means, to take two garments for Friday other than his work clothes. Amr said: And Ibn Abi Habib informed me, from Musa ibn Said, from Ibn Hibban, from Ibn Salam: That he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that upon the pulpit."
"3359","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Musa ibn Sad, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, from Abdullah ibn Salam, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the pulpit: It is no burden upon you, if you find means, to take two garments for Friday other than work clothes. Ibn Majah narrated it from Harmalah ibn Yahya, and from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from a shaykh of his, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah, from his father. I say: The shaykh whom Ibn Abi Shaybah alluded to without naming is Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi. Musa ibn Sad is the son of Zayd ibn Thabit; Muslim narrated for him. Abd al-Razzaq said: He is Musa ibn Said."
"3360","Another. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Ismail ibn Sinan narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Qasim who said: Abdullah ibn Hanzalah claimed that Abdullah ibn Salam passed through the market carrying a bundle of firewood. It was said to him: Has Allah not sufficed you from this? He said: Yes, but I wanted to suppress pride. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None shall enter Paradise in whose heart is a mustard seed weight of pride."
"3361","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Salim ibn Muslim al-Warraq narrated to us (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Isbahani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Ismail ibn Sinan Abu Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated to us, both saying: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Hanzalah al-Rahib claimed that Abdullah ibn Salam passed through the market carrying a bundle of firewood. It was said to him: What makes you do this when Allah has sufficed you from this? He said: I wanted to crush pride. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None shall enter Paradise in whose heart is a mustard grain of pride."
"3362","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr and Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi said: Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us (Ha). And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali reported to us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Mamar ibn Rashid, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Yaqub, from Bishr ibn Shaghaf, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, without boasting; the first for whom the earth will split, the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted. In my hand is the banner of praise; beneath me Adam and all below him. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili."
"3363","Another. Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Zurayk ibn Abi Zurayk narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Abdullah ibn Salam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of women delights you when you look, obeys you when you command, and guards your absence concerning herself and your wealth."
"3364","Another. With the same chain al-Tabarani reported to us: Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Isbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Zurayk ibn Abi Zurayk narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The distance between the two leaves of the gate of Paradise is forty years, and a day will come upon it when it is crowded as camels crowd when they come after five days of thirst. Zurayk ibn Abi Zurayk was declared trustworthy by Yahya ibn Main. This hadith has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Utbah ibn Ghazwan with its meaning."
"3365","Another. Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us at al-Harim that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, al-Fudayl, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Khunays al-Ghifari, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: What is between Kuda and Uhud is sanctuary; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made it sanctuary. I would neither cut a tree in it nor kill a bird in it."
"3366","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us, Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, both saying: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Khunays, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: What is between Ayr and Uhud is sanctuary; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made it sanctuary. I would neither cut a tree from it nor hunt a bird. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim mentioned Ubaydullah ibn Khunays, and he is in the musnad of the Imam, and in the book of al-Tabarani: Hubaysh. Fudayl ibn Sulayman was criticized, though Muslim narrated for him."
"3367","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad reported to them while present: Abu Nuaym reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, from Mamar, from Muhammad ibn Hamzah, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: When hardship befell his family, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would command them to pray, then recite: And command your family to prayer and be patient upon it, the verse. Al-Tabarani said: It is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Salam except with this chain; Mamar is alone in it."
"3368","Another. Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Fadail ibn Ali al-Tikriti informed us at Baghdad that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Umar reported to them: Asim ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Asim reported to us, Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Farisi reported to us, Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us by dictation, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Hawaribi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: The description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Torah: We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of glad tidings, a warner, and a refuge for the unlettered; neither harsh nor rude nor noisy in the markets; he does not repay evil with evil, but pardons and overlooks. I shall not take him until I straighten through him the crooked religion, and open through him deaf ears, blind eyes and covered hearts, that they say: There is no god but Allah. Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hafiz narrated similarly from Abdullah ibn Salih, from al-Layth, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Hilal ibn Usamah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Salam."
"3369","Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir ibn Awf ibn Kab ibn Waqdan ibn al-Harish al-Harishi, may Allah be pleased with him. Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Wahid al-Saydalani informed us at Isfahan that Abu al-Fath Ismail ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Akhshid al-Sarraj reported to them: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim reported to us, Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saigh reported to us, Abu Bakr Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah reported to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying, and in his chest was a moaning like the moaning of a cooking pot, from weeping."
"3370","With the same chain Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi reported to us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Balkhi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak reported to us, Hammad ibn Salamah reported to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Mutarrif, from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying, and in his chest was a moaning like the moaning of a cooking pot."
"3371","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us (Ha). Sulayman said: And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Mutarrif, from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and in his chest was a moaning like the moaning of a cooking pot."
"3372","With the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad reported to us: Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us (Ha). Sulayman said: And Abu Usamah Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Yahya, from Abd al-Karim ibn Rashid, from Ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father who said: I used to hear for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a moaning in supplication while prostrating like the moaning of a cooking pot."
"3373","Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi informed us that Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khidr al-Sulami reported to them: Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kattani reported to us, Tamam ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Razi reported to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Baghdadi reported to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Jad narrated to us at Baghdad, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father who said: I reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and in his chest was a moaning like the moaning of a cooking pot."
"3374","Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali reported to us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Hawtharah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque while he was standing praying, and in his chest was a moaning like the moaning of a cooking pot. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun. Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: None said from weeping except Yazid ibn Harun. He also narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Hammad ibn Salamah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Sallam, from Yazid ibn Harun. Al-Nasai and al-Tirmidhi in the book of Shama il both narrated it from Suwayd ibn Nasr, from Ibn al-Mubarak. Al-Nasai also narrated it from Isa ibn Yunus al-Ramli, from Damrah. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili, and from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh."
"3375","Another. Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Waiz informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, saying: I heard Qatadah say: I heard Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir narrating from his father who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You are the master of Quraysh. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Master is Allah. He said: You are the best of them in speech and the greatest of them in bounty. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you speak his word, and let not Satan draw him on."
"3376","Abu Jafar ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad reported to them while present: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab reported to us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from his father who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You are the master of Quraysh. He said: The Master is Allah. He said: You are the best of them in speech and the greatest of them in bounty. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you speak a word; let not Satan draw him on, or he said: the devils. Ghaylan ibn Jarir also narrated it from Mutarrif."
"3377","Abu Jafar also informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad reported to them while present: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim reported to us, Abdullah al-Qabbab reported to us, Ahmad ibn Amr reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a delegation of Banu Amir. We greeted him and said: You are our father, our master, the best of us in merit over us, the greatest of us in bounty over us, and the overflowing bowl. He said: Say your saying; let not Satan mock you. Abu Nadrah also narrated it from Mutarrif."
"3378","Abu Jafar also informed us that Fatimah reported to them, recited to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Abu Maslamah Said ibn Yazid narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Mutarrif who said: My father said: I went with the delegation of Banu Amir to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: You are our master. He said: The Master is Allah. They said: The best of us in merit and the greatest of us in bounty. He said: Say your saying, or part of your saying; let not Satan allure you. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Suwayd ibn Amr and Abd al-Samad, from Mahdi. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad. Al-Nasai narrated it in the book of deeds of day and night from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, and from Humayd ibn Masadah, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, and from Harami ibn Yunus ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Mahdi ibn Maymun similarly."
"3379","Another. Abu Hamid Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit al-Baghdadi informed us there that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari reported to them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari reported to us, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kaysan reported to us, Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ismail al-Qadi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from his father: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who fasts the whole year. He said: He neither fasted nor broke fast."
"3380","Abu Jafar Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi reported to them while present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab reported to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He did not fast who fasts forever."
"3381","Abu Jafar also informed us that Fatimah reported to them, recited to her: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi and Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Adawi al-Basri said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah reported to us. Sulayman said: And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us (Ha). He said: And Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, both saying: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from his father who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so fasts perpetually. He said: He neither fasted nor broke fast. In the narration of Aban ibn Yazid: That it was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Hisham, Shubah, Said ibn Abi Arubah, Hammam ibn Yahya, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, al-Awzai and Aban ibn Yazid narrated it from Qatadah. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Affan, from Hammam; and from Yazid ibn Harun and others from Shubah; and from Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh from Said. Al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Hisham al-Harrani, from Makhlad ibn Yazid, from al-Awzai; and from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Abu Dawud, from Shubah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ubayd ibn Said; and from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Yazid and Abu Dawud, all of them from Shubah. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ubayd ibn Said, the uncle of Said ibn Yahya ibn Said, from Shubah. Muslim narrated for Abdullah a hadith from Hudbah, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from his father: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reciting: Rivalry has distracted you, the hadith."
"3382","Another. Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Jafar reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Humayd, meaning al-Tawil, narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from his father: That a man said: O Messenger of Allah, stray camels we come upon? He said: The stray of the Muslim is the burning of the Fire."
"3383","Abu Jafar Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Mutarrif, from his father: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The stray of the believer is the burning of the Fire."
"3384","Abu Jafar also informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad reported to them while present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a delegation of Banu Amir and said: O Messenger of Allah, we find stray camels. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The stray of the Muslim is the burning of the Fire. Al-Tabarani said: None narrates this hadith from Shubah except Ibn Mahdi. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Said. Ibn Majah brought it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, both from Yahya ibn Said. Al-Nasai also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, from Khalid, from Ashath, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mursal. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Khalifah, from Musaddad, from Yahya ibn Said."
"3385","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari said: Abu Hurayrah Muhammad ibn Firas al-Sayrafi narrated to us (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, both saying: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The likeness of the son of Adam, with ninety-nine deaths beside him: if the deaths miss him, he falls into old age until he dies. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Qatadah except Imran; Salm ibn Qutaybah is alone in it. I say: It has been narrated through Hajjaj ibn Hajjaj from Qatadah."
"3386","Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us at Isfahan that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has likened the son of Adam, with ninety-nine deaths of fate beside him; then if these miss him, old age is behind him. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Hurayrah Muhammad ibn Firas and said: A fair, strange hadith. I say: Imran al-Qattan was criticized by some and declared trustworthy by others, so he is a witness for others."
"3387","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Hani ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father who said: I was traveling and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was eating, and I was fasting. He said: Come and eat. I said: I am fasting. He said: Do you not know what Allah Almighty has lifted from the traveler? I said: And what has Allah lifted from the traveler? He said: Fasting and half the prayer. Al-Nasai narrated it from Abu Zurah, from Sahl ibn Bakkar."
"3388","Another. Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi informed us there that Abu al-Majd Maali ibn Hibatullah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Thalabi reported to them: Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini reported to us, Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Munir al-Khallal reported to us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh al-Naysaburi reported to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali ibn Sinan ibn Bahr al-Nasai reported to us, al-Hasan ibn Ahmad, who is al-Kirmani, reported to us, Ibrahim, who is Ibn Hajjaj, narrated to us, Hammad, who is Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abi al-Ala, from Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he wore a new garment would say: O Allah, I ask You of its good and the good of what it was made for, and I seek refuge with You from its evil and the evil of what it was made for. Thus al-Nasai narrated it in the book of deeds of day and night. Ibn al-Mubarak, Isa ibn Yunus and Abu Usamah narrated it from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri."
"3389","Another. Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from al-Thawri, from al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinks, and it was said: They are unavoidable. He said: Drink what does not befool your minds nor consume your wealth."
"3390","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad reported to them while present: Abu Nuaym reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad reported to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq reported to us, from Mamar, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abi al-Ala ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Anas ibn Malik."
"3391","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad reported to us, Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Sayyar Abu al-Hakam narrated to us, saying: I heard Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrating from his father: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Allah, let me enjoy my hearing and my sight, and make them the inheritors from me."
"3392","Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah ibn Malik ibn Amir ibn Rabiah ibn Hajar ibn Salaman ibn Malik ibn Rabiah ibn Rufaydah ibn Anz ibn Wail ibn Qasid ibn Wahb, ally of Banu Adi, Abu Muhammad, may Allah be pleased with him. Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Saqqar informed us at Nishapur that Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad reported to them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Hamdun the merchant reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sharqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Ibn Ajlan narrated to me (Ha). And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Ziyad, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Amir, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah that he heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to my mother while I was a boy, and I turned away going out, so my mother called me: O Abdullah, come, take. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What will you give him? She said: I will give him dates. He said: Indeed, had you not done it, a lie would have been written against you. The wording is one. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hashim ibn al-Qasim. Abu Dawud narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Said, both from al-Layth ibn Sad, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from the freedman of Abdullah ibn Amir, from Abdullah ibn Amir. Al-Layth did not name Ziyad, and Yahya ibn Ayyub named him."
"3393","Abdullah ibn Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim, the Hashimi, Abu al-Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. Ibrahim ibn Ikrimah ibn Yala ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas. Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi reported to us that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim reported to them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman reported to us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh reported to us, Abu Amr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Adam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Ibrahim ibn Ikrimah ibn Yala ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: And he is a burden upon his master; wherever he directs him he brings no good; is he equal to one who commands justice: that he is Uthman ibn Affan, and the one who is a burden upon his master, he said: was a freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, who disliked Islam, while Uthman would spend on him."
"3394","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Mabad ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas. Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us that Abu al-Fath Muflih ibn Ahmad al-Dumi reported to them: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib reported to us, Abu Umar al-Qasim ibn Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Hashimi reported to us, Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lului reported to us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashab al-Sijistani narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Wuhayb, meaning Ibn Khalid, narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abdullah ibn Mabad ibn al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Asking is to raise your hands level with your shoulders or near them; seeking forgiveness is to point with one finger; and earnest supplication is to stretch both your hands."
"3395","With the same chain Abu Dawud reported to us: Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abbas ibn Abdullah ibn Mabad ibn Abbas narrated to me this hadith, saying in it: And earnest supplication is thus, and he raised his hands and made their backs toward his face."
"3396","With the same chain Abu Dawud reported to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Abdullah ibn Mabad ibn Abbas, from his brother Ibrahim ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned similar."
"3397","Ibrahim ibn Abi Khidash, from Ibn Abbas. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Khidash narrated to me that Ibn Abbas said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) overlooked the graveyard, which was on his first route, he gestured with his hand beyond al-Saghirah, or he said: beyond al-Dafirah, Abd al-Razzaq doubted, and said: What a fine graveyard this is. I said to the one informing me: Did he single out al-Shib? He said: Like this. He said: He did not inform me that he singled out anything except that he gestured with his hand beyond al-Saghirah or al-Dafirah. And we used to hear that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) singled out al-Shib facing the House. The wording is that of Imam Ahmad. The narration of al-Dabari is similar, and in it there is no doubt of Abd al-Razzaq."
"3398","Arbad, and it is said: Arbidah al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali reported to us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, who is Ibn Mahdi, narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be seen when he prostrated."
"3399","Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas who said: I pondered the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him spreading apart, and I saw the whiteness of his armpits."
"3400","With the same chain my father narrated to me: Ishaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated, the whiteness of his armpit would be seen while prostrating."
"3401","Abu Jafar Muhammad reported to us that Abu Ali al-Haddad reported to them while present: Abu Nuaym reported to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar reported to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq who said: I heard al-Tamimi narrating from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the whiteness of the armpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while prostrating."
"3402","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad reported to them while present: Abu Nuaym reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq reported to us, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would appear when he prostrated."
"3403","Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us that Abu al-Badr Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi reported to them: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib reported to us, al-Qasim ibn Jafar reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lului reported to us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufayli narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Tamimi, who used to narrate tafsir, from Ibn Abbas who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind and saw the whiteness of his armpits while he was spreading apart, having separated his hands. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq; and from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi; and similarly to the narration of Zuhayr from Husayn, from Abu Waki, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas who said: I faced the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw the whiteness of his armpit while prostrating. And he narrated it from Aswad ibn Amir, from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq with his chain: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating spreading apart until I saw the whiteness of his armpits. And he narrated it from Hajjaj, from Sharik similarly; and from Waki, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq similarly. It has a witness from the hadith of Abdullah."
"3404","Another. Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported to us, Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq (Ha). With the same chain Abu Yala reported to us: Zuhayr, who is Ibn Harb, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, who is Ibn Mahdi, narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (Ha)."
"3405","Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, and he mentioned something, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would use the siwak much until we thought, or we suspected, that it would be revealed upon him. The wording is that of Sufyan. The narration of Sharik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I have been commanded with the siwak until I thought that Quran or revelation would come down upon me concerning it."
"3406","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad reported to them while present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar reported to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the siwak and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept commanding us with it until we feared it would be revealed upon him concerning it. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun, from Sharik ibn Abdullah, without saying: or revelation. And he narrated it from Aswad ibn Amir, from Sharik, like the narration of Sharik except that in it: until I thought it would come down; the rest is similar. And he narrated it from Yahya ibn Adam, from Sharik, similarly. And he narrated it and the hadith before it from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, that he heard a man of Banu Tamim similarly."
"3407","Arqam ibn Shurahbil al-Awdi al-Kufi, brother of Huzayl, from Ibn Abbas. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Arqam ibn Shurahbil who said: I traveled with Ibn Abbas from Medina to Sham and asked him: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) make a bequest? He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill with the illness in which he died, he was in the house of Aishah. He said: Call Ali for me. She said: Shall we not call Abu Bakr, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Call him. Then Hafsah said: Shall we not call Umar? He said: Call him. Then Umm al-Fadl said: Shall we not call al-Abbas, your uncle? He said: Call him. When they were present he raised his head and did not see Ali, so he remained silent and did not speak. Umar said: Leave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had he a need from us he would have mentioned it, doing that three times. Then he said: Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer. Aishah said: Abu Bakr is present. Abu Bakr advanced leading the people in prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt some relief and came supported between two men. When the people perceived, they glorified Allah. Abu Bakr went to step back, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him with his hand: your place. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began from where Abu Bakr had reached in recitation, Abu Bakr standing and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting. Abu Bakr followed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people followed Abu Bakr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had hardly finished prayer before he became very heavy. He went out supported between two men, his feet dragging on the ground. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died without making a bequest."
"3408","Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Arqam ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill with the illness in which he died, he was in the house of Aishah. He said: Call Ali for me. Aishah said: Shall we not call Abu Bakr for you? He said: Call him. Hafsah said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we call Umar for you? He said: Call him. Umm al-Fadl said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we call al-Abbas for you? He said: Call him. When they gathered he raised his head and did not see Ali, so he remained silent. Umar said: Leave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Bilal came to announce prayer. He said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Aishah said: Abu Bakr is a man overcome, and whenever people do not see you they weep; had you commanded Umar to lead the people in prayer. Abu Bakr went out and led the people in prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt some relief and came out supported between two men, his feet dragging on the ground. When the people saw him they glorified Allah for Abu Bakr. He went to step back, and he gestured to him, meaning: your place. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and sat. Abu Bakr stood on his right. Abu Bakr would follow the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people would follow Abu Bakr. Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took up recitation from where Abu Bakr had reached, and died in that illness of his, peace be upon him. Waki once said: Abu Bakr would follow the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people would follow Abu Bakr."
"3409","With the same chain my father narrated to me: Hajjaj narrated to us, Israil reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Arqam ibn Shurahbil who said: I traveled with Ibn Abbas from Medina to Sham and asked him: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) make a bequest? He mentioned its meaning, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had hardly finished prayer before he became very heavy. He went out supported between two men, his feet dragging on the ground. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died without making a bequest. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, abridged. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad, from Waki, similarly. Our shaykh Abu al-Faraj Ibn al-Jawzi said: al-Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam, saying: the name of Abu Arqam is Shurahbil. Al-Bukhari said: unknown. He erred in what he said, for al-Bukhari and others made them two persons; Ibn Shurahbil was narrated from by more than one, while the unknown one is Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam, from whom only one man narrated, and none said the name of Abu Arqam is Shurahbil. I think our shaykh thought that because both narrate from Ibn Abbas, and Allah knows best. Abu Zurah said: al-Arqam ibn Shurahbil is trustworthy."
"3410","Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kinanah al-Madani, from Ibn Abbas. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kinanah, from his father who said: A commander among the commanders sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about prayer at istisqa. Ibn Abbas said: What prevented him from asking me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out humble, shabby, fearful, deliberate, supplicating, and prayed two rakahs as he prays at Eid, without delivering a sermon like these sermons of yours."
"3411","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ismail ibn Rabiah ibn Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kinanah, of Banu Amir ibn Luayy, narrated to us that he heard his grandfather Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn Abdullah narrating, from his father Ishaq ibn Abdullah, that al-Walid ibn Utbah sent him to Abdullah ibn Abbas saying: O son of my brother, ask him how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did at istisqa on the day he sought rain with the people. Ishaq said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas and said: O Abu Abbas, how did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do at istisqa on the day he sought rain? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out fearful, shabby, and did in it as he did at Fitr and Adha."
"3412","With the same chain Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kinanah, from his father who said: A commander among the commanders sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about istisqa. He said: Who sent you? I said: So-and-so. He said: What prevented him from coming to me and asking me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out humble, supplicating, shabby, did not deliver a sermon like this sermon of yours, and prayed two rakahs as he prays at Eid."
"3413","Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Adib reported to them: Ibrahim reported to us, Muhammad reported to us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan say: Hisham ibn Abdullah ibn Kinanah narrated to me, from his father who said: A commander among the commanders sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about the istisqa prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out renouncing, humble, supplicating, or humble, without delivering a sermon like this sermon of yours, and prayed two rakahs as he prays at Eid. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Nufayli and Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Hatim ibn Ismail, from Hisham ibn Ishaq, from his father. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Said, from Hatim, and said: A fair, sound hadith; and from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Waki. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Mansur and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Hisham ibn Abdullah, from his father, saying similarly; and from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Muhammad, from Hatim, from Hisham ibn Ishaq; and from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Waki. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad and Muhammad ibn Ismail, from Waki, all similarly. Some named al-Walid, some said: a commander among the commanders. Abu Dawud said: Uthman said: al-Walid ibn Uqbah, and the correct is Utbah. Abu Awanah al-Isfarayini narrated it in his Sahih from Bakr ibn Sahl, from Abdullah ibn Yusuf with his chain, with: al-Walid ibn Utbah. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili, with: your sermons, and with: supplicating, humble."
"3414","Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abbas. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us at Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr at Cairo, that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had been married, and they asked him to judge stoning concerning them, so he stoned them in the courtyard of the mosque."
"3415","Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim reported to us, Muhammad reported to us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Rukanah, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had been married, and they asked him to judge concerning them, so he judged stoning concerning them, and they were stoned in the courtyard of the mosque among Banu Ghanm. When he felt the touch of stones he stood toward his companion and bent over her to shield her from the stones. Ibn Abbas said: Among what Allah did for His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was his standing bending over her. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Ibn Umar similarly."
"3416","Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Suddi, from Ibn Abbas. Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karaji reported to them: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khatib reported to us, al-Qasim ibn Jafar al-Hashimi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar reported to us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami narrated to us, Yunus, meaning Ibn Bukayr, narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made peace with the people of Najran for two thousand garments, half in Safar and the rest in Rajab, which they pay to the Muslims, and the loan of thirty coats of mail, thirty horses, thirty camels, and thirty of every kind of weapon with which they fight; the Muslims guarantee them until they return them to them if in Yemen there is plotting or treachery; on condition that no church of theirs is demolished, no priest of theirs expelled, nor are they turned from their religion so long as they do not innovate or consume riba. Ismail said: They have consumed riba. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it. Ismail and Asbat, Muslim narrated for them in his Sahih, though reports differed about their trustworthiness or criticism."
"3417","Barakah ibn Uryan Abu al-Walid al-Mujashii al-Basri, from Ibn Abbas. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Musa, who is Ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Khalid, from Barakah Abi al-Walid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting behind the Maqam, raised his head to the sky, looked a while, then said: May Allah destroy the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, yet they sold them and ate their prices. Allah Almighty has not forbidden anything to a people except that He has forbidden its price to them."
"3418","Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi reported to them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal reported to us, Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq reported to us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, Barakah ibn al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Ibn Abbas narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was facing the Stone, raised his head to the sky and said: May Allah curse the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, yet they sold them and ate their prices. When Allah forbids a thing to a people, He forbids its price to them."
"3419","Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Surayj narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha reported to us, from Barakah ibn Uryan al-Mujashii who said: I heard Ibn Abbas narrating, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, yet they sold them and ate their prices. When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, forbids eating a thing, He forbids its price."
"3420","With the same chain my father narrated to me: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Barakah Abi al-Walid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: May Allah curse the Jews; Allah forbade them fats, yet they sold them and ate their prices. When Allah Almighty forbids a thing to a people, He forbids its price to them. Ali ibn Asim, we brought him for consideration. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hushaym and Ali ibn Asim, from Khalid. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal and Khalid ibn Abdullah, from Khalid al-Hadhdha similarly. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah."
"3421","Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Ibn Abbas. Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi informed us at Cairo that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad reported to them: Muhammad Shaykh ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii reported to us, Ishaq ibn al-Hasan ibn Maymun al-Harbi reported to us, Abu Hudhayfah Musa al-Nahdi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Said al-Thawri narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Ibn Abbas who said: Rafath is touching, ifda is covering, and limas is intercourse, but Allah Almighty uses euphemism."
"3422","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us at Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr at Cairo, that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended Hajj, and a woman said to her husband: Take me for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I have nothing with which to take you for Hajj. She said: Take me for Hajj upon your camel so-and-so. He said: That is confined in the path of Allah. She said: Take me for Hajj upon your water-camel. He said: That you and I take turns upon. She said: Then sell your fruit. He said: That is my provision and yours. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived, she sent her husband to him, saying: Convey to him peace and the mercy of Allah, and ask him what equals a Hajj with him? He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife conveys to you peace and the mercy of Allah, and she had asked me for Hajj with you. I said: I have nothing with which to take you for Hajj. She said: Take me for Hajj upon your camel so-and-so. I said: That is confined in the path of Allah. He said: Had you taken her for Hajj upon it, it would have been in the path of Allah. She said: Then take me for Hajj upon your water-camel. I said: That you and I take turns upon. She said: Then sell your fruit. I said: That is my provision and yours. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at her eagerness for Hajj. He said: She commanded me to ask you what suffices for a Hajj with you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Convey to her peace and the mercy of Allah, and tell her that an Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj with me. Abu Dawud narrated it similarly from Musaddad. It is narrated in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a woman of the Ansar called Umm Sinan: What prevented you from performing Hajj with us? She said: Two water-camels belonged to Abu so-and-so, her husband; he and his son performed Hajj upon one of them, and the other watered land of ours. He said: An Umrah in Ramadan fulfills a Hajj, or: a Hajj with me. In the narration of al-Bukhari: An Umrah in it equals a Hajj. In the hadith we mentioned is what is not in this one."
"3423","Thabit ibn Yazid al-Khawlani, from Ibn Abbas. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us there that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Tahir ibn Isa ibn Qayras al-Misri narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh, al-Layth ibn Sad and Ibn Lahiah informed me, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Thabit ibn Yazid al-Khawlani who reported to him: That he came to Medina and met Ibn Abbas and asked him about wine. He said: I shall tell you about wine. I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque; while he was sitting with knees drawn up, he released his sitting posture, then said: Whoever has any wine with him, let him inform me of it. People began coming to him; one saying: I have a skin of wine; another saying: I have a skin; another saying: I have skins; and whatever Allah willed one had. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather it at Baqi so-and-so, then inform me. They did, then informed him. He stood, and I stood with him. I walked on his right while he leaned on me. Abu Bakr caught up with us, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me and placed me on his left and placed Abu Bakr in my place. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab caught up with us, and he took him and placed him on his left, walking between them. When he stood over the wine he said to the people: Do you know this? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, this is wine. He said: You spoke the truth. Allah has cursed wine, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its drinker, its server, and the eater of its price. Then he called for a knife and said: Sharpen it. They did. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and tore the skins. People said: In these skins there is benefit. He said: Yes, but I do so in anger for Allah because of what is in it of His displeasure. He said: Some add over others in the hadith. Khalid ibn Yazid is the freedman of Ibn Abi al-Subaygh al-Iskandarani al-Misri, freedman of Banu Jumah; Abu Zurah al-Razi declared him trustworthy."
"3424","Jabir ibn Zayd al-Azdi Abu al-Shatha al-Basri, from Ibn Abbas. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik reported to them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali reported to us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya, who is Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us, saying: I heard Jabir ibn Zayd narrating from Ibn Abbas, Yahya said: None raised it except Shubah, saying: A menstruating woman and a dog cut off prayer."
"3425","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, Shubah raising it, who said: A black dog and a menstruating woman cut off prayer. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, saying: Said, Hisham and Hammam stopped it from Qatadah. Al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Ali, from Yahya, from Shubah and Hisham. Yahya said: Shubah raised it. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Yahya, from Shubah. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Hashim al-Tusi, from Yahya ibn Said."
"3426","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us at Isfahan, and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr at Cairo, that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abi al-Anbas, from Abi al-Shatha, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the ransom of the people of Badr four hundred. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi, from Sufyan ibn Habib. Al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Mansur al-Nasai, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak. Abu al-Anbas, al-Hakim did not name him in al-Kuna."
"3427","Another. Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur, who is al-Tusi, narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi al-Shatha, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every division divided is upon what was divided, and every division Islam meets is upon what was divided. Abu Dawud narrated it from Hajjaj ibn Abi Yaqub. Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Abbas ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib, both from Musa ibn Dawud."
"3428","Another. Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi reported to them: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khatib reported to us, al-Qasim ibn Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar reported to us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Subayh narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Sharik al-Makki, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi al-Shatha, from Ibn Abbas who said: The people of Jahiliyyah would eat some things and leave some out of disgust. Allah sent His Prophet and revealed His Book, made lawful His lawful and forbade His forbidden. What He made lawful is lawful, what He forbade is forbidden, and what He was silent about is pardon. And he recited: Say: I do not find in what is revealed to me forbidden, to the end of the verse. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan."
"3429","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya and al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Bistam al-Zafarani said: Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Mani narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prostitutes are those who marry themselves off without evidence. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Yusuf ibn Hammad, saying: Yusuf said: Abd al-Ala raised this hadith in Tafsir and stopped it in the book of divorce without raising it. He also narrated it from Qutaybah, from Ghundar, from Shubah, correctly Said, without raising it, saying: This is more correct, and it is not raised; we know none who raised it except what is narrated from Abd al-Ala."
"3430","Another. With the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us: Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Mansur informed me, Mubashshir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Yala ibn Muslim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were emigrants because they left the polytheists; and some of the Ansar were emigrants because Medina was a land to come to, and they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of al-Aqabah. Thus al-Nasai narrated it."
"3431","Another. With the same chain Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us: Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Yala ibn Muslim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between al-Zubayr and Ibn Masud."
"3432","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad reported to them, recited to him while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar reported to us, Ismail ibn Abdullah reported to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Yala ibn Muslim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between al-Zubayr and Ibn Masud."
"3433","Jafar ibn Ayyash, from Ibn Abbas. Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar, narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Ayyash, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gabriel came to me and commanded me to proclaim the talbiyah aloud. Jafar ibn Ayyash: Ibn Abi Hatim did not mention him in his book."
"3434","Habib ibn Abi Thabit ibn Qays ibn Dinar al-Kufi, Abu Yahya, from Ibn Abbas. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us: That Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Husayn, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I have come to you from people for whom no shepherd provides and no stallion neighs for them. He ascended the pulpit, praised Allah, then said: O Allah, give us a rescuing, fertile, abundant, comprehensive, immediate rain, not delayed. Then he descended. None comes to us from any direction except saying: We have been revived."
"3435","Abu al-Muzaffar Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Samani informed us that Abu al-Barakat Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Farawi reported to them: Abu Amr Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Mahmi reported to us, Abu Nuaym Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan al-Mihrajani reported to us, Abu Awanah Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Isfarayini reported to us, Abu al-Ahwas the judge of Ukbara and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to me, both saying: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Ayyash who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you from people for whom no shepherd provides, and no stallion neighs for them. He ascended the pulpit, praised Allah, then said: O Allah, give us a rescuing, fertile, wholesome, comprehensive, abundant, immediate rain, not delayed. Then he descended. None comes to him from any direction except saying: We have been revived. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad ibn al-Haytham the judge of Ukbara. Abu Awanah likewise brought it in his Sahih."
"3436","Another. Abu Jafar ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army, and its banner was repelled; then he sent, and it was repelled; then he sent, and it was repelled because of misappropriation of a gazelle head of gold. Then it was revealed: It is not for a Prophet to misappropriate."
"3437","Hafiz Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja ibn al-Fadl informed us at Isfahan that Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi reported to them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani reported to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh reported to us, Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Hammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib: A Prophet among the Prophets sent an army, and its banner was repelled three times because of misappropriation of a gazelle head of gold. Then it was revealed: It is not for a Prophet to misappropriate. Al-Hadrami said: Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated it to me in two places, one thus, and in the other place: Habib from Ibn Abbas."
"3438","With the same chain Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa reported to us: Umar ibn Jafar al-Warraq narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Prophet sent an army, and he mentioned similar."
"3439","Another. Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Said al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, my father died; shall I free a slave on his behalf? He said: Yes."
"3440","Husayn ibn Jundub al-Janbi Abu Zibyan al-Kufi, from Ibn Abbas. Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two qiblahs are not proper in one land, and no jizyah is upon a Muslim."
"3441","Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi reported to them, by ijazah if not hearing: Ibn Abi al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Numan reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two qiblahs are not proper in one land, and no jizyah is upon a Muslim. Imam Ahmad also heard it from Aswad ibn Amir, from Jafar al-Ahmar, from Qabus with his chain: Two qiblahs are not proper in one city, and no jizyah is upon the Muslims. Abu Dawud narrated: Two qiblahs do not exist in one town, from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Ataki, from Jarir. And he narrated: No jizyah is upon a Muslim, from Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah al-Qahastani, from Jarir. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it complete from Yahya ibn Aktham and Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala, from Jarir, saying: It is narrated from Qabus, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mursal."
"3442","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Good guidance and good demeanor are one part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"3443","Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan narrated to us, that his father narrated to him, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Zuhayr said: There is no doubt in it, saying: Good guidance, good demeanor and moderation are one part of twenty-five parts of prophethood."
"3444","With the same chain my father narrated to me: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr and Jafar, meaning al-Ahmar, narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good demeanor, and he mentioned similar."
"3445","Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim reported to us, Muhammad reported to us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr, who is Ibn Harb, narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan narrated to me, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good guidance, good demeanor and moderation are one part of twenty-five parts of prophethood. Abu Dawud brought it from Abu Jafar al-Nufayli, from Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah, like the hadith of the narration of Imam Ahmad from his two shaykhs."
"3446","Another. Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi reported to them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal reported to us, Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq reported to us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Mecca, then he was commanded with emigration, and it was revealed upon him: And say: My Lord, admit me a sound admission and bring me out a sound bringing, and grant me from Yourself a helping authority."
"3447","Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik reported to them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Mecca and was commanded with emigration, and it was revealed upon him: And say: My Lord, admit me a sound admission and bring me out a sound bringing, and grant me from Yourself a helping authority. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Jarir similarly. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani, saying: A fair, sound hadith."
"3448","Another. Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Maqdisi informed us that Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi reported to them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq reported to us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He in whose belly there is nothing of the Quran is like a ruined house."
"3449","Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The man in whose belly there is nothing of the Quran is like a ruined house."
"3450","Abu Ahmad Abdullah al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He in whose belly there is nothing of the Quran is like a ruined house. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani, saying: A fair, sound hadith."
"3451","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi said: Ibn al-Isbahani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: By what do I know that you are the Messenger of Allah? He said: What if I call this cluster from this palm, will you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. The cluster came down from the palm until it fell to the ground, hopping until it came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said to it: Return. It returned until it went back to its place. He said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, and he believed in him. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ismail, from Muhammad ibn Said al-Isbahani, saying: A fair, sound hadith."
"3452","Another. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, that his father narrated to him, saying: We said to Ibn Abbas: What of the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: Allah has not made for a man two hearts in his belly, what is meant by that? He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood one day praying, and a thought crossed. The hypocrites who prayed with him said: Do you not see he has two hearts, a heart with you and a heart with them? Then Allah, Mighty and Exalted, revealed: Allah has not made for a man two hearts in his belly."
"3453","Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us (Ha). He said: And Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Khalid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, all saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, Qabus narrated to us that his father narrated to him, saying: We said to Ibn Abbas: What of the saying of Allah Almighty: Allah has not made for a man two hearts in his belly? He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood one day praying and a thought crossed. The hypocrites who prayed with him said: Do you not see that he has two hearts, a heart with you and a heart with them? Then Allah Almighty revealed: Allah has not made for a man two hearts in his belly. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi, from Said al-Harrani, from Zuhayr; and from Abd ibn Humayd, from Ahmad ibn Yunus, similarly, saying: A fair hadith."
"3454","Another. Abu Jafar also informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he passed by the graves at Medina and said: Peace be upon you, O people of the graves, believers and Muslims. I seek forgiveness from Allah for us and for you. You are our predecessors, and we follow."
"3455","Another. Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Saadat ibn Tirad informed us at Baghdad that Hafiz Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Nasir ibn Ali reported to them: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Saqr al-Anbari reported to us, Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Maymun ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ghaffar al-Sadafi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh reported to us, Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali reported to us, from Mutamir, from his father, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan who said: Ibn Abbas said to us: Which of the two readings do you read? We said: The reading of Abdullah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have the Quran presented to him every year once, and in the year in which he died it was presented to him twice. Abdullah witnessed what was abrogated. Thus al-Nasai narrated it in Fada il al-Quran."
"3456","Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi reported to us that al-Husayn al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan who said: Ibn Abbas said: Which of the two readings do you count the first reading? They said: The reading of Abdullah. He said: Your reading is the first reading, and the reading of Abdullah is the last reading. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have the Quran presented to him every Ramadan once; in the year in which he died it was presented to him twice. Abdullah witnessed it and witnessed what was abrogated of it and what was changed. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Fatimah bint the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the presentation of the Quran."
"3457","Another. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal reported to them: Ibrahim reported to us, Muhammad reported to us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came hastening while we were sitting, until his haste toward us startled us. When he reached us he greeted, then said: I came to you to tell you of Laylat al-Qadr, but I forgot it between me and you. Seek it in the last ten."
"3458","Abu Ahmad Abdullah al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ubaydah narrated to us, Qabus narrated to me, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them hastening, saying: Until his haste startled us. He said: When he reached us he said: I came hastening to tell you of Laylat al-Qadr, but I was made to forget it between me and you; seek it in the last ten of Ramadan. Yahya ibn Main narrated it from Jarir."
"3459","Another. Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib informed us that Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna reported to them: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari reported to us, Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Qatii reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any boy who performs Hajj then comes of age must perform another Hajj; any Bedouin who performs Hajj then emigrates must perform another Hajj; and any slave who performs Hajj then is freed must perform another Hajj."
"3460","Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Asadi informed us at Damascus that his grandfather al-Husayn reported to them: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Missisi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun ibn Musa reported to us, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any boy who performs Hajj before reaching puberty must perform another Hajj; and he mentioned the rest similarly."
"3461","Another. Abu Jafar Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you except that a companion from the devils has been assigned to him. They said: And you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, but Allah helped me against him, so he submitted."
"3462","Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik reported to them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is not one among you except that a companion from the devils has been assigned to him. They said: And you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, but Allah helped me against him, so he submitted. Imam Ahmad and his son Abdullah narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Jarir. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Abu al-Jad, from Ibn Masud, and from the hadith of Urwah, from Aishah bint Abi Bakr."
"3463","Another. Abu Tahir ibn al-Matush informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Qabus, that his father narrated to him, from Ibn Abbas who said: Two men with one need came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them spoke, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found a foul smell from his mouth. He said to him: Will you not use the siwak? He said: I do, but I have not eaten food for three days. He ordered a man to shelter him and fulfilled his need."
"3464","Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: Two men with one need came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them greeted, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found a foul smell from his mouth. He said to him: Do you not use the siwak? He said: I do, but I have not eaten food for three days. He ordered a man to host him and fulfilled his need."
"3465","Another. Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us, Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from laziness, old age, the trial of the chest, and the punishment of the grave."
"3466","Another. Abu Ahmad Abdullah al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from him, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father who said: Ibn Abbas narrated to us, saying: On the night the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night, he entered Paradise and heard a sound in its side. He said: O Gabriel, what is this? He said: This is Bilal the caller to prayer. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he came to the people: Bilal has succeeded; I saw for him such-and-such. He said: Musa met him and welcomed him, saying: Welcome to the unlettered Prophet. He is a dark, tall man with lank hair at his ears or above them. He said: Who is this, O Gabriel? He said: This is Musa, peace be upon him. He said: He went on and a man met him and welcomed him. He said: Who is this, O Gabriel? He said: This is Isa. He said: He went on and a venerable, awe-inspiring elder met him, welcomed him and greeted; all of them greeted him. He said: Who is this, O Gabriel? He said: This is your father Ibrahim. He said: He looked into the Fire and saw people eating carrion. He said: Who are these, O Gabriel? He said: These are those who eat the flesh of people. And he saw a red, blue-eyed, curly-haired, disheveled man when you see him. He said: Who is this, O Gabriel? He said: This is the hamstringer of the she-camel. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered al-Masjid al-Aqsa he stood praying, then turned and all the Prophets were praying with him. When he finished, two cups were brought, one on the right and one on the left, in one milk and in the other honey. He took the milk and drank from it. The one with whom the cup was said: You have hit the natural way."
"3467","Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja reported to them, by ijazah if not hearing: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, Ibn Abbas narrated to us, saying: He said on the night the Prophet of Allah was taken, correctly: with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he entered Paradise and heard a sound in its side. He said: O Gabriel, who is this? He said: This is Bilal the caller to prayer. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he came to the people: Bilal has succeeded; I saw for him such-and-such. It is narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Abbas: the meeting of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the Prophets and their description. It is narrated in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Abu Zurah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Bilal at the dawn prayer: O Bilal, tell me of the most hopeful deed you did with me in Islam in benefit; for I heard tonight the rustle of your sandals before me in Paradise, the hadith."
"3468","Another. Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who plunders, robs, or points to plunder. Abu Kudaynah is Yahya ibn al-Muhallab."
"3469","Another. With the same chain Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us: Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The women said: O Messenger of Allah, why does he mention believing men and not mention believing women? Then it was revealed: The Muslim men and the Muslim women, the believing men and the believing women."
"3470","Another. al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us that Hibatullah reported to them: al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man of Banu Amir came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, show me the seal between your shoulders, for I am among the most skilled of people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Shall I not show you a sign? He said: Yes. He looked at a palm tree and said: Call that cluster. He called it, and it came hopping until it stood before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to it: Return. It returned to its place. The Amiri said: O family of Banu Amir, I have never seen a man more magical than today."
"3471","Another. Abu Jafar informed us that Fatimah reported to them: Muhammad reported to us, Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Basri narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) part the thighs of al-Husayn and kiss his little private part. Muhammad ibn Humayd and al-Husayn ibn Isa narrated it from Jarir."
"3472","Another. With the same chain Sulayman al-Tabarani reported to us: Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had the beggar known what is in begging for him, he would not ask."
"3473","Another. With the same chain al-Tabarani reported to us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth narrated to us, al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas: And if there were a Quran by which mountains were moved, or the earth cut, or the dead spoken to. He said: They said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If it is as you say, show us our first elders among the dead that we may speak to them, and open for us these mountains, the mountains of Mecca which have hemmed us. Then it was revealed: And if there were a Quran by which mountains were moved, or the earth cut, or the dead spoken to. Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan: reports differed from Yahya ibn Main concerning him. Ibn Abi Maryam narrated, saying: I heard Yahya ibn Main say: Qabus is trustworthy, his hadith permissible. And it is narrated from Abdullah ibn Ahmad, saying: I asked Yahya ibn Main about Qabus and he said: Weak in hadith. And I asked my father about him and he said: People narrated from him. Ibn Adi mentioned him, narrating for him some hadiths we mentioned and others we did not mention, saying: His hadiths are close, and I hope there is no harm in him. I say: Al-Tirmidhi authenticated more than one hadith of his."
"3474","What Abu Zibyan Husayn ibn Jundub narrated from Ibn Abbas of tafsir; al-Bukhari narrated in the Sahih from his hadith, from Ibn Abbas: As We sent down upon the dividers. He said: They believed in part and disbelieved in part, the Jews and the Christians. And he narrated from the narration of Mujahid from him, likewise Ata ibn Abi Rabah, Ikrimah, Said ibn Jubayr and others from him, more than a little of tafsir. The venerable shaykh Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Shukr al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us, with my recitation to him at Isfahan, I said to him: Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus reported to you, recited to him while you heard: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani reported to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ali ibn Ismail ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Qabus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas His saying: And a party of the People of the Book said: Believe in what was sent down upon those who believe in the morning of the day, the verse. He said: They would be with them in the morning of the day, disputing with them and speaking to them; when evening came and prayer was due, they disbelieved in him and left them. Abu Kudaynah is Yahya ibn al-Muhallab al-Bajali al-Kufi; Yahya ibn Main declared him trustworthy. Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi Abu al-Walid: Abu Hatim al-Busti criticized him, though Muslim narrated for him in his Sahih, and Yahya ibn Main and Muslim declared him trustworthy; Yahya and Muslim know men better than Ibn Hibban, and Allah knows best."
"3475","Another. With the same chain Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa reported to us: Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Raja ibn Abdullah Abu Salih al-Saghani, who was a neighbor at Mecca until he died, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam al-Kufi narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which verse sent down from heaven was hardest upon you? He said: I was at Mina in the days of the season, and the polytheists of the Arabs and the riffraff gathered in the season. Gabriel came down upon me and said: O Messenger, convey what was sent down to you from your Lord; if you do not, you have not conveyed His message; Allah will protect you from people. I stood at al-Aqabah and called: O people, who will support me to convey the messages of my Lord, and for you is Paradise? O people, say: There is no god but Allah, and I am the Messenger of Allah to you; you will prosper or succeed, and for you is Paradise. No man, woman or child remained except throwing dust and stones at me, spitting in my face, saying: Liar, apostate. An opponent presented himself to me, saying: O Muhammad, if you are the Messenger of Allah, it is time for you to supplicate against them as Nuh supplicated against his people with destruction. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, guide my people, for they do not know, and help me against them that they answer me to Your obedience. Al-Abbas, his uncle, came and rescued him from them and drove them from him. Al-Amash said: By that the Banu al-Abbas boast; and he says concerning them it was revealed: You do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inclined to Abu Talib, and Allah willed Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam and Raja ibn Abdullah, Ibn Abi Hatim did not mention them in his book."
"3476","Another. With the same chain Ahmad ibn Musa reported to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Bishr al-Marthadi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, saying: Shubah reported to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas concerning His saying: Giving its produce every season. He said: Morning and evening."
"3477","Another. With the same chain Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh reported to us: Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Abdullah al-Basri reported to us, Abu Qilabah Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Raqqashi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: Allah did not send a Prophet except as a youth, nor was knowledge given except to a youth. And he recited: They said: We heard a youth mentioning them called Ibrahim. And he recited: When Musa said to his youth. And he recited: They were youths who believed in their Lord."
"3478","With the same chain Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa reported to us: Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: Allah did not send a Prophet except as a youth. He said: I think he recited: A youth mentioning them called Ibrahim. Ubayd ibn Ishaq we mentioned as a witness."
"3479","Another. Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Ahmad known as Ibn al-Saffar informed us, with my recitation to him at Nishapur, I said to him: The sister of your father Aishah bint Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Saffar reported to you, recited to her, it was said to her: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Khalaf al-Shirazi reported to you, recited to him: Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya reported to us, Abu al-Fadl al-Hasan ibn Yaqub ibn Yusuf al-Bukhari reported to us, Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Bukayr al-Absi narrated to us, saying: Waki ibn al-Jarrah ibn Malih ibn Adi ibn Faras al-Ruasi reported to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Abdullah ibn Abbas who said: There is nothing in Paradise of what is in this world except names."
"3480","Another. With the same chain, from Ibn Abbas that he used to read this word: So mention the name of Allah over them lined up, saying: Hobbles of three, saying: In the name of Allah, Allah is Greatest; O Allah, from You and to You. He said: He was asked about their skins with me? He said: We give them in charity or benefit from them."
"3481","Another with the same chain, from Ibn Abbas who said: The first thing Allah created of things was the Pen, and He said: Write. It said: My Lord, what shall I write? He said: Write the decree. He said: So it ran with what will be from that day until the Hour. He said: Then He created the Nun (whale) and spread the earth upon it, so the vapor of water rose and He split the heavens from it, and the Nun shook so the earth swayed, so it was made firm with the mountains; and the mountains are upon the earth until the Day of Resurrection. Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Marduwayh narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Bukayr."
"3482","Another (no. 9): Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Baqa al-Aquli informed us, by my reading to him in Baghdad - I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Sadaqah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Mihlaban informed you, by reading to him - it was said to him: Abu al-Husayn Asim ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Asim informed you: Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi al-Bazzaz informed us, Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn Ayyash informed us, Yahya - he is Ibn al-Sari - narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us from Qabus from his father from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (On the Day the sky will be like molten brass) (70:8): he said: Like the dregs of oil."
"3483","No. 10: Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us from Qabus from his father from Ibn Abbas who said: The last hardship the believer meets is death. And regarding His saying: (On the Day the sky will be like molten brass): he said: Like the dregs of oil. And regarding His saying: (in hours of the night): he said: The hollow (middle) of the night. And he said: Do you know what the departure of knowledge is? He said: It is the departure of the scholars from the earth."
"3484","Another (no. 11): Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Said al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us from Qabus from his father from Ibn Abbas who said: When Ibrahim (peace be upon him) finished building the House, it was said to him: Call the people to Hajj. He said: How will my voice reach? It was said: Call, and upon Me is the conveyance. So Ibrahim called out: O people, Hajj to the Ancient House has been prescribed upon you. So all between heaven and earth heard him; do you not see that people come for Hajj from the farthest land, chanting the talbiyah."
"3485","Hanash ibn Abdullah - also said Ibn Ali - al-Sabai al-Sanani from Ibn Abbas. No. 12: Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi and Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim informed us, by my reading to each of them in Isfahan - I said to them: Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading to him - he said: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa ibn Shammah informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn Zadham informed us, Muhammad ibn Zabban informed us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us - he said: al-Layth ibn Sad informed us from Qays ibn al-Hajjaj from Hanash ibn Abdullah from Ibn Abbas - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me as a riding companion one day and put his hand behind his back, and said: Boy, shall I not teach you words: Guard Allah, He will guard you; guard Allah, you will find Him before you; when you seek help, seek help from Allah; and when you ask, ask Allah; the pens have been lifted and the pages have dried; by the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if the nation strove to harm you they could not harm you except with something Allah has written against you."
"3486","No. 13: The imam Abu al-Jud Ghiyath ibn Faris ibn Makki al-Muqri informed us, by my reading to him in Cairo - I said to him: Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Rifaa ibn Ghadir al-Saadi al-Faradi informed you, by reading to him: Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Khilii informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Said al-Bazzaz informed us, Abu al-Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Musa Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sadafi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah and al-Layth ibn Sad informed me from Qays ibn al-Hajjaj from Hanash ibn Abdullah from Abdullah ibn Abbas who said: I rode behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day and he put his hand behind me, and said: Boy, shall I not teach you words by which Allah will benefit you: Guard Allah, He will guard you; guard Allah, you will find Him before you; when you seek help, seek help from Allah; and when you ask, ask Allah; the pens have been lifted and the pages have dried; if the nations strove to benefit you they could not benefit you except with something Allah has written for you, and if they strove to harm you they could not harm you except with something Allah has written against you. And Ibn Wahb added in the hadith of another than him: Draw near to Him in ease, He will draw you near in hardship; and know that in patience over what you dislike is much good, and that victory is with patience, and that relief is with distress, and that with hardship is ease."
"3487","No. 14: Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyub ibn Ali al-Harbi informed us there that Abu al-Izz Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Kadish informed them, by reading to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Banna informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yahya al-Sukkari informed us, Ismail al-Saffar narrated to us, Abbas al-Duri narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman - he is al-Muqri - narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid and Ibn Lahiah and Kahmas ibn al-Hasan and Hammam ibn Habib narrated to us - they said: Qays ibn al-Hajjaj al-Zarqi informed us from Hanash from Ibn Abbas - who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Boy, or: my son, shall I not teach you words by which Allah will benefit you? I said: Yes. He said: Guard Allah, He will guard you; guard Allah, you will find Him before you; know Him in ease, He will know you in hardship; when you ask, ask Allah; and when you seek help, seek help from Allah; the Pen has dried with what will be; so if all creation together intended to benefit you with something Allah has not decreed for you, they could not; and if they intended to harm you with something Allah has not decreed against you, they could not; act for Allah with gratitude and certainty; and know that patience over what you dislike is much good, and that victory is with patience, and that relief is with distress, and that with hardship is ease."
"3488","No. 15: Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim and Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Mihrabzadh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abu Shurayh informed me from Qays ibn al-Hajjaj from Hanash ibn Abdullah al-Sabai from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - while he was his riding companion: Boy, I shall tell you words: Guard Allah, He will guard you; guard Allah, you will find Him before you; when you ask, ask Allah; and when you seek help, seek help from Allah; the pens have dried and the pages have been lifted; by the One in whose Hand is my soul, if the nation intended to benefit you they could not benefit you except with something Allah has written for you, and if they intended to harm you they could not harm you except with something Allah has written for you. Abu Shurayh's name is Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh al-Misri al-Maafiri al-Iskandarani, among the men of the Sahih. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yunus from Layth in the manner of the hadith of Abu Shurayh. And from Yahya ibn Ishaq from Ibn Lahiah from Nafi ibn Yazid, and from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri from Ibn Lahiah from Nafi ibn Yazid from Qays ibn al-Hajjaj similarly. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, in his narration an abridgement similarly, from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Musa from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak from al-Layth and Ibn Lahiah, and from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu al-Walid from al-Layth ibn Sad, and he said: A hasan sahih hadith."
"3489","Rufay Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi al-Basri from Ibn Abbas. No. 16: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us from Qatadah from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas that a person cursed the wind, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse it, for it is commanded; and whoever curses a thing that does not deserve it, the curse falls upon him."
"3490","Nos. 17-18: Abu Jafar also informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while present: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Musab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Mabad informed us, Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abu al-Khattab Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us (hawala). And Abu Jafar also informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while present: Abu Dharr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Salihani informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Hammad narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas that a man cursed the wind, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse it, for it is commanded; and whoever curses a thing that does not deserve it, the curse returns upon him. Their wording is one, except that in the narration of Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad it is: for whoever curses."
"3491","No. 19: The imam Abu al-Futuh Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli, Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani, and Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh informed us of it in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Bishran al-Dirhami al-Basri narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Bishr ibn Imran al-Zahrani narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us from Qatadah from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas that a man cursed the wind in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse it, for it is commanded; and whoever curses a thing that does not deserve it, the curse returns to him. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Aban ibn Yazid. And he and al-Tirmidhi both narrated it from Zayd ibn Akhzam, and al-Tirmidhi said: Gharib, we know none who ascribed it (marfu) except Bishr. I say: except that Muslim ibn Ibrahim did not raise it, but only conveyed it to Abi al-Aliyah. That is, in some of its chains is one who was criticized, so it is a witness for others."
"3492","Another (no. 20): Abu Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, Awf informed us from Ziyad ibn Husayn from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the morning of Jam (Muzdalifah): Come, pick pebbles for me. So I picked for him pebbles like the pebbles of khadhf (small flung stones). When I placed them in his hand he said: Yes, with the likes of these; and beware of extremism in religion, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion."
"3493","No. 21: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Husayn from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the morning of al-Aqabah while upon his mount: Come, pick up. He said: So I picked up for him pebbles like the pebbles of khadhf. When I placed them in his hand he said: Yes, with the likes of these - three times - and beware of extremism, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion."
"3494","No. 22: Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak and Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Awf al-Arabi from Ziyad ibn Husayn from Abi al-Aliyah from Abdullah ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the morning of the jamrah: Come, pick for me. So I picked for him pebbles like the pebbles of khadhf. When I placed them in his hand he said: Yes, with the likes of these, yes with the likes of these, yes with the likes of these; and beware of extremism, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion."
"3495","No. 23: Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi and others informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Awf from Ziyad ibn al-Husayn from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand me pebbles. So I handed him like the pebbles of khadhf, and he kept moving them in his hand, saying: With the likes of these; and beware of extremism, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism. Al-Nasai narrated it in meaning from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi from Ibn Ulayyah from Awf, and from Abu Qudamah Ubayd Allah ibn Said from Yahya from Awf similarly. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad from Abu Usamah from Awf similarly. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan from Hibban from Ibn al-Mubarak."
"3496","Another (no. 24): Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from al-Amash from Ziyad ibn Husayn from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people shooting, and said: Shoot, O sons of Ismail, for your father was an archer."
"3497","No. 25: Abu Jafar Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from al-Amash from Ziyad ibn Husayn from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people shooting, and said: Shoot, O sons of Ismail, for your father was an archer."
"3498","No. 26: My maternal uncle the imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Qasim ibn Bishr al-Narsi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafii narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib ibn Harb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri informed us from al-Amash from Ziyad ibn al-Husayn from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon youths competing in shooting, and said: Shoot, O sons of Ismail, for your father was an archer. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya from Abd al-Razzaq."
"3499","Another (no. 27): Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding His saying: (And We made him a guidance for the Children of Israel) (32:23): he said: Musa was made a guidance for the Children of Israel; (So be not in doubt about meeting Him): he said: About Musa's meeting with his Lord, mighty and majestic."
"3500","No. 28: Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz known as Qafak informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Bukayr - of the people of Samarra - narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): So be not in doubt about Musa's meeting with the Children of Israel; (And We made him a guidance for the Children of Israel): he said: Musa was made a guidance for the Children of Israel."
"3501","No. 29: And with it, Abu Bakr ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Salih ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Abi al-Aliyah from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding His saying: (So be not in doubt about meeting Him): he said: About Musa's meeting with his Lord; and regarding His saying: (And We made him a guidance for the Children of Israel): he said: Meaning Musa, a guidance for the Children of Israel."
"3502","Zaidah ibn Umayr al-Tai from Ibn Abbas. No. 30: Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Zaidah ibn Umayr al-Tai narrated to us, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: What do you think about coitus interruptus (azl)? He said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said anything about it, it is as he said; otherwise I say about it: (Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish) (2:223): whoever wishes may practice azl and whoever wishes may leave it."
"3503","No. 31: The shaykh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Muaddib al-Tamimi informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Harun ibn Isa al-Baladi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, Adam narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Zaidah ibn Umayr al-Tai narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about azl? He said: About it was revealed this verse: (Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish)."
"3504","No. 32: And with it, Abu Bakr ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn informed us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Zaidah ibn Umayr al-Tai narrated to us, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: What do you think about azl? He said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said anything about it, it is as he said; otherwise I say about it by opinion: (Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish): so whoever wishes may practice azl and whoever wishes may leave it."
"3505","No. 33: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us that Said al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us from Zaidah ibn Umayr from Ibn Abbas who said: I said: What do you say and what do you think about azl? He said: If the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said anything about it, it is as he said; otherwise I say: (Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish): whoever wishes may practice azl, and whoever wishes may leave it."
"3506","Zurarah ibn Awfa al-Amiri from Ibn Abbas. No. 34: Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh al-Mani narrated to us, they said: Awf narrated to us from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken by night (Isra) and I woke in Makkah, I was distressed by my matter, and I knew the people would belie me, so I sat apart grieving. He said: The enemy of Allah Abu Jahl passed by him, came and sat with him, and said to him mockingly: Was there anything? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He said: What is it? He said: I was taken by night this night. He said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Then you woke among us? He said: Yes. He said: He did not show him that he belied him, fearing he would deny the account if he called his people to it. He said: What if I call your people, will you tell them what you told me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. So he said: Come, O company of Banu Kab ibn Luayy. He said: The gatherings broke up toward him and they came and sat with them. He said: Tell your people what you told me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was taken by night this night. They said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. They said: Then you woke among us? He said: Yes. He said: Some clapped and some placed his hand on his head, astonished at the lie, as he claimed. They said: Can you describe the mosque to us, and among the people were those who had traveled to that land and seen the mosque. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I went to describe it and kept describing until part of the description became confused to me. He said: The mosque was brought while I looked until it was placed before the house of Uqayl or Iqal, so I described it while looking at it. He said: The people said: As for the description, by Allah he is right."
"3507","No. 35: Abu Ali Diya ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Ali known as Ibn al-Khurayf informed us in Baghdad that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us by dictation: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan informed us, by reading to him while I listened: Bishr ibn Musa al-Asadi narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us from Zurarah ibn Awfa who said: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken by night and I woke in Makkah, I was distressed by my matter, and I knew the people would belie me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat apart grieving, and Abu Jahl passed by him, came and sat with him, and said to him mockingly: Was there anything? He said: Yes. He said: What is it? He said: I was taken by night this night. He said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Then you woke among us? He said: Yes. He said: He did not show him that he belied him, fearing he would deny the account if he called his people. And he said to him: Will you tell your people what you told me if I call them to you? He said: Yes. He said: Come, O company of Banu Kab. He said: The gatherings dispersed and they came and sat with them. He said: Tell your people what you told me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was taken by night this night. They said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. They said: Then you woke among us? He said: Yes. He said: Some clapped and some placed his hand on his head, laughing at what he reported, as he claimed. They said: Can you describe the mosque to us? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I went to describe it to them and kept describing until the description became confused to me. He said: The mosque was brought while I looked at it until it was placed before the house of Aqil or Iqal. He said: So I described it while looking. The people said: As for the description, by Allah he is right."
"3508","Nos. 36-37: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us (hawala). Al-Tabarani said: And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Muadhdhin narrated to us from Awf from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night and woke in Makkah, he sat apart grieving, and the enemy of Allah Abu Jahl came upon him and said mockingly: Was there anything? He said: Yes, I was taken by night this night to Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Then you woke among us? He said: Yes. He did not show him that he belied him, fearing if he called his people to it they would deny the account. He said: What if I call your people, will you tell them what you told me? He said: Yes. Abu Jahl said: O Banu Kab ibn Luayy, come. The gatherings dispersed until they sat with them. Abu Jahl said: Tell your people what you told me. He said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I was taken by night this night. He said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. They said: Then you woke among us? He said: Yes. Some clapped and some placed his hand on his head, marveling at the lie, as he claimed. Among the people were those who had traveled to that mosque and seen it. They said: Can you describe the mosque to us? He said: Yes. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I described it to them until part of the description became confused to me. He said: The mosque was brought while I looked at it until it was placed before the house of Aqil or Iqal, so I described it while looking at it. The people said: As for the description, by Allah he is right."
"3509","Zirr ibn Hubaysh al-Asadi Abu Maryam al-Kufi from Ibn Abbas. No. 38: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us in Isfahan - and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr in Cairo - that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Bishr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Asim from Zirr who said: Ibn Abbas said to me: Which of the two readings do you recite? I said: The latter. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, used to present the Quran to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan. He said: He presented the Quran to him in the year the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died twice, so Abdullah witnessed what was abrogated of it and what was changed, so Abdullah recited the latter. Something like it has preceded in the narration of Abu Zibyan from Ibn Abbas."
"3510","Another (no. 39): And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Asim from Zirr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (And was at a distance of two bow lengths or nearer) (53:9): he said: The qab (measure) is the qaid (fetter-length), and the two bows are the two cubits."
"3511","Salim ibn Abi al-Jad al-Ghatafani al-Kufi from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. No. 40: Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya al-Mujabbir al-Tamimi narrate from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Ibn Abbas that a man came to him and said: What about a man who killed a man deliberately? He said: (So his recompense is Hell, abiding therein, and Allah is angry with him and cursed him and prepared for him a great punishment) (4:93). He said: It was revealed among the last revealed; nothing abrogated it until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and no revelation came down after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What if he repented and believed and did righteous deeds then was guided? He said: How can repentance be his, when I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: May his mother be bereft of him, a man who killed a man deliberately will be brought on the Day of Resurrection holding his killer with his right or his left, and holding his head with his right or his left, his jugular veins gushing blood before the Throne, saying: My Lord, ask Your servant for what he killed me. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yunus from Abd al-Wahid from Yahya ibn Abdullah similarly, and from Abd al-Razzaq from Sufyan from Yahya similarly."
"3512","Nos. 41-42: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja ibn al-Fadl al-Isbahani informed us there that Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd informed us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Ammar al-Duhni and Yahya al-Jabir (hawala). Ibn Marduwayh said: And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Abu Mamar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Ammar al-Duhni and Yahya al-Jabir and Thabit al-Thumali, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ibn Abbas who said: It was said to him: What do you say about one who killed a believer deliberately then repented and believed and did righteous deeds then was guided? He said: How can he be guided; I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The slain will come on the Day of Resurrection clinging to the killer, his jugular veins gushing blood, until he says: My Lord, ask this one for what he killed me. Said ibn Mansur added: By Allah, nothing abrogated it after it was revealed: (And whoever kills a believer deliberately) (4:93) the verse. Al-Nasai narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Said, and Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, both from Sufyan similarly. It is mentioned in the two Sahihs from the narration of Said ibn Jubayr who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza ordered me to ask Ibn Abbas about these two verses: (And whoever kills a believer deliberately, his recompense is Hell); so I asked him, and he said: Nothing abrogated it; and about this verse: (And those who do not invoke another god with Allah nor kill the soul Allah forbade except by right) (25:68), he said: It was revealed about the people of shirk. There is no mention of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it, Allah knows best, as mentioned in the hadith of Salim we cited."
"3513","Another (no. 43): Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari and Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us, they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Aishah narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Ibn Abbas who said: A man of Banu Amir came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he used to treat and remedy, and said: O Muhammad, you say things; will you let me treat you? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him to Allah, then said: Will you let me show you a sign? And there were date-palms and a tree; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a cluster from it, and it came toward him prostrating and lifting its head until it reached him, and stood before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to it: Return to your place; so it returned to its place. Al-Amiri said: By Allah, I shall never belie you in any word ever; then he said: O family of Amir ibn Sasaa, by Allah, I shall never belie anything he says ever. Something like it has preceded in the narration of Abu Zibyan. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan from Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad similarly."
"3514","Those named Said from Ibn Abbas: Said ibn Jubayr Abu Abdullah, freedman of Walibah of Banu Asad, from Ibn Abbas; Ibrahim ibn Maysarah al-Taifi al-Makki from Said ibn Jubayr. Nos. 44-45: Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz and Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Muaddib al-Tamimi informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Ibrahim ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Sulayman narrated to us (hawala). Ibn Marduwayh said: And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Hamzah narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, they said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Muslim from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah from Said ibn Jubayr who said: Ibn Abbas said to his sons: O my sons, go out from Makkah on foot until you return to Makkah on foot; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The mounted pilgrim has for every step his mount takes seventy good deeds, and the walker has seven hundred good deeds of the Haram's good deeds. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the Haram's good deeds? He said: The good deed equals one hundred thousand good deeds. Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated it from Yahya ibn Sulaym from Muhammad ibn Muslim from Ismail ibn Umayyah from Said."
"3515","Ibrahim - not ascribed - from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 46: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Sultan al-Bayyi informed us in Baghdad that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Yusuf al-Urmawi informed them: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muslimah informed us, Abu Amr Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Adami informed us, Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Mighfar wrote to me: Yahya narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Sulayman from Ibrahim from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: (And complete the Hajj and Umrah) (2:196, to the House)."
"3516","Ismail ibn Umayyah from Said. No. 47: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi from Ismail ibn Umayyah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that he said to his sons: O my sons, go out from Makkah as pilgrims on foot; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The mounted pilgrim has for every step his mount takes seventy good deeds, and the walker has for every step he takes seven hundred good deeds. Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi: some imams criticized him, while Yahya ibn Main trusted him, and Muslim narrated from him. And Yahya ibn Sulaym: Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He is not used as proof, without clarifying the wound; while Yahya ibn Main trusted him, and al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated from him."
"3517","Ismail ibn Rashid al-Sulami from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 48: The shaykh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Shukr al-Tamimi and Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad known as Qafak al-Khabbaz informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman from Ismail ibn Rashid from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (Kaf-Ha-Ya-Ayn-Sad) (19:1), he said: Great, Guiding, Trustworthy, Mighty, Truthful."
"3518","Ashath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha - and the name of Abu al-Sha'tha is Sulaym - al-Muharibi al-Kufi from Said. No. 49: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from Ashath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah does not look at a musbil (one who trails his garment)."
"3519","No. 50: Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: Ibn al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Nasr and Hasan narrated to us, they said: Shayban narrated to us from Ashath: Said ibn Jubayr narrated to me from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, does not look at a musbil."
"3520","No. 51: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that his father Abu Mansur Ali informed them: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Sarifini informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us, Ali - he is Ibn al-Jad - narrated to us: Sharik informed us from al-Ashath from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah does not look at one who trails his izar. Al-Nasai narrated it from Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman from Husayn from Zaidah; and from Amr ibn Mansur from Adam from Shayban; and from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil from his grandfather from Shubah; all from Ashath from Said with it; and from Ahmad ibn Sulayman from Ubayd from Israil from Ashath from Said from Ibn Abbas as his saying (mawquf)."
"3521","Ayyub ibn Abi Tamimah - his name is Kaysan - al-Sakhtiyani from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 52: Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi and others informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Ayyub from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that he said: Regarding advance payment for habal al-habalah (the fetus of a fetus, sale of unborn camel offspring) is riba."
"3522","No. 53: And with it, my father narrated to me: Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us - from memory - from Ayyub from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade habal al-habalah."
"3523","No. 54: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us that his father informed them: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Hababah informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Ayyub from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Regarding advance payment for habal al-habalah is riba. Al-Baghawi said: Thus Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated this hadith from Shubah from Ayyub from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Uthman ibn Umar narrated it from Shubah from Ayyub who said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrate from Ibn Umar from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mentioning the like. No. 55: Abdullah said: And Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated it to me: Arim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Ayyub from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like, without doubt. He said: And Mamar, Wuhayb, Hammad ibn Salamah and Ibn Uyaynah narrated this hadith, all from Ayyub from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I say: It is possible Said ibn Jubayr preserved it from both, Allah knows best. Al-Nasai narrated it from Yahya ibn Hakim al-Muqawwim from Muhammad ibn Jafar."
"3524","Another (no. 56): Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Yahya al-Muaddib informed us that Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Tarrah informed them: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nammur informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us - by reading to him - while I listened; it was said to him: Abu Hamid Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Abdullah ibn Mayyah al-Hadrami narrated to you - by reading to him -: Yaqub ibn Ismail, he is Ibn Hammad, narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Said ibn Jubayr who said: I came to Ibn Abbas at Arafah while he ate pomegranate, and he said: Sit and eat, perhaps you are fasting; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fast this day. Imam Ahmad narrated it with the doubt of Ayyub."
"3525","No. 57: Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, he said: I do not know whether I heard it from Said ibn Jubayr or was informed of it from him, he said: I came upon Ibn Abbas at Arafah while he ate pomegranate, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke fast at Arafah, and Umm al-Fadl sent him milk and he drank it. Al-Nasai transmitted it from Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri from Sufyan with its chain, and from Ahmad ibn Harb from Ibn Ulayyah from Ayyub from Said similarly, in it: I brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) milk and he drank it. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, she is the mother of Abdullah ibn Abbas."
"3526","Another (no. 58): Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us in Isfahan that Umm Ibrahim Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Hamzah ibn al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us from his father from Ayyub from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued the talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Bakr ibn Khalaf from Hamzah ibn al-Harith. And al-Nasai narrated it from the narration of Hubayq ibn Abi Thabit from Said. Al-Harith ibn Umayr Abu Umayr: a resident of Makkah, of Ayyub's companions; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, Abu Usamah, Yala ibn Ubayd, al-Muammal ibn Ismail, Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii and his son Hamzah narrated from him; Abu Hatim al-Razi said that, and he, Yahya ibn Main and Abu Zurah al-Razi trusted him, saying: A righteous man."
"3527","Another (no. 59): The shaykh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ayyub who said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrate from Ibn Abbas that he recited {darasta} with an alif; he said: You studied (qara'ta)."
"3528","Bukayr ibn Shihab al-Makki - and he is not al-Damighani - from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 60: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Ijli narrated to us from Bukayr ibn Shihab from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: Jews came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim, we ask you about things; if you answer us in them we shall follow you and believe you and believe in you. He said: He took upon them what Israil took upon himself; they said: Allah is witness over what we say. They said: Tell us about the sign of the Prophet. He said: His eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep. They said: Tell us how the woman feminizes and how she masculinizes? He said: The two waters meet; if the woman's water prevails over the man's water she feminizes, and if the man's water prevails over the woman's water she masculinizes. They said: You are right. They said: Tell us about thunder, what is it? He said: An angel of the angels entrusted with the clouds directs it where Allah wills. They said: What is this sound heard? He said: The rebuke of the clouds when he drives it until it reaches where he was commanded. They said: You are right. They said: Tell us what Israil forbade upon himself? He said: He lived in the desert and complained, and found nothing suitable except camel meats and their milks; so he forbade them. They said: You are right. They said: Tell us about the one who comes to you of the angels, for no prophet is but an angel comes to him with message and revelation; who is your companion? Only this remains? He said: Jibril, peace be upon him. They said: He who descends with war and fighting, he is our enemy; if you said Mikail who descends with rain we would follow you. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: (Say: Whoever is an enemy to Jibril) (2:97) the verse."
"3529","No. 61: Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Ijli narrated to us - and he had a fine appearance we saw at Hasan - from Bukayr ibn Shihab from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim, we ask you about five things; if you tell us them we shall know you are a prophet and follow you. So he took upon them what Israil took upon his sons when they said: Allah is witness over what we say. He said: Ask. They said: Tell us about the sign of the Prophet. He said: His eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep. They said: Tell us how the woman feminizes and how she masculinizes? He said: The two waters meet; if the man's water prevails over the woman's water she masculinizes, and if the woman's water prevails over the man's water she feminizes. They said: Tell us what Israil forbade upon himself? He said: He complained of sciatica, and found nothing suitable except the milks of such-and-such; my father said: he said: some of them meaning camels, so he forbade their meats. They said: You are right. They said: Tell us about this thunder. He said: An angel of Allah's angels, mighty and majestic, entrusted with the clouds, in his hands - or in his hand - a mikhraq of fire with which he drives the clouds, leading it where Allah commanded him. They said: What is this sound heard? He said: His voice. They said: You are right. Only one remains, by which we shall follow you if you tell us: tell us, for no prophet is but an angel brings him good; tell us who is your companion? He said: Jibril, peace be upon him. They said: Jibril! He who descends with war, fighting and punishment, our enemy; if you said Mikail who descends with mercy, vegetation and rain it would be. So Allah revealed: (Whoever is an enemy to Jibril) (2:97) to the end of the verse. Al-Tirmidhi narrated from it the mention of thunder from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Nuaym, saying: A hasan gharib hadith. And al-Nasai narrated it in full from Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi from Abu Nuaym similarly."
"3530","Another (no. 62): Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah al-Sulami informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them by ijazah (hawala). No. 63: Our shaykh said: And Abu Bakr Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ghazzal informed us - by reading to him -: Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us, they said: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman, he is Ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani, narrated to us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Ijli narrated to us: Bukayr ibn Shihab narrated to me from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: I wish I had a man of Qadar and struck his head. They said: Why? He said: Because Allah, exalted, created a Preserved Tablet of white pearl, its two covers of red ruby, its pen light and its writing light, its width what is between heaven and earth; He looks into it every day three hundred and sixty looks; with each look He creates, gives life and death, honors and humbles, and does what He wills."
"3531","Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyah - and Abu Wahshiyah's name is Iyas al-Yashkuri Abu Bishr - from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 64: The shaykh Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Shukr al-Muaddib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Ashath ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Shubah from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas (hawala)."
"3532","No. 65: Ibn Marduwayh said: And Dalaj narrated to us: Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: A woman of the Ansar would be miqlat (whose children die) and vow upon herself that if a child lived she would make him Jewish; so when Banu al-Nadir were expelled, the Ansar said: What shall we do with our sons? So was revealed: (There is no compulsion in religion) (2:256). Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Umar al-Muqaddami from Ashath ibn Abdullah. And he and al-Nasai also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar from Ibn Abi Adi from Shubah. And al-Nasai narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali from Wahb ibn Jarir, and from Ibrahim ibn Yunus ibn Muhammad from Uthman ibn Umar from Shubah similarly. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim in Bust from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani from Wahb ibn Jarir similarly."
"3533","Another (no. 66): Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muammal narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said regarding the saying of the jinn: (And when the servant of Allah stood calling Him, they almost crowded upon him) (72:19): he said: When they saw him pray with his companions, praying his prayer, bowing with his bowing and prostrating with his prostration, they marveled at his companions' obedience to him; so when they returned to their people they said: When the servant of Allah - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - stood calling Him, they almost crowded upon him."
"3534","No. 67: Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Jarbadhqani informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them - by reading to him while present -: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: (And when the servant of Allah stood calling Him, they almost crowded upon him): he said: When the jinn came upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed with his companions, bowing with his bowing and prostrating with his prostration, they said: How obedient they are to him! So they returned to their people and said: (And when the servant of Allah stood calling Him, they almost crowded upon him). Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd ibn Humayd from Abu al-Walid from Abi Awanah similarly, saying: A sahih hadith."
"3535","Another (no. 68): Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us there that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Jafar ibn Iyas from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: They disliked giving small gifts to their relatives of the idolaters, so they asked and were permitted; so this verse was revealed: (Not upon you is their guidance, but Allah guides whom He wills; and whatever good you spend is for yourselves) (2:272) to His saying: (And you shall not be wronged)."
"3536","No. 69: The shaykh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Isam narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Jafar ibn Iyas from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: They disliked giving small gifts to their relatives while they were idolaters, so was revealed: (Not upon you is their guidance) until it reached: (And whatever good you spend, Allah knows it) (2:272-273). He said: So they were permitted. Al-Nasai narrated it similarly from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim from al-Firyabi. Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam: Ibn Adi criticized him. We transmitted it for consideration (itibar)."
"3537","Another (no. 70): And with it, Abu Bakr ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Hushaym from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The known days (al-ayyam al-malumat) are those before al-Tarwiyah, al-Tarwiyah and Arafah; and the numbered (al-madudat) are the days of tashriq."
"3538","Another (no. 71): Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us in Baghdad that Abu Mansur Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah, nephew of Mimi al-Daqqaq, informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Uthman - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us from al-Amash from Jafar ibn Iyas from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The people of Makkah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to make al-Safa gold for them, and to remove the mountains from them so they plant a garden; so it was said to him: If you wish, be patient with them, perhaps we shall draw some of them; and if you wish, give them what they asked, but if they disbelieve they shall be destroyed as those before them were destroyed. He said: Rather, I shall be patient with them. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed this verse: (And nothing prevented Us from sending the signs except that the former denied them; and We gave Thamud the she-camel as clear) (17:59); perhaps He shall draw some of them."
"3539","No. 72: Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and others informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us - and I heard it from him -: Jarir narrated to us from al-Amash from Jafar ibn Iyas from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The people of Makkah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to make al-Safa gold for them, and to remove the mountains from them so they cultivate; so it was said to him: If you wish, be patient with them; and if you wish, give them what they asked, but if they disbelieve they shall be destroyed as those before them were destroyed. He said: No; rather, I shall be patient with them. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: (And nothing prevented Us from sending the signs except that the former denied them; and We gave Thamud the she-camel as clear)."
"3540","Another (nos. 73-74): The shaykh Ismail ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Qattan informed us in Baghdad that Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah informed us, Umar ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Kattani narrated to us, Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili and Abu Abdullah ibn al-Ala narrated to us, they said: Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us (hawala). And Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Saqr al-Qurashi informed us in Damascus that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami al-Mawazini informed them - by reading to him in the year 511 - it was said to him: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd ibn Sadan al-Shahid informed you in Damascus, he said: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Rabii informed us, by reading to him: Abu al-Abbas Hajib ibn Arkin al-Farghani informed us - of what I read to him -: al-Dawraqis Ahmad and Yaqub narrated to us, they said: Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Report is not like seeing."
"3541","No. 75: Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Report is not like seeing."
"3542","No. 76: And with it, my father narrated to me: Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Report is not like seeing; Allah, exalted His praise, told Musa what his people did with the calf, and he did not cast the tablets; but when he saw what they did, he cast the tablets and they broke. It was said: Hushaym did not hear it from Abi Bishr, but heard it from Abi Awanah from him and concealed it (tadlis), Allah knows best. Al-Bukhari narrated: They are the People of the Book who divided it; believed in part and disbelieved in part; from Ziyad ibn Ayyub from Hushaym from Abi Bishr."
"3543","Another (no. 77): Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us: Abu Bishr said: He informed from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: When I take the two precious ones (eyes) of a servant and he is patient and seeks reward, I am not content with a reward for him less than Paradise. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abi Yala al-Mawsili from Ibrahim ibn Mahan. And likewise I saw it in an old copy from Abi Yala, while it is in the hearing of our shaykh Yaqub ibn Ibrahim... and I deem it an error, by proof of what follows:"
"3544","No. 78: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Mahan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: When I take the two precious ones (eyes) of My servant and he is patient and seeks reward, I am not content with a reward for him less than Paradise."
"3545","No. 79: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn ... al-Haddad informed them - by reading to him - while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Salih al-Nahhas narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Whose two beloved (eyes) I take and he is patient and seeks reward, I am not content with a reward for him less than Paradise. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Abi Bishr except Hushaym. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Anas ibn Malik."
"3546","Another (no. 80): Abu Tahir Muawiyah ibn Ali ibn Muawiyah al-Sufi and Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid known as al-Falji, both Isbahani - in their book - informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - by reading to him -: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Isbahani informed us, Abu al-Qasim Salman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hammad ibn Numayr narrated to us, my uncle Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us from Sufyan ibn Husayn from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed three on the day of Badr in custody: he killed al-Nadr ibn al-Harith of Banu Abd al-Dar, killed Tuaymah ibn Adi of Banu Nawfal, and killed Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Abi Bishr except Sufyan ibn Husayn; Husayn ibn Numayr is alone in it."
"3547","Another (no. 81): Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Harith Khuruust informed them while present: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Attar al-Muqri informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Hafiz narrated to us - in Safar 384 -: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated to us, Abu Ubayd Allah al-Makhzumi - he is Said ibn Abd al-Rahman - narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (And upon those who can bear it) (2:184): he said: It is the old man, and the pregnant in her month, and the nursing woman who fears for her child; they break fast and feed a poor person for each day, with no make-up upon them. Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni said: Ibn Uyaynah is alone in it from Ayyub. Al-Bukhari narrated from the narration of Amr ibn Dinar from Ata: he heard Ibn Abbas recite: (And upon those who can bear it, a ransom of food for a poor person). Ibn Abbas said: It is not abrogated; it is for the old man and the old woman who cannot fast, so they feed in place of each day a poor person. In what we narrated is the addition of the pregnant and nursing, and leaving the make-up."
"3548","Another (no. 82): Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Ijli narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said al-Zayyat narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that al-As ibn Wail took a bone from al-Batha and crumbled it in his hand, then said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Will Allah give this life after what I see? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, Allah shall make you die, then give you life, then admit you into Hellfire. So the verses at the end of Ya-Sin were revealed."
"3549","Another (nos. 83-84): And with it, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Junayd and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Hammad narrated to us: Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Abi Bishr (hawala). And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Mani narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr - I know it only - from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited al-Najm; when he reached: (Have you seen al-Lat and al-Uzza, and Manat the third, the other), Satan cast upon his tongue: those high cranes (al-gharaniq al-ula) and their intercession is hoped; when he reached its end he prostrated, and the Muslims and idolaters prostrated; so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: (And We sent before you no messenger or prophet but when he recited, Satan cast) (22:52) to His saying: (the punishment of a barren day) - the day of Badr. In Ibn Marduwayh's narration: and her intercession is hoped; at its end he said: the day of Badr; the rest alike."
"3550","No. 85: And with it, Ahmad ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Hammad narrated to us: Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr, I know it only from Ibn Abbas: A barren day - the day of Badr. Al-Bukhari narrated from the narration of Ayyub from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated by al-Najm, and with him prostrated the Muslims, idolaters, jinn and men."
"3551","Another (no. 86): And with it, Ahmad ibn Marduwayh informed us: Abu Amr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us: Adam narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Jafar ibn Iyas Abu Bishr narrated to us, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr say: A man said to Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (until you seek familiarity - tasta'nisu) (24:27); Ibn Abbas said to him: It is only tasta'dhinu (seek permission), and it is a slip of the book (copy)."
"3552","No. 87: And with it, Ahmad ibn Marduwayh informed us: Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (until you seek familiarity and greet its people): Ibn Abbas said: Seeking familiarity is seeking permission; in what I think, the scribes erred in it."
"3553","Another (no. 88): And with it, Ahmad ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Imran narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Bistam narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi and Ghundar both narrated to us from Shubah from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: (and honor him - tuazziruhu) (48:9): he said: Strike with him with the sword."
"3554","Another (no. 89): And with it, Ahmad ibn Marduwayh informed us: Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us from his book: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us: Bundar narrated to us: Ghundar narrated to us from Shubah from Hushaym from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (You shall be called to a people of mighty war) (48:16): he said: Hawazin and Banu Hanifah."
"3555","Another (no. 90): Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Zaybaqi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us: Ayyash ibn Ayyash ibn Ziyad al-Bahili narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding Allah's saying: Alif-Lam-Mim, Ha-Mim, Nun... he said: A discontinuous name."
"3556","Another (no. 91): And with it, Ahmad ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Ijli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us: Said ibn Shurahbil narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: (So if you are in doubt about what We sent down to you) (10:94): he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not doubt nor ask."
"3557","Another (no. 92): Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Muaddib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them while present: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: my father narrated to us: my father narrated to us from Shubah from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: This verse was revealed: (They are those who say: Do not spend upon those with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse) (63:7) about a hireling (asif) of Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"3558","Another (no. 93): Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh al-Hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Abi Bishr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding this word: (the king's cup - suwa al-malik) (12:72): he said: It was like a makkuuk (measure); and al-Abbas had the like of it in the Jahiliyyah, drinking in it."
"3559","Another (no. 94): And with it, Ahmad ibn Musa informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Farisi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari narrated to us: Husayn ibn Mansur narrated to us: Mubashshir ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us from Jafar ibn Iyas from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that he said regarding His saying: (Indeed We suffice you against the mockers) (15:95): he said: The mockers are al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth, al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib Abu Zamah, al-Harith ibn Antal, and al-As ibn Wail. He said: Jibril came to him and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained of them to him; so he showed him al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah and Jibril, peace be upon him, gestured to his ankle-vein (anjal); he said: What did you do? He said: He is sufficed. Then he showed him al-Aswad ibn Abd al-Muttalib and gestured to his eyes; he said: What did you do? He said: He is sufficed. Then he showed him al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth al-Zuhri and gestured to his head; he said: What did you do? He said: He is sufficed. Then he showed him al-Harith ibn Antal al-Sahmi and gestured to his belly; he said: What did you do? Then he said: He is sufficed. Then he showed him al-As ibn Wail and gestured to the sole of his foot; he said: What did you do? He said: He is sufficed. As for al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, a man of Khuzaah passed while feathering his arrow, and it struck his ankle-vein and cut it. As for al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib, he went blind; some say he went blind thus, and some say he alighted under a tree and kept saying: Will you not defend me, I am killed; they kept saying: We see nothing; he kept saying: O my sons, will you not defend me! Hud has perished; am I pierced by a thorn in my eye? They kept saying: We see nothing, and he remained so until his eyes went blind. As for al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth, sores came out on his head from which he died. As for al-Harith ibn Antal, yellow water seized him in his belly until his excrement came out of his mouth, and he died of it. As for al-As ibn Wail, while thus a thorny plant entered his feet until it filled from it, and he died of it."
"3560","Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah al-Qummi al-Khuzai from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 95: Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us: Jafar narrated to us from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am ruined. He said: What ruined you? He said: I turned my saddle (had intercourse from behind) last night, and he did not answer him anything; so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) this verse: (Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish) (2:223): he says: Come front and back, but avoid the anus and menstruation."
"3561","No. 96: Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me: Hasan narrated to us: Yaqub, meaning al-Qummi, narrated to us from Jafar from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined. He said: What ruined you? He said: I turned my saddle last night. He said: When he did not answer him anything, he said: This verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): (Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish): come front and back, and avoid the anus and menstruation. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd ibn Humayd from Hasan ibn Musa, saying: A hasan gharib hadith. And al-Nasai narrated it from Ali ibn Mabad ibn Nuh al-Baghdadi and Ahmad ibn al-Khalil, both from Yunus ibn Muhammad. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abi Yala al-Mawsili from Abi Khaythamah from Yunus ibn Muhammad from Yaqub al-Qummi similarly."
"3562","Another (nos. 97-99): Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Hafiz informed us: al-Qasim ibn Jafar al-Hashimi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar informed us: Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath al-Sijistani narrated to us: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jarjarai narrated to us: Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lengthened the recitation in the two rakahs after Maghrib until the people of the mosque dispersed. No. 98: Abu Dawud said: Nasr al-Mujaddar narrated it from Yaqub al-Qummi, ascribing it likewise: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba narrated to us: Nasr al-Mujaddar narrated to us from Yaqub the like. No. 99: Abu Dawud said: Ahmad ibn Yunus and Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Ataki narrated to us, they said: Yaqub narrated to us from Jafar from Said ibn Jubayr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in meaning; mursal. Abu Dawud said: I heard Muhammad ibn Humayd say: I heard Yaqub say: Everything I narrated to you from Jafar from Said ibn Jubayr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is musnad from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I say: Yahya al-Himmani narrated it from Yaqub al-Qummi and ascribed it."
"3563","Another: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai said: al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Yaqub al-Qummi from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not break fast on the white days (13th-15th) in travel nor residence. No. 100: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us of it that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not leave fasting the white days in travel nor residence. Ibrahim al-Sini and Muhammad ibn Uthman were both criticized; except that others narrated it, by proof of al-Nasai's narration."
"3564","Another (no. 101): Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, Iblis wailed a wail and his troops gathered to him; he said: Despair that the nation of Muhammad returns to shirk after this day of yours, but tempt them in their religion, and spread wailing among them."
"3565","No. 102: Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us from Jafar, meaning Ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, Iblis wailed a wail and his offspring gathered to him; he said: Despair that they return - the nation of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - to shirk after this day of yours; but spread in it - meaning Makkah - poetry and wailing."
"3566","Another (no. 103): And with it, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahib al-Harithi narrated to us: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man of the Ansar; when he neared his house he heard him speak inside; when he sought permission upon him he entered upon him and saw no one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I heard you speak to another. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I entered inside grieved by people's talk due to my fever, and there entered upon me one entering - I never saw a man more honorable in sitting nor finer in speech than him. He said: That is Jibril, peace be upon him; and among you are men, if one of them swore upon Allah He would fulfill him. In al-Bukhari from the hadith of Humayd from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among Allah's servants are those who, if they swore upon Him, He would fulfill him."
"3567","Another (no. 104): And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Fadl ibn Abi Rawh al-Basri narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us from Ashath ibn Ishaq from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): (Indeed Allah's allies, no fear upon them nor do they grieve) (10:62): he said: Allah is remembered by seeing them. Yahya ibn Yaman: more than one of the people of knowledge criticized him, while Yahya ibn Main trusted him, and Muslim narrated from him."
"3568","No. 105: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn ... informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Asim, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zayd, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Sabiq narrated to us: Yaqub al-Ashari narrated to us from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are Allah's allies? He said: Those who, when seen, Allah is remembered."
"3569","No. 106: Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us of it that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Adib, he is al-Kanjarudhi, informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Hafiz narrated to us by dictation: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Isbahani informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan ibn Abd al-Salam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Sabiq narrated to us from Yaqub al-Qummi from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Who are Allah's allies? He said: Those who, when seen, Allah is remembered."
"3570","Another (no. 107): Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Shukr al-Muaddib al-Tamimi informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Sad al-Dashtaki narrated to us: my father narrated to me from his father from Ashath ibn Ishaq from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israil said: O Musa, does your Lord dye? He said: Fear Allah. So his Lord called him: O Musa, they asked you, does your Lord dye? So say: Yes, I dye colors, the red, white and black; all colors are of My dye. So Allah revealed to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): (The dye of Allah; and who is better than Allah in dye?) (2:138)."
"3571","Another (no. 108): And with it, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu Said al-Dashtaki narrated to us: my father narrated to me: my father narrated to me from his father from Ashath ibn Ishaq from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The people of Jahiliyyah stood in the mawsim (gathering) and a man of them said: My father fed and bore burdens and bore blood-money; they had no mention but the deeds of their fathers. So Allah revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): (So remember Allah as you remember your fathers) (2:200), meaning their remembering their fathers in Jahiliyyah, (or with stronger remembrance)."
"3572","Another (no. 109): And with it, Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Said al-Dashtaki narrated to us: my father narrated to me: my father narrated to us from his father from al-Ashath from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: People of the Bedouins came to the standing place (mawqif) saying: O Allah, make it a year of rain, a year of fertility and a year of good birth; they mentioned nothing of the Hereafter. So Allah revealed about them: (So of people is he who says: Our Lord, give us in this world, and he has in the Hereafter no share) (2:200)."
"3573","Another (no. 110): And with it, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu Said al-Dashtaki narrated to us: my father narrated to me from his father from Ashath ibn Ishaq from Jafar from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Jews came to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Allah revealed: (Who is it that lends Allah a good loan?) (2:245); they said: O Muhammad, is your Lord poor? He asks His servants for a loan. So Allah revealed: (Allah has heard the saying of those who said: Allah is poor and we are rich) (3:181) to the end of the verse."
"3574","Another (no. 111): And with it, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dashtaki narrated to us: my father narrated to me from his father from Ashath ibn Ishaq from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israil asked Musa, peace be upon him: Does your Lord sleep? So take two glass bottles in your hand and stand the night. So Musa did; when two-thirds of the night passed he dozed and fell to his knees, then awoke and held them; when the end of the night came he dozed and the two bottles fell and broke. He said: O Musa, had I slept, the heavens would fall upon the earth and they would perish as the two bottles in your hand perished. So Allah revealed to His Prophet the verse of al-Kursi."
"3575","Another (no. 112): And with it, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu Said al-Dashtaki narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me: my father narrated to us from his father from Ashath from Jafar from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought cheap food and gave it in charity; so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): (O you who believe, spend of the good of what you earned) (2:267) to the end of the verse."
"3576","Another (no. 113): And with it, from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he ordered that charity be given only to the people of Islam until this verse was revealed: (Not upon you is their guidance, but Allah guides whom He wills) (2:272) to its end; then he ordered charity after it to everyone who asks you, of every religion."
"3577","Another (no. 114): And with it, Ahmad ibn Musa informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Qasim ibn Yahya ibn al-Mukharrimi narrated to us: Abu Hammam narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us from Ashath ibn Ishaq from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not give charity except to the people of your religion. He said: So Allah revealed: (Not upon you is their guidance, but Allah guides whom He wills) the verse."
"3578","Another (no. 115): Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja ibn al-Fadl al-Hafiz al-Isbahani informed us there that Masud ibn al-Hasanah al-Thaqafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu Said al-Dashtaki narrated to us: my father narrated to me: my father narrated to us from his father from Ashath from Jafar from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (And do not wish for what Allah favored some of you with over others) (4:32) the verse: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, the male has the share of two females and the testimony of two women equals a man; are we in deeds likewise - if a woman does a good deed she has half a good deed? So Allah revealed this verse: (And do not wish for what Allah favored some of you with over others): for it is justice from Me, and I made it."
"3579","Another (no. 116): Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Muaddib informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Amir narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Yaqub narrated to us from Jafar from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The people of Jahiliyyah circumambulated the House naked; so Allah revealed: (And their prayer at the House was but whistling and clapping) (8:35). He said: Al-muka is whistling, and al-tasdiyah is clapping; and He revealed about them: (Say: Who forbade the adornment of Allah) (7:32)."
"3580","Another (no. 117): And with it, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me from his father from Ashath from Jafar from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, this sky? He said: This is a withheld wave above you."
"3581","Another (no. 118): And with it, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu Said al-Dashtaki narrated to us: my father narrated to me from his father from Ashath ibn Ishaq from Jafar from Said ibn Jubayr who said: Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepting Islam; when they returned to their lands, if they found a year of rain, fertility and good birth they said: Our religion is righteous, so hold to it; and if they found it a year of drought, bad birth and famine they said: Is there in this religion of ours any good? So Allah revealed to His Prophet: (And of people is he who worships Allah on an edge) (22:11) the verse. Al-Bukhari narrated from the narration of Abi Husayn from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: (And of people is he who worships Allah on an edge): he said: A man came to Madinah; if his wife bore a boy and his horses foaled he said: This is a righteous religion; and if his wife did not bear and his horses did not foal he said: This is an evil religion. In what we cited is an addition in exegesis."
"3582","Another (no. 119): And with it, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us - as I deem -: Abu Said al-Dashtaki narrated to us: my father Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Sad narrated to us: my father narrated to me from his father from Ashath ibn Ishaq from Jafar from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The idolaters said: If Muhammad claims to be a prophet, why does his Lord not punish him? Why is the Quran not sent upon him at once! One or two verses and a surah are sent upon him! So Allah revealed to His Prophet the answer to what they said: (And those who disbelieve said: Why was the Quran not sent upon him at once?) (25:32) to: (and more astray in way)."
"3583","Another (no. 120): And with it, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: They worshipped al-Uzza in their hands, a white stone; when they found better than it they cast that and worshipped what was better; so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: (Have you seen he who took his desire as his god?) (45:23)."
"3584","Another (no. 121): Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Razi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Sad al-Dashtaki narrated to us: my father narrated to us from his father from Ashath ibn Ishaq from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israil said: O Musa, does your Lord pray? He said: Fear Allah. So his Lord called him: O Musa, they asked, does your Lord pray? So say: Yes, I pray, and My angels, upon My prophets and messengers. So Allah revealed to His Prophet: (Allah and His angels pray upon the Prophet) (33:56) to the end of the verse."
"3585","Another (no. 122): And with it, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Harawi narrated to us: Abu Yusuf Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Mutarrif narrated to us from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (Allah takes the souls at death, and those not dead in their sleep) (39:42): he said: The souls of the living and dead meet in sleep, know one another and ask; then the souls of the living are returned to their bodies, none mistaken; that is His saying, mighty and majestic: (Indeed in that are signs for a people who reflect)."
"3586","No. 123: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Yahya - he is Ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi - narrated to us: Amr ibn Khalid - he is al-Harrani - narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us from Mutarrif ibn Tarif from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas: (Allah takes the souls at death): he said: The souls of the living and dead meet in sleep and ask among themselves; so Allah holds the souls of the dead and sends the souls of the living to their bodies. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Mutarrif except Musa. I say: Had al-Tabarani, may Allah have mercy on him, come upon the narration of Abu Yusuf from Mutarrif cited above, he would not have said what he said, Allah knows best."
"3587","Another (no. 124): Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Jarbadhqani informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them while present: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us - as I deem -: Abu Said Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad al-Muqri narrated to us: my father narrated to us: my father narrated to me from his father, he said: Ashath ibn Ishaq informed us from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: (O tranquil soul) (89:27), i.e. the believing: (Return to your Lord, pleased) (89:28), he says: to your body, (pleased, pleasing; so enter among My servants; and enter My Paradise) (89:28-30). He said: It was revealed while Abu Bakr sat; so he said: O Messenger of Allah, how fine is this! He said: It shall indeed be said to you."
"3588","Another (nos. 125-126): And with it, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Marduwayh informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amir ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: my father narrated to us (hawala). Ibn Marduwayh said: And Abdullah narrated to us: Usayd ibn Asim narrated to us: Amir ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, they said: Khattab ibn Jafar - he is Ibn Abi al-Mughirah - narrated to us from his father from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas regarding Allah's saying, mighty and majestic: (For the accustomed security of Quraysh) (106:1): he said: My favor upon Quraysh, the understanding: (their journey of winter and summer) (106:2): he said: They wintered in Makkah and summered in Taif; (So let them worship the Lord of this House) (106:3): he said: The Kabah; (Who fed them against hunger and secured them against fear) (106:4): he said: Against leprosy (judham)."
"3589","Another (no. 127): Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi and Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us in Baghdad that Abu Mansur Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them: al-Sharif Abu al-Ghanaim Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mamun informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi al-Sukkari informed us: Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Razi narrated to us from Yaqub al-Qummi from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Convey salaam to Umar, and tell him his pleasure is might and his anger is judgment. Ismail ibn Aban: I do not deem him al-Ghanawi, and I think him al-Warraq... Allah knows best."
"3590","Another (no. 128): Abu al-Muzaffar Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad al-Samani informed us in Marw that Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Furawi informed them: Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Mahmi informed us: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan al-Isfarayini informed us: Abu Awanah Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: Usayd ibn Asim al-Isbahani narrated to us: Amir ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us from Jafar - he is Ibn Abi al-Mughirah - from Ibn Abbas who said: A cloud shaded us while we hoped for it; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: The angel who drives it told me he drives it to a valley in Yemen called Dar al-Sama; then people came to us and told us they were rained upon that day. Here speech is effaced."
"3591","No. 129: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us: Ibrahim ibn Amir narrated to us: my father narrated to us from Yaqub from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while a cloud shaded us and we hoped for it; so he said: The angel who drives the clouds came to me just now and greeted me, and mentioned he drives it to a valley in Yemen called Dar al-Sama; then a rider came after that and we asked him about the cloud; so he said: They were rained upon that day. End of the juz; praise be to Allah alone; and may Allah bless our master Muhammad and his family with much salutation."
"3592","The sixtieth juz of al-Ahadith al-Mukhtarah. In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate. Praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant salutation. Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Said ibn Jubayr. No. 130: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say between the two prostrations: My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me health, and provide for me."
"3593","No. 131: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Bazzaz informed them, he said: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Fath known as al-Ushari informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi ibn Masud al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz informed us: al-Qadi Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Buhlul narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Kamil ibn al-Ala narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say between the two prostrations: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me health, provide for me, and mend me. Al-Daraqutni said: Kamil ibn al-Ala is alone in it from Habib ibn Abi Thabit."
"3594","No. 132: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Kamil ibn al-Ala narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Ibn Abbas, or from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said between the two prostrations in the night prayer: My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, raise me, provide for me, guide me. Then he prostrated. And in his narration: Forgive me, have mercy on me, mend me, guide me, provide for me. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Masud al-Ajami from Zayd ibn al-Hubab as the narration of Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, and with him: Forgive me, have mercy on me, have mercy on me, mend me, provide for me, raise me. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Salamah ibn Shabib, and from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal from Yazid ibn Harun from Zayd ibn al-Hubab, saying: A gharib hadith; and some narrated this hadith from Kamil Abi al-Ala mursal. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abi Kurayb from Ismail ibn Subayh from Kamil. Kamil ibn al-Ala Abu al-Ala al-Fuqaymi: Ibn Abi Hatim cited him without citing any wound; and he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Khaythamah informed us, in what he wrote to me, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Main say: Kamil Abu al-Ala is thiqah (trustworthy); while Abu Hatim al-Busti criticized him; and Yahya ibn Main knows better than Abu Hatim al-Busti, Allah knows best."
"3595","Another (nos. 133-134): Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Habib from Said ibn Jubayr (hawala). And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu al-Raja Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Qari informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Hulali informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Talhah ibn Muhammad informed us: Abu Usayd Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Usayd informed us: Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Bazzaz al-Isbahani narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Habib from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No man who believes in Allah and His Messenger hates the Ansar, but Allah and His Messenger hate him. In Imam Ahmad's narration: and His Messenger, or: but Allah and His Messenger hate him."
"3596","No. 135: My maternal uncle the imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Ahmad ibn al-Muqarrib al-Karkhi informed them: Tirad ibn Muhammad al-Zaynabi informed us: Ali ibn Abdullah al-Isawi informed us: Ammar ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Mukram al-Bazzaz narrated to us: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Ansar but Allah and His Messenger hate him."
"3597","No. 136: Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Sayyid Abu al-Izz al-Hasan ibn al-Hadi ibn al-Hasan al-Alawi and Abu al-Qasim Ismail ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr al-Naysaburi informed them, they said: al-Adib Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mihrabzadh al-Nahwi narrated to us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri narrated to us: Mamun ibn Harun al-Tusi narrated to us: al-Husayn - he is Ibn Isa ibn Humran al-Bistami - narrated to us: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us from Sufyan al-Thawri from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Ansar - or he said - but Allah hates him. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan from Bishr ibn al-Sari and al-Muammal from Sufyan similarly, saying: A hasan sahih hadith. And al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Adam ibn Sulayman from Abi Kurayb from Abu Muawiyah from al-Amash from Adi ibn Thabit from Said similarly."
"3598","Another (no. 137): Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me: Aththam ibn Ali al-Amiri narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs of the night then left and used the siwak."
"3599","Nos. 138-139: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Isbahani informed us there that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us (hawala). Al-Tabarani said: And Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, they said: Aththam ibn Ali narrated to us from al-Amash from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs of the night, then left and used the siwak. Page 222 of the manuscript is missing; hence I apologize for not writing the hadiths on that page."
"3600","Another (no. 140): Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: Allah took the covenant of the prophets upon their peoples."
